[2026-04-27 10:28:12] Raw text/plain payload: b"Explore new working papers published by the Center for Economic Studies in the fourth quarter of 2025.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/library/working-papers/series/ces-wp.html?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNew Economic and Social Science Research Published in the CES Working Paper Series\r\n\r\nMagnifying Glass - Research [ https://www.census.gov/library/working-papers/series/ces-wp.html?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nNine working papers were published by the\xc2\xa0Center for Economic Studies (CES)\xc2\xa0in the fourth quarter of 2025.\xc2\xa0The\xc2\xa0CES Working Paper Series\xc2\xa0features research in economics and other social sciences, by U.S. Census Bureau and\xc2\xa0Federal Statistical Research Data Centers researchers, using restricted-use Census Bureau microdata. A small sample of this recently published research [ https://www.census.gov/library/working-papers/series/ces-wp.html?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] can be found below.\r\n\r\n\r\n  * _Parental Death, Inheritance, and Labor Supply in the United States [ https://www.census.gov/library/working-papers/2025/adrm/CES-WP-25-71.html?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]_\r\nElif Tasar and John Voorheis \r\n  * _Measurement Matters: Financial Reporting and Productivity [ https://www.census.gov/library/working-papers/2025/adrm/CES-WP-25-72.html?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]_\r\nJohn M. Barrios, Brian C. Fujiy, Petro Lisowsky, and Michael Minnis \r\n  * _Gifted Identification Across the Distribution of Family Income [ https://www.census.gov/library/working-papers/2025/adrm/CES-WP-25-73.html?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]_\r\nNicholas J. Ainsworth, Aaron J. Ainsworth, Christopher Cleveland, Leah R. Clark, Quentin Brummet, Emily K. Penner, Jacob Hibel, Andrew Saultz, Michelle Spiegel, Paul Hanselman, and Andrew Penner \r\n  * _School-Based Disability Identification Varies by Student Family Income [ https://www.census.gov/library/working-papers/2025/adrm/CES-WP-25-74.html?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]_\r\nNicholas J. Ainsworth, Christopher Cleveland, Leah R. Clark, Jacob Hibel, Quentin Brummet, Andrew Saultz, Emily K. Penner, Michelle Spiegel, Paul Y. Yoo, Juan Camilo Cristancho, Paul Hanselman, and Andrew Penner \r\n  * _Food Fight: U.S. Exporters'\xc2\xa0Adjustments to Russia's 2014 Agricultural Import Ban [ https://www.census.gov/library/working-papers/2025/adrm/CES-WP-25-79.html?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]_\r\nEmek Basker and Fariha Kamal \r\n\r\nOpinions and conclusions within these working papers are those of the authors and do not represent the views of the Census Bureau. \r\n\r\nExplore the complete CES working paper series at the link below.\r\n\r\n*Explore * [ https://www.census.gov/library/working-papers/series/ces-wp.html?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nStay Connected with the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nFollow us on our social media channels, Facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], LinkedIn [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Twitter/X [ https://x.com/uscensusbureau?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], and\xc2\xa0YouTube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], so you never miss an update.\r\n\r\nStay Connected With Us on Social Media [ https://www.census.gov/about/contact-us/social_media.html?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Follow Us* [ https://www.census.gov/about/contact-us/social_media.html?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nWe serve as the nation\xe2\x80\x99s leading provider of quality data about its people and economy.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau is the federal government's largest statistical agency. As the world\xe2\x80\x99s premier statistical agency, we are dedicated to making our nation a better place. Policy-makers, businesses, and the public use our data to make informed decisions.\r\n\r\nSubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/signup/34555 ] | Manage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] | Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] | Help [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/s/?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*Share This * [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/4036cfa ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260108research&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n"
