[2026-04-27 10:28:46] Raw text/plain payload: b'1st Generic: Robenacoxib for Postoperative Pain & Inflammation in Cats  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nIf your email program has trouble displaying this email, view as a webpage [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/bulletins/4039057 ].\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nUS Food and Drug Administration\r\n\r\nBookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/bulletins/4039057?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\n*FDA Approves First Generic Robenacoxib Tablet for Postoperative Pain & Inflammation in Cats*\r\n\r\nCVM Update [ https://www.fda.gov/animal-veterinary/cvm-updates/fda-approves-first-generic-robenacoxib-tablet-postoperative-pain-inflammation-cats?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nJanuary 9, 2026\r\n\r\nThe FDA recently approved the first generic robenacoxib tablets for the control of postoperative pain and inflammation associated with orthopedic surgery, ovariohysterectomy and castration in cats at least four months of age that weigh at least 5.5 pounds.\r\n\r\nRobenacoxib tablets contain the same active ingredient (robenacoxib) as the approved brand name drug product, Onsior, which was first approved in 2011. The FDA determined that Robencoxib tablets are bioequivalent to the brand name product.\r\n\r\nRobenacoxib tablets are a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) and are only available via a prescription from a licensed veterinarian. Robenacoxib tablets can be given for up to three days.\r\n\r\nRobenacoxib tablets are sponsored by ZyVet Animal Health, Inc., based in Pennington, New Jersey.\r\n\r\n*For more information:*\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Freedom of Information Summary \xe2\x80\x93 Robenacoxib tablets (ANADA 200-832) [ https://animaldrugsatfda.fda.gov/adafda/app/search/public/document/downloadFoi/17827?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0 \r\n  * Veterinary Nonsteroidal Anti-Inflammatory Drugs (NSAIDs) [ https://www.fda.gov/animal-veterinary/product-safety-information/veterinary-nonsteroidal-anti-inflammatory-drugs-nsaids?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * What Veterinarians Should Advise Clients About Pain Control and Nonsteroidal Anti-Inflammatory Drugs (NSAIDs) in Dogs and Cats [ https://www.fda.gov/animal-veterinary/resources-you/what-veterinarians-should-advise-clients-about-pain-control-and-nonsteroidal-anti-inflammatory-drugs?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nfeed [ https://www.fda.gov/about-fda/contact-fda/subscribe-podcasts-and-news-feeds?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://www.twitter.com/US_FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/USFoodandDrugAdmin?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]flickr [ https://www.flickr.com/photos/fdaphotos/albums/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\n*Manage Subscriptions* [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 *Unsubscribe All* [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.ee0243ee8741fe358146537aecf40e1e&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 *Help* [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} td {line-height:1;} \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: U.S. Food and Drug Administration \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\r\n10903 New Hampshire Ave\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0Silver Spring, MD \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0 20993-0002\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa01-888-INFO-FDA GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
