[2026-04-27 10:29:12] Raw text/plain payload: b'rad \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nSPOTLIGHT\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nWHAT\'S NEW IN THIS ISSUE?\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*World Cup Academy Spring Break Camp [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30214&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\r\n\r\nPrepare your players for travel soccer tryouts or just have a great time improving their skills! Campers will receive individualized attention in small, skill-appropriate groups from former collegiate and semi-professional players.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nDates: March 30- April 3\r\nTime: 9:00 AM- 12:00 PM\r\nAges 6-14\r\nFee: $275\r\nRadnor Memorial Park, 60 Matsonford Rd, Wayne\r\n\r\n  World Cup Sports Academy \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\nLight up Wayne recap\r\n\r\nThank you to all our partner organizations for making our December 30th, 2025, inaugural *Light Up Wayne Hanukkah Festival* a success! Our community gathered at the Wayne train station for live music, storytelling, delicious food, pop Up Hanukkah shops, children\'s arts and crafts activities, and more!\r\n\r\nThank you to Cantor Tifani Coyot of Temple Brich Achim, The Jewish Federaton of Greater Philadelphia, The Kibitz Room and all our generous sponsors of our first-ever Light Up Wayne Hanukkah event!\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nCOMMUNITY EVENTS\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*Sponsorship Opportunities*\r\n\r\nThe Parks & Recreation Department strives to provide a range of activities that appeal to all ages and segments within our great community.\xc2\xa0\r\nSponsorships are available to local, regional, and national businesses and organizations.\r\n\r\n*2026 Sponsorships are now available!*\r\n\r\nEnhance your recognition, public image, and good will in Radnor Township.\r\n\xc2\xa0Provide great quality of life opportunities for members of the community.\r\n\xc2\xa0Increase awareness of your products and services and overall marketing strategy.\r\n\xc2\xa0Make connections and interact with people while you reach various markets.\r\n\xc2\xa0Promote your business or organization to numerous people.\r\n\xc2\xa0Assist the Parks & Recreation Department in meeting its mission.\r\n\r\n*2026 Sponsorship Brochure coming soon!* [ https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/PARADNOR/2025/01/31/file_attachments/3149621/Sponsorships%20Opportunities%20Brochure%20Events%202025.pdf ] \r\n \r\n\r\n*2026 Community Events* [ https://www.radnor.com/government/departments/parks-recreation/draft-community-events?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nThank you Harmelin Media! [ https://harmelin.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nThank you for your generous support of our Radnor Sweetheart Dance 2026!\r\n\r\nHarmelin Media [ https://harmelin.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://harmelin.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*Calling Local Community Organizations, Institutions, and Groups*\r\n\r\nWe would like to ask for your consideration in participating at our many community events this year. Our community events offer an opportunity to interact with members of the community by providing information about your organization and services, providing fun giveaways, conducting interactive games, and even having fundraisers that will help your organization.\r\n\r\nThere is no fee to attend any of the great events taking place.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nPlease email Tammy Cohen at tcohen@radnor.org with your interest.\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30269&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nSPRING/ SUMMER CAMPS\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*World Cup Sports Academy Spring Break Soccer Camp 2026* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30214&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nMarch 30- April 3, 9:00-12:00 PM\r\nAges 6-14\r\nRadnor Memorial Park\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Junior Pickleball Summer Camps with Universal Rackets* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30222&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nMonday-Thursday, 9:00-12 PM\r\nSession 1: June 29th-July 2nd\r\nSession 2: July 13th-July 16th\r\nSession 3: August 3rd-August 6th\r\nSession 4: August 17th-August 20th\r\n\r\n*Survivor Nature and Hiking Camp 2026* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30295&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nMonday- Friday, 9:00- 2:00 PM\r\nWeek 1: June 15- June 19\r\nWeek 2: June 22- June 26\r\nWeek 3: June 29- July 3\r\nWeek 4: July 6- July 10\r\nWeek 5: July 13- July 17\r\nWeek 6: July 20- July 24\r\nWeek 7: July- July 31\r\nWeek 8: Aug 3- Aug 7\r\nWeek 9: Aug 10- Aug 14\r\n\r\n*Junior Tennis Summer Camp with Universal Rackets* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30223&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nMonday- Thursday, 9:00-12:00 PM\r\nSession 1: July 6th- July 9th\r\nSession 2: July 27th- July 30th\r\nSession 3: August 10th- August 13th\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n  World Cup Sports Academy [ https://www.wcupsa.com/programs/spring-break-soccer.php?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nYOUTH PROGRAMS\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHiking Hound Logo [ https://www.radnorpickleball.com/intro1722450465413?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Little Tykes Go on Hikes with Hiking Hound [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30188&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n*Multiple hikes throughout the year.\xc2\xa0\r\n*Upcoming:\xc2\xa0\r\n**"Storybook Hike: 3/21, 12-1 PM\r\n"**"Bingo Hike: 4/18, 12-1 PM\r\n"*Skunk Hollow Park and Trails, 490 Darby Paoli Road, Villanova\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Treats on The Trail with Hiking Hound* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30275&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nJanuary 24 & February 28 @ 1PM\r\nSkunk Hollow Park and Trails, 490 Darby Paoli Road, \r\nVillanova\r\n\r\n*World Cup Sports Academy Junior Soccer Winter 2026 [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30215&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n*Wednesdays\r\n**January 14- February 25\r\nAges 3-5: 1:30-2:30 PM\r\nSulpizio Gym, 125 S. Wayne Avenue*\r\n*\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Radnor Champions Fitletics with Skyhawks* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30291&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n*Sundays\r\n*January 11- February 8 (No class 1/18)\r\nFebruary 22- March 22 (No class 3/1)\r\nK-5th: 11-11:45 AM\r\n6th-12th: 12-12:45 PM\r\nIthan Elementary School\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Multisport Tots with Skyhawks [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30234&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n**Sundays Multisport Tots:***\r\n**January 11- February 8 (No class 1/18)\r\nFebruary 22- March 22 (No class 3/1)\r\nAges 2-3: 9:15- 9:55 AM\r\nAges 3-4: 10:05- 10:45 AM\r\nIthan Elementary School\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Ready Set Rackets! [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30272&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\r\n*Tuesday Indoor Clinics:*\r\nPickleball & Tennis Together (For Parents and Kids Ages 1.5-5)\r\nWinter 2: February 10th-March 10th\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Mini Hoopers with PA Hoops Academy [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30265&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nSundays\r\n* January 11- March 8 (no session 1/18)\r\nAges 5, 9:00-9:50 am\r\nAges 4 & 6 10:00-10:50 am\r\nSulpizio Gym, 125 S. Wayne Avenue\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Winter Indoor Tennis with Pamela Rende* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30290&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n*Sundays, January 25- March 22\r\n*Multiple sessions for beginners to intermediate from 3-8 PM\r\nRadnor Racquet Club, 175 King of Prussia Road\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn more about these programs!* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/default.aspx?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nADULT & SENIOR PROGRAMS\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nad [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30271&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Men\'s Winter Pick Up Basketball [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30286&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n*Mondays, December 1- March 9*\r\n*8:00 PM- 10:00 PM\r\nAges: 18+\r\nRadnor Activity Center\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Indoor Open-Play Pickleball- Winter & Spring 2026 [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30292&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n*Mondays, Tuesdays, Thursdays, Saturdays\r\nJanuary 5- April 2\r\nAges: 18+\r\nRadnor Activity Center\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Radnor Steps  [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30075&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n*Every Friday on the Radnor Trail\r\nAll ages\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Winter Indoor Tennis with Pamela Rende [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30290&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\r\nSundays, Sundays, January 25- March 22*\r\n*Session for Adult and Teens from 7-8:00 PM\r\nRadnor Racquet Club, 175 King of Prussia Road\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Pickleball Clinics with Universal Rackets [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30256&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\r\n*Indoor Winter 1*: January 16th- February 13th\r\n*Indoor Winter 2:* February 20th- March 20th\r\nRadnor Activity Center\r\nAges 18+\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn more about these programs!* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/default.aspx?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHealth & Wellness\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHello Winter\r\n\r\nThis section includes winter wellness tips.\r\n\r\n*Boost Your Immunity and Nutrition This Winter*\r\n\r\nWinter brings cozy vibes\xe2\x80\x94but also a higher risk of colds, flu, and low energy. Supporting your immune system through smart nutrition and daily habits can help you stay healthy and energized all season long.\r\n\r\n*1. Eat Immune-Boosting Foods*\r\nFocus on a balanced diet rich in whole foods. Seasonal fruits and vegetables like oranges, kiwis, carrots, spinach, and sweet potatoes are packed with vitamins A and C, which support immune function. Include garlic, ginger, and turmeric\xe2\x80\x94they have natural anti-inflammatory and antimicrobial properties.\r\n\r\n*2. Don\xe2\x80\x99t Skip Protein and Healthy Fats*\r\nProtein helps your body repair and build immune cells. Add lentils, beans, eggs, dairy, fish, or lean meats to your meals. Healthy fats from nuts, seeds, olive oil, and fatty fish provide omega-3s, which help regulate inflammation.\r\n\r\n*3. Support Your Gut Health*\r\nA strong immune system starts in the gut. Include probiotic-rich foods like yogurt, kefir, or fermented foods, along with fiber from whole grains, fruits, and vegetables to nourish good gut bacteria.\r\n\r\nNew food pyramid 2026\r\n\r\nThe USDA released a new set of dietary guidelines [ https://realfood.gov/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] on Wednesday, January 7th, which encourages Americans to prioritize whole nutrient- dense foods, protein, vegetables, fruits, healthy fats, and whole grains, and dramatically reduce highly processed foods. Winter wellness isn\xe2\x80\x99t about one magic food\xe2\x80\x94it\xe2\x80\x99s about consistent, nourishing choices. Eat well, rest enough, stay active, and listen to your body. Small daily habits can make a big difference in keeping your immunity strong all winter long. \xe2\x9d\x84\xef\xb8\x8f??\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*NAMI Mainline PA* [ https://namimainlinepa.org/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nWhether you\xe2\x80\x99re thriving, surviving, or somewhere in between \xe2\x80\x94 your feelings are valid, and you are not alone. NAMI Mainline PA is an affiliate of the National Alliance on Mental Illness and provides information and support to people with mental illness, their families and friends. All of their services are FREE of Charge. Contact Lisa Parker at lisa@namimainlinepa.org or 267-251-6240 for more information.\r\n\r\n  Nami \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n2026 Board Meetings\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nThursday, February 12\r\n\r\nThursday, March 12\r\n\r\nThursday, April 9\r\n\r\nThursday, May 14\r\n\r\nThursday, June 11\r\n\r\nThursday, July 9\r\n\r\nThursday, September 10\r\n\r\nThursday, October 8\r\n\r\nThursday, November 12\r\n\r\nThursday, December 10\r\n\r\n6:30 PM | Radnor Township Building\r\n\r\n*Parks & Recreation Board Website* [ https://www.radnor.com/government/boards-and-commissions/parks-recreation-board?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Current Parks & Trails Projects* [ https://www.radnor.com/government/departments/parks-recreation/park-trails-projects?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n*_Fenimore Woods Park Improvements Project \xe2\x80\x93 Stable Renovation are underway._*\r\n\r\nThe\xc2\xa0Fenimore Woods Improvement Project continues to advance steadily and is well underway. In addition to the fencing improvements taking place around the park, the stable will be renovated into park restrooms and storage - as part of the overall improvement project. Following on the heels of the stable renovation beginning, the park pavilion replacement will also start in mid-fall.\xc2\xa0 Please contact Tammy Cohen, Director of Parks & Recreation, at tcohen@radnor.org\xc2\xa0or 610-688-5600.\r\n\r\n*_Important Notice to Park Users_**: *The main parking lot will be closed. **We kindly ask that all park visitors observe and adhere to posted signage, fencing, and established area closures as various phases of the project continue to unfold.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n  Fenimore Stable \r\n\r\nAny questions or concerns regarding park projects, please contact Tammy Cohen, Director of Parks & Recreation, at tcohen@radnor.org.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nRECURRING NEWS\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*"The following section includes recurring, ongoing information.\xc2\xa0"*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nemployment [ https://content.govdelivery.com/landing_pages/54152/a1d1f7f5e35134e15d44cd5a504fb3d6 ]\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nparks [ https://content.govdelivery.com/landing_pages/54154/c4b9ae6bf3cab426371459f1bcc8be2b ]\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\ndogs [ https://content.govdelivery.com/landing_pages/54131/baa90887fe82ebd5554a3455b2034fc3 ]\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nEnvironmental Awareness [ https://content.govdelivery.com/landing_pages/54148/2d570d84e32eb40f3f7ec1f629f5fe79 ]\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nCOMMUNITY INFO\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*Wayne Senior Center*\r\n\r\nThe mission of the Wayne Senior Center is to provide community, friendship, and resources which enrich the lives of older adults.\r\n\r\nWould you like to be added to the WSC Connect Newsletter to get a weekly update on programming offered?\r\n\r\nEmail: info@wayneseniorcenter.org\r\n\r\n  wayne senior center \r\n\r\n*WSC Website* [ https://wayneseniorcenter.org/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Wayne Cares* is committed to providing and maintaining a network of people providing food and other material support to people in need.\r\n\r\nFood donations are accepted Monday-Friday 8am- 4pm at 210 S. Wayne Ave. Monetary donations and a link to their Amazon wish list can be found here:\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nFood Pantry Wish List [ https://www.amazon.com/hz/wishlist/ls/13NRW6MSJNT0/ref=hz_ls_biz_ex?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n  Wayne Cares Logo \r\n\r\n*Wayne Cares Website* [ https://waynecares.org/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nmansion \r\n\r\n*The Willows Park Preserve*\r\n\r\nRadnor Township operates and maintains the Willows Park, a 47.5 - acre estate purchased in 1973. This irresistible combination of quiet elegance within the unsurpassed beauty of the landscaped grounds includes a picturesque pond with flowing fountains, sweeping panoramas of stately trees, and flowering plants. The grounds are great for a hike, lunch in the picnic area, or just to sit on a bench and take in the scenery.\r\n\r\n"*Reserve the Willows Picnic Grove for your next event! Reservation requests can be made at www.radnorrecreation.com!*"\r\n\r\nThe Willows Park Preserve (WPP) has been established with a vision and passion for preserving the Willows Park Mansion The WPP is a nonprofit organization whose mission is to physically restore the Mansion and to make it available for community use. In 2019, the WPP signed a 25-year lease with Radnor Township to restore, maintain and operate the Willows Mansion, bringing the Mansion to life for all to enjoy!\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More about the Willows Park Preserve* [ https://willowsparkpreserve.org/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Radnor Township Civic Association*\r\n\r\nLocated at 248 highland Ave in Wayne\r\n\r\nThe RTCA has a main hall with a seating capacity of approximately 150 people. For more information on rentals and reservations, please contact:\r\n\r\nHoward Childs; 267-562-9793\r\nPamela Deans; 484-431-3044\r\nCharles Marshall; 610-420-1538\r\n\r\n  RTCA building \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Skunk Hollow Community Garden - Openings for New Members!*\r\n\r\ngarden \r\n\r\nAre you a Radnor Township resident interested in learning how to grow your own food?\xc2\xa0 Want to join a group of enthusiastic neighbors who enjoy working together to accomplish group goals.\xc2\xa0 Are you looking for a way to spend more time enjoying the outdoors, perhaps doing some good old fashioned manual labor in the dirt?\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nIf any of this sound like you, then come join the Skunk Hollow Community Garden. We have space available for new members to our community garden.\xc2\xa0 No experience needed. We\xe2\x80\x99ll provide the tools, gloves, guidance, and weeds J and you bring the energy and commitment.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nContact skunkhollowgarden@gmail.com for more information. If you want to see the space, we are located just south of the Willows Mansion in adjacent to the township leaf composting site. Park at either the upper lot or the picnic area at The Willows Park and walk south of the mansion to the garden.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://skunkhollowgarden.org/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nsports \r\n\r\n*Community Sport Organizations*\r\n\r\nRadnor Township offers a variety of sport and civic organizations for our youth and adult community members to join.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://radnor.prod.govaccess.org/government/departments/parks-recreation/community-organizations?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nManage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/PARADNOR/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe All [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/PARADNOR/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.8df60fc98d8610bdd9ee8a9e391652de&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using govDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: Township of Radnor, PA \xc2\xb7 301 Iven Avenue \xc2\xb7 Wayne, PA 19087-5297 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;}\r\n'
