&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026\r\n\r\nhttps://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/gmail/gmail-is-entering-the-gemini-era/?utm_source=kw-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026&utm_content=image\r\nNew year, new Gmail\r\n\r\nGmail is becoming a personal, proactive inbox assistant to help you  \r\nnavigate your busy life. New AI Overviews\r\nwill summarize long conversations and answer questions, while Suggested  \r\nReplies and Proofread will help you\r\ndraft and polish emails in seconds. These updates are rolling out now in  \r\nthe U.S. and to more regions in the\r\ncoming months. Plus, to clear the clutter, we're launching AI Inbox  \r\ninitially to a set of trusted testers,\r\nwhich can highlight your urgent to-dos and VIP messages in a personalized  \r\nbriefing.\r\n\r\nSee what's new in your inbox\r\nhttps://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/gmail/gmail-is-entering-the-gemini-era/?utm_source=kw-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026&utm_content=cta\r\n\r\nPopular on the Keyword\r\n\r\nGOOGLE TV\r\n\r\nGoogle introduces new Gemini for Google TV features\r\n\r\nRead more\r\nhttps://blog.google/products-and-platforms/platforms/google-tv/ces-2026/?utm_source=kw-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026&utm_content=cta\r\n\r\nXR and AR\r\n\r\nAndroid XR lights up Sphere in Las Vegas for CES\r\n\r\nRead more\r\nhttps://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/xr-ar/android-xr-sphere-ces-2026/?utm_source=kw-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026&utm_content=cta\r\n\r\nAI\r\n\r\nGoogle's year in review: 8 areas with research breakthroughs in 2025\r\n\r\nRead more\r\nhttps://blog.google/technology/ai/2025-research-breakthroughs/?utm_source=kw-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026&utm_content=cta\r\n\r\nAI\r\n\r\n60 of our biggest AI announcements in 2025\r\n\r\nRead more\r\nhttps://blog.google/technology/ai/google-ai-news-recap-2025/?utm_source=kw-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026&utm_content=cta\r\n\r\nAI\r\n\r\n40 of our most helpful AI tips from 2025\r\n\r\nRead more\r\nhttps://blog.google/technology/ai/ai-tips-2025/?utm_source=kw-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026&utm_content=cta\r\n\r\nAI\r\n\r\nThe latest AI news we announced in December\r\n\r\nRead more\r\nhttps://blog.google/technology/ai/google-ai-updates-december-2025/?utm_source=kw-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026&utm_content=cta\r\n\r\nBeyond the news\r\n\r\nTo say Nano Banana has _mass a-peel_ is an understatement, with our image  \r\ngeneration and editing model\r\ndebuting in August as the top-rated image editing model in the world. As we  \r\nslip into 2026, the time's ripe to\r\nlook back at some of the most fun ways people used Nano Banana in 2025,  \r\nfrom transforming pets into realistic\r\n3D figurines to testing new hairstyles and generating complex infographics  \r\nquickly. Here are some of our\r\nfavorite Nano Banana trends of the year.\r\n\r\nTry the best of the bunch\r\nhttps://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/gemini/nano-banana-google-trends-2025/?utm_source=kw-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026&utm_content=cta\r\nhttps://blog.google/?utm_source=kw-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026\r\nThis email was sent to <jasonnorman66994@gmail.com> because you've signed  \r\nup to receive news and updates from Google.\r\n\r\n(c) <2026> Google LLC. All Rights Reserved. Google and the Google logo are  \r\ntrademarks of\r\nGoogle LLC. 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043.\r\n\r\nMore news from Google\r\nhttps://blog.google/?utm_source=kw-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026&utm_content=footer-kwlink\r\n|About Google  \r\nhttps://about.google/?utm_source=kw-newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=01092026\r\n|Unsubscribe  \r\n<https://myaccount.google.com/communication-preferences/unsubscribe/gt/ANnMTcbuY1q6bi6o3Tw63P8LrHW2ikdNSefOunOV0a_KJJMuGkX8yR9Cj2izm56trUu9CIN6dwSqbfej