[2026-04-27 10:29:17] Raw text/plain payload: b'$1M AI Challenge Open to New Jersey Teams  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nView as a webpage / Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJGOV/bulletins/403a361 ]\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nJanuary 9, 2026\r\n\r\n State of New Jersey [ https://nj.gov/ ]  \r\nNJ Updates: Events, Deadlines, Programs, Guidance, and More\r\n\r\nWant to know about current topics in New Jersey? The State of New Jersey Update features information, news, resources, guidance, and more. Additional featured news is also available at\xc2\xa0*NJ.gov [ https://nj.gov/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term= ].*\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Child Care Assistance Program Opens New Registrations [ https://www.childcarenj.gov/CCAPClosed?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ]*\r\n\r\nchildcare icon [ https://www.childcarenj.gov/CCAPClosed?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ] \r\n\r\nThe Registration Form for the New Jersey\'s Child Care Assistance Program (CCAP) is now available. The program helps income-eligible working families, students, and job trainees pay for child care costs for children up to age 13 or age 19 for children with special needs.\r\n\r\nPriority will be given to families with children experiencing homelessness, children with special needs, and households with very low incomes. Due to limited funding, not all families who qualify will receive assistance.\r\n\r\nFamilies must complete a registration form first. If selected, they will be invited to submit a full application. More information and the Registration Form are available at *ChildCareNJ.gov [ https://www.childcarenj.gov/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ].*\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Register Now [ https://www.childcarenj.gov/CCAPClosed?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ]*\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*New Jersey Awarding $3.34M for AI Innovation and Problem-Solving [ https://www.plugandplaytechcenter.com/innovation-services/challenge-offerings/ai-innovation-challenge?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ]*\r\n\r\nComputer screen with dollar sign [ https://www.plugandplaytechcenter.com/innovation-services/challenge-offerings/ai-innovation-challenge?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ] \r\n\r\nNew Jersey is investing $3.34 million in artificial intelligence solutions that address real challenges facing the State. The AI Innovation Challenge awards grants and resources through competitive program where companies and academic teams leverage AI and State datasets to build innovative tools meant to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of State government.\r\n\r\nTeams of at least three members must be based in New Jersey, with at least 50 percent of members as State residents. Early-stage companies with fewer than 225 employees may also apply. New publicly-available datasets have been added to the *NJOIT Open Data Center [ https://data.nj.gov/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=event ]* to help applicants.\r\n\r\nWinners receive up to $1 million for product development, with additional funding available based on progress demonstrated by March. Applications are open through January 19.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More [ https://www.plugandplaytechcenter.com/innovation-services/challenge-offerings/ai-innovation-challenge?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ]*\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*New Jersey State Parks Are Hiring 800+ Seasonal Workers [ https://nj.gov/dep/workinparks?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ]*\r\n\r\nPark [ https://nj.gov/dep/workinparks?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ] \r\n\r\nNew Jersey State Parks are accepting applications for more than 800 seasonal positions running from Memorial Day through Labor Day. Available roles include lifeguards, maintenance personnel, visitor service assistants, naturalists, history educators, and office staff.\r\n\r\nMost positions start at $16.50 per hour. Lifeguards earn $19-20 per hour depending on location. No prior experience is required for most positions. Lifeguards receive paid training and certification. Weekend and holiday availability is required. Positions are available Statewide from High Point State Park to Cape May Point State Park.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Apply Now [ https://nj.gov/dep/workinparks?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ]*\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Caring for an Aging Parent or Family Member? PACE Can Help [ https://www.nj.gov/humanservices/doas/services/l-p/pace/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=pubhealth ]*\r\n\r\nHealthcare [ https://www.nj.gov/humanservices/doas/services/l-p/pace/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=pubhealth ] \r\n\r\nIf you\'re caring for someone 55 or older who needs nursing home level of care, the Program of All-Inclusive Care for the Elderly (PACE) can help them stay at home. The program is now available in all 21 New Jersey counties. PACE provides coordinated medical and social services, including primary care, dental, prescriptions, home care, adult day health care, and transportation to appointments. Participants receive all Medicare and Medicaid services without the limitations those programs normally impose.\r\n\r\nSome PACE centers are accepting enrollments now, while others will open over the next 18-24 months. Contact your local PACE agency to check eligibility and availability in your area.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More [ https://www.nj.gov/humanservices/doas/services/l-p/pace/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=pubhealth ]*\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*New Jersey Residents Can Get Help With Heating Bills [ https://dcaid.dca.nj.gov/en-US/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ]*\r\n\r\nFire [ https://dcaid.dca.nj.gov/en-US/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ] \r\n\r\nThe Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program provides financial assistance for heating and cooling costs, including past-due electric and gas bills. The program also covers emergency heating system repairs and emergency fuel delivery.\r\n\r\nApplications are open now. Call *1-800-510-3102 [ tel:1-800-510-3102 ]* to determine eligibility and find your nearest application agency, or apply online through the State portal. The assistance is not a loan and does not need to be repaid.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Apply Now [ https://dcaid.dca.nj.gov/en-US/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ]*\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*New Jersey Needs You to Conserve Water This Winter [ https://dep.nj.gov/drought/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=env ]*\r\n\r\nWater conservation [ https://dep.nj.gov/drought/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=env ] \r\n\r\nNew Jersey has issued a Statewide drought warning after 15 months of below-average rain. Reservoir levels across the State are critically low, and the State is asking residents to help protect supplies.\r\n\r\nThere are no State level restrictions yet, but you can help now: run full loads in appliances, fix leaks, winterize irrigation systems, and upgrade to low-flow fixtures and showerheads.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More [ https://dep.nj.gov/drought/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=env ]*\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Cybersecurity Professionals: New Jersey Wants YOU [ https://www.cyber.nj.gov/grants-and-resources/new-jersey-civilian-cyber-resilience-corps?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=event ]*\r\n\r\nPerson working on a laptop [ https://cyber.nj.gov?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=comser ] \r\n\r\nNew Jersey has launched the Civilian Cyber Resilience Corps, a volunteer program that deploys cybersecurity professionals to help government agencies, schools, hospitals, and critical infrastructure organizations prevent and respond to cyberattacks.\r\n\r\nIf you work in cybersecurity or IT, you can volunteer to provide expertise in incident response, vulnerability assessment, and resilience training\xe2\x80\x94at no cost to your community.\r\n\r\nOrganizations needing cybersecurity support can also request assistance at no charge.\r\n\r\nLearn more and apply at *cyber.nj.gov [ https://cyber.nj.gov?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=econ ]* or call *1-833-465-2242 [ tel:1-833-465-2242 ].*\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More [ https://www.cyber.nj.gov/grants-and-resources/new-jersey-civilian-cyber-resilience-corps?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=state&utm_term=event ]*\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*New Jersey\'s Minimum Wage is Now $15.92 [ https://nj.gov/labor/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=biz&utm_term=ben ]*\r\n\r\nHouse money [ https://nj.gov/labor/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=biz&utm_term=ben ] \r\n\r\nNew Jersey\'s minimum wage is now $15.92 per hour, an increase of 43 cents. The change affects multiple worker categories with different rates. Tipped workers will earn a cash minimum of $6.05 per hour. Small business employees and agricultural workers receive phased increases. Long-term care facility workers will earn $18.92 per hour.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More [ https://nj.gov/labor/?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=20260109_nwsltr&utm_content=biz&utm_term=ben ]*\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*Was this email helpful?*\r\n\r\nyes it was helpful [ https://innovatenj.jotform.com/210624871986869?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] no it was not helpful [ https://innovatenj.jotform.com/210625672286862?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n"Some newsletter content was created with the assistance of generative AI.\xc2\xa0*Learn more [ https://innovation.nj.gov/skills/ai/ ].*"\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nStay Connected with The State of New Jersey: Facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/governorphilmurphy/ ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter [ https://twitter.com/GovMurphy ]\xc2\xa0 Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/govmurphy/ ]\xc2\xa0 SUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\nManage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJGOV/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe All [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJGOV/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.7342faa5c6504bfcaf96eabf517c12fc&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]  \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 0px;} \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: The State of New Jersey \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\r\nPO Box 001\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7 Trenton, NJ 08625 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ]\r\n'
