[2026-04-27 10:31:21] Raw text/plain payload: b'Census Bureau Upcoming and Recently Released Products  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/en.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nCensus Bureau: American Community Survey 2020-2024 5-year estimates pre-release webinar [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-estimates-webinar-embargo.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nOn Jan. 22, the U.S. Census Bureau is scheduled to hold a prerelease webinar [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/2026/2020-2024-acs-5-year-prerelease.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] about the 2020-2024 American Community Survey [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/about.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (ACS) 5-year estimates on Thursday, Jan. 22, at 1 p.m. ET. The webinar will explain how to access ACS data and give tips on comparing geographies and statistics over time.\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-estimates-webinar-embargo.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nBusiness Formation Statistics Monthly Data Release\r\n\r\nOn Jan. 14, the U.S. Census Bureau will release new Business Formation Statistics [ https://www.census.gov/econ/bfs/index.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (BFS) for December 2025. The BFS provide timely and high frequency information on new business applications and formations in the United States and Puerto Rico. The BFS are a standard data product of the Census Bureau, developed in research collaboration with economists affiliated with the Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, the Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta, the University of Maryland, and the University of Notre Dame.\r\n\r\nBTOS \r\n\r\nOn Jan. 15, the U.S. Census Bureau will release The Business Trends and Outlook Survey (BTOS) [ https://www.census.gov/hfp/btos/data?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]. BTOS measures business conditions on an ongoing basis. BTOS experimental data products are representative of all employer businesses other than farms in the U.S. economy. The data allow greater insight into the state of the economy by providing continuous, timely information for key economic measures. Data are released biweekly and are available by sector, state, employment size and the 25 most populous metropolitan statistical areas.\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*?? In Case You Missed It*\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nJarmin blog: Revolutionizing Economic Measurement at the Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/blogs/deputy-director/2026/01/revolutionizing-economic-measurement.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n"Written by Census Bureau Deputy Director Dr. Ron S. Jarmin"\r\n\r\nI recently had the privilege of speaking at conferences honoring two economists who\xe2\x80\x99ve made huge contributions to the profession and, most importantly for this blog, to the U.S. Census Bureau. Mark Roberts of Penn State University and John Haltiwanger of the University of Maryland and their colleagues used Census Bureau data to change how economists and policymakers view the economy and how the Census Bureau measures it. Beyond their scientific contributions, both Mark and John have served the Census Bureau in variety of roles.\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/blogs/deputy-director/2026/01/revolutionizing-economic-measurement.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThe U.S. Census Bureau announced additional revisions to its release calendar for the 2025/2026 economic indicators that were delayed due to the recent lapse in federal funding.\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/economic-indicators/calendar-listview.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_content=&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nPublic Information Office\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nUpcoming Events and News Releases:\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*_Tuesday, Jan. 13_*\r\n\r\n********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *******************Random Samplings Blog:* Annual Updates to the Data and Methodology used to Produce Population Estimates (tentative)\r\n\r\n********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *******************Economic Indicator:* (10 a.m.) New Residential Sales [ http://www.census.gov/construction/nrs/?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x93 September/October 2025\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*_Wednesday, Jan. 14_*\r\n\r\n*********************\xe2\x80\xa2 ********************Tip Sheet: *Business Formation Statistics\r\n\r\n*********************\xe2\x80\xa2 ********************Data Release:* (10 a.m.) Business Formation Statistics [ https://census.gov/econ/bfs/index.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x93 December 2025\r\n\r\n*********************\xe2\x80\xa2 ********************Economic Indicator:* (8:30 a.m.) Advance Monthly Sales for Retail and Food Services [ http://www.census.gov/retail/index.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x93 November 2025\r\n\r\n*********************\xe2\x80\xa2 ********************Economic Indicator:* (10 a.m.) Manufacturing and Trade: Inventories and Sales [ http://www.census.gov/mtis/?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x93 October 2025__\r\n\r\n*_Thursday, Jan. 15_*\r\n\r\n********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *******************Media Advisory: *2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-year Estimates Webinar and Embargo (resend from Jan. 8)\r\n\r\n********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *******************Tip Sheet: *Business Trends and Outlook Survey Data Release\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Newsroom* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nNews media: 301-763-3030 or 877-861-2010 or\xc2\xa0pio@census.gov\r\n\r\nNon-media: 1-800-923-8282 or\xc2\xa0ask.census.gov [ https://ask.census.gov/?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nSubscribe now [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/new? ]\xc2\xa0to receive Census Bureau releases and information via e-mail or SMS.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nWe serve as the nation\xe2\x80\x99s leading provider of quality data about its people and economy.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau is the federal government\'s largest statistical agency. As the world\xe2\x80\x99s premier statistical agency, we are dedicated to making our nation a better place. Policy-makers, businesses, and the public use our data to make informed decisions.\r\n\r\n*Resources for Media*\r\n\r\nFor media interviews, please contact the\xc2\xa0Public Information Office [ https://lnks.gd/l/eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..p-5wpj2DTx0_qgyLiv6JuMTDOF_vZlHcwFpt971jIDs/s/866068797/br/124287751808-l?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Toll Free at 877-861-2010, 301-763-3030, or\xc2\xa0pio@census.gov.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n*Stay connected with us!*\r\n\r\nJoin the conversation on social media.\r\n\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nSubscriber Settings [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Remove me from All Subscriptions  [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n&lt;!-- /* template top padding on mobile */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { table#flexible-abe-main-table { padding:0 !important; } } --&gt; ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260112mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbo