[2026-04-27 10:31:43] Raw text/plain payload: b"Here's a quick note on what's coming up as we continue the month of January.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/data/data-tools/survey-explorer/index.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n?? This Week: Discover Census Survey Explorer\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nCensus Survey Explorer [ https://www.census.gov/data/data-tools/survey-explorer/index.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nHow can you figure out which of our many surveys meet your data needs?\r\n\r\nStart with our Census Survey Explorer. This helpful data tool searches and filters our data to help you find the topics, geography, and frequency you need.\r\n\r\n?? Check it out.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Explore* [ https://www.census.gov/data/data-tools/survey-explorer/index.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n?? Economic Indicators\r\n\r\n*January 13:* New Residential Sales [ https://www.census.gov/construction/nrs/?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nSeptember 2025 (originally scheduled for October 24, 2025)\r\nOctober 2025 (originally scheduled for November 26, 2025)\r\n\r\n*January 14: *Advance Monthly Sales for Retail and Food Services [ https://www.census.gov/retail?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nNovember 2025 (originally scheduled for December 17, 2025)*\r\n\r\nJanuary 14: *Manufacturing and Trade: Inventories and Sales [ https://www.census.gov/mtis/?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nOctober 2025 (originally scheduled for December 17, 2025)\r\n\r\n*January 14: *Business Formation Statistics [ https://www.census.gov/econ/bfs/index.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nDecember 2025\r\n\r\n*Economic Indicators* [ https://www.census.gov/economic-indicators/calendar-listview.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n?? Save The Date\r\n\r\nCensus Bureau: American Community Survey 2020-2024 5-year estimates pre-release webinar [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/2026/2020-2024-acs-5-year-prerelease.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nOn January 22, we'll outline how to access American Community Survey (ACS) data and share tips on comparing geographies and statistics over time, so you have everything you need before the release of 2020-2024 ACS 5-year estimates on January 29.\r\n\r\n*Join Us* [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/2026/2020-2024-acs-5-year-prerelease.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\nRelated Content\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n  * *Press Kit:* 2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-Year Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-kits/2026/acs-5-year-estimates.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nMore Upcoming Webinars\r\n\r\n  * *January 20:* Methodology Updates for the Vintage 2025 Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/2026/methodology-updates-vintage-2025-estimates.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * *January 27:* Essential Skills for Finding ACS Data on data.census.gov [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/2026/essential-skills-for-finding-acs-data.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Webinars* [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/upcoming.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n?? Upcoming Releases\r\n\r\n  * *January 21: *State-to-State Migration Flows Table Package [ https://www.census.gov/topics/population/migration/guidance/state-to-state-migration-flows.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * *January 22:* 2024 Planning Database [ https://www.census.gov/topics/research/guidance/planning-databases.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * *January 27:* Small Area Income and Poverty Estimates for States, Counties and School Districts [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/saipe.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * *January 27:* Vintage 2025 Population Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/popest/about/schedule.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n  * *January 29:* 2024 Community Resilience Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/community-resilience-estimates.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * *January 29:\xc2\xa0*2020-2024 American Community Survey (ACS) 5-Year Estimates and 2020-2024 ACS 5-Year Variance Replicate Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/news/data-releases/2024/release-schedule.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nStay Connected with the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nFollow us on our social media channels, Facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], LinkedIn [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Twitter/X [ https://x.com/uscensusbureau?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], and\xc2\xa0YouTube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], so you never miss an update.\r\n\r\nStay Connected With Us on Social Media [ https://www.census.gov/about/contact-us/social_media.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Follow Us* [ https://www.census.gov/about/contact-us/social_media.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nIn Case You Missed It\r\n\r\nJarmin blog: Revolutionizing Economic Measurement at the Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/blogs/deputy-director/2026/01/revolutionizing-economic-measurement.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nIn our first blog of 2026, Deputy Director Dr. Ron Jarmin discusses how the Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s Center for Economic Studies became a hub for new data-driven research and economic measurement.\r\n\r\n*Read More * [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/blogs/deputy-director/2026/01/revolutionizing-economic-measurement.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nWe serve as the nation\xe2\x80\x99s leading provider of quality data about its people and economy.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau is the federal government's largest statistical agency. As the world\xe2\x80\x99s premier statistical agency, we are dedicated to making our nation a better place. Policy-makers, businesses, and the public use our data to make informed decisions.\r\n\r\nSubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/signup/34555 ] | Manage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] | Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] | Help [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/s/?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*Share This * [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/40409ce ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260112cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n"
