[2026-04-27 10:32:10] Raw text/plain payload: b'US Food and Drug Administration \r\nConstituent Updates\r\n\r\nFDA Human Foods Program\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nFDA Announces Australia Certificate Requirements for Bivalve Molluscs and Bivalve Mollusc Products Imported into Australia\r\n\r\n*View on the FDA Website [ https://www.fda.gov/food/hfp-constituent-updates/fda-announces-australia-certificate-requirements-bivalve-molluscs-and-bivalve-mollusc-products?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\r\n\r\nJanuary 13, 2026\r\n\r\nThe Australia Department of Agriculture, Fisheries and Forestry (DAFF) will require an official certificate for imports of bivalve molluscs and bivalve molluscs products effective February 16, 2026. DAFF has agreed to accept an FDA-issued "Certificate to a Foreign Government" (CFG) for U.S. exports of FDA-regulated bivalve molluscs and bivalve molluscs products.\r\n\r\nTo meet Australian biosecurity conditions for bivalve molluscs, only non-viable (dead) molluscs are permitted entry. Non-viable bivalve molluscs are those that have undergone processing such as shucking, chilling, freezing, cooking, marinating, and smoking. Oysters must be flesh only (no shell) and other bivalve molluscs can only include shell if they are frozen. Details on biosecurity conditions for bivalve molluscs can be found in the department\xe2\x80\x99s BICON system under seafood (excluding finfish) for human consumption\xc2\xa0BICON [ https://bicon.agriculture.gov.au/ImportConditions/Questions/EvaluateCase?elementID=0003082927&elementVersionID=187&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]External Link Disclaimer [ http://www.fda.gov/about-fda/website-policies/website-disclaimer?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\r\n\r\nBivalve molluscs and bivalve molluscs products that are covered by the certification requirement include:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Bivalve molluscs \xe2\x80\x93 clams, cockles, mussels, oysters, pipi, and scallops.\xc2\xa0 \r\n  * Bivalve mollusc products \xe2\x80\x93 foods containing any bivalve molluscs; for example, seafood mixes (such as marinara mix) that contain bivalve molluscs as an ingredient. \r\n\r\nProducts that are excluded include bivalve molluscs that are both retorted and shelf stable, or dried.\r\n\r\nIndustry may request a CFG for these covered products by submitting an online application in the HFP Export Certification Application and Tracking System (HFP eCATS). Please visit\xc2\xa0Online Applications for Export Certificates for Food [ https://www.fda.gov/food/food-export-certificates/online-applications-export-certificates-food?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0for a link to HFP eCATS and general instructions for submitting an application. \xc2\xa0U.S. applicants should select \xe2\x80\x9cSeafood\xe2\x80\x9d as the product type. Please see below for information required by DAFF for these products and instructions on how to provide this information in HFP eCATS.\r\n\r\n*Additional Certification Statements for Bivalve Molluscs and Bivalve Molluscs Products*\r\n\r\nFor a list of certification data elements required by DAFF and additional information, please refer to FDA\xe2\x80\x99s\xc2\xa0Food Export Library [ https://www.fda.gov/food/exporting-food-products-united-states/food-export-library?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0webpage. Please note that DAFF also requires an additional certification statement for bivalve molluscs and bivalve molluscs products, based on an applicant\xe2\x80\x99s attestation that the products were harvested from an area meeting U.S. shellfish standards. Applicants should copy and paste the following statement into the \xe2\x80\x9cAdditional Information for Certificate\xe2\x80\x9d free-text field box in the \xe2\x80\x9cAdditional Information\xe2\x80\x9d section of the application.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cThe product(s) described above, have been harvested from an area classified as suitable and open at the time of harvest, in accordance with U.S. shellfish sanitation controls.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\nApplicants will be required to attest that the above statement they requested to print on the certificate is factual when they electronically sign the HFP eCATS application.\r\n\r\nAdditional Information\r\n\r\n  * Food Export Library [ https://www.fda.gov/food/exporting-food-products-united-states/food-export-library?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * Online Applications for Export Certificates for Food [ https://www.fda.gov/food/food-export-certificates/online-applications-export-certificates-food?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*View Past Updates [ https://www.fda.gov/food/news-events-cfsan/cfsan-constituent-updates?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nfeed [ https://www.fda.gov/about-fda/contact-fda/subscribe-podcasts-and-news-feeds?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://www.twitter.com/US_FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/USFoodandDrugAdmin?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]flickr [ https://www.flickr.com/photos/fdaphotos/albums/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\n*Manage Subscriptions* [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 *Unsubscribe All* [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.ee0243ee8741fe358146537aecf40e1e&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 *Help* [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} td {line-height:1;} \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: U.S. Food and Drug Administration \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\r\n10903 New Hampshire Ave\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0Silver Spring, MD \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0 20993-0002\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa01-888-INFO-FDA GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
