[2026-04-27 10:32:36] Raw text/plain payload: b'Thanks for asking me to work on this. I will get started on it and keep this PR&#39;s description up to date as I form a plan and make progress.\r\n\r\n\r\n&lt;!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT --&gt;\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n&lt;details&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;summary&gt;Original prompt&lt;/summary&gt;\r\n\r\n&gt; ## Problem Description\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; Address the code quality and accessibility issues identified in PR #1 review comments:\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; ### Issues to Fix\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; 1. **Regex Pattern Issues**\r\n&gt;    - Phone number pattern `/\\d{10}/` is too broad and causes false positives\r\n&gt;    - Date pattern `/\\d{1,2}\\/\\d{1,2}\\/\\d{4}/` matches invalid dates like &quot;99/99/9999&quot;\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; 2. **Missing Test Counter Updates**\r\n&gt;    - Performance test functions don&#39;t increment `totalPassCount` or `totalFailCount`\r\n&gt;    - Affects: `testCrossDomainPerformance()`, `testNetworkOverheadOptimization()`, `testConcurrentSessionPerformance()`, `testCachingStrategy()`\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; 3. **Magic Numbers**\r\n&gt;    - Hardcoded setTimeout delays (200, 400, 600ms) without constants\r\n&gt;    - Hardcoded &quot;4&quot; for tests per category without explanation\r\n&gt;    - Hardcoded &quot;12&quot; for total tests without explanation\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; 4. **Accessibility Issues**\r\n&gt;    - Buttons lack aria-label attributes for screen readers\r\n&gt;    - Master control buttons should have accessible labels\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; 5. **HttpOnly Flag Documentation**\r\n&gt;    - Add comment explaining HttpOnly flag limitation (server-side only)\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; ### Specific Changes Required\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; 1. Update regex patterns in `containsPHI()` method:\r\n&gt;    - Phone: Change from `/\\d{10}/` to `/\\b\\d{3}[-.]?\\d{3}[-.]?\\d{4}\\b/`\r\n&gt;    - Date: Change from `/\\b\\d{1,2}\\/\\d{1,2}\\/\\d{4}\\b/` to `/\\b(0?[1-9]|1[0-2])\\/(0?[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])\\/\\d{4}\\b/`\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; 2. Extract timing constants at top of script:\r\n&gt;    - `const COMPLIANCE_TEST_INITIAL_DELAY_MS = 100`\r\n&gt;    - `const COMPLIANCE_TEST_STEP_DELAY_MS = 200`\r\n&gt;    - `const TESTS_PER_CATEGORY = 4`\r\n&gt;    - `const TOTAL_COMPLIANCE_TESTS = 12`\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; 3. Add `totalPassCount++` to performance test functions after successful logging\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; 4. Add aria-label attributes to master control buttons\r\n&gt; \r\n&gt; 5. Add clarifying comment above HttpOnly cookie option in setCookie method\r\n\r\n\r\n&lt;/details&gt;\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n&lt;!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX --&gt;\r\n\r\n*This pull request was created from Copilot chat.*\r\n&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS --&gt;\r\n---\r\n\r\n\xf0\x9f\x92\xa1 You can make Copilot smarter by setting up custom instructions, customizing its development environment and configuring Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers. Learn more [Copilot coding agent tips](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-tips) in the docs.\r\nYou can view, comment on, or merge this pull request online at:\r\n\r\n  https://github.com/jasonnorman66994-dot/vscode-wiki/pull/2\r\n\r\n-- Commit Summary --\r\n\r\n  * Initial plan\r\n\r\n-- File Changes --\r\n\r\n\r\n-- Patch Links --\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/jasonnorman66994-dot/vscode-wiki/pull/2.patch\r\nhttps://github.com/jasonnorman66994-dot/vscode-wiki/pull/2.diff\r\n\r\n-- \r\nReply to this email directly or view it on GitHub:\r\nhttps://github.com/jasonnorman66994-dot/vscode-wiki/pull/2\r\nYou are receiving this because you were assigned.\r\n\r\nMessage ID: &lt;jasonnorman66994-dot/vscode-wiki/pull/2@github.com&gt;\r\n'
