[2026-04-27 10:32:51] Raw text/plain payload: b"Industry-level detail provides new insights on the growing space economy. Learn more in this America Counts story.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/space-economy.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAmerica Counts: Stories Behind the Numbers\r\n\r\nA satellite orbits Earth above glowing city lights. [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/space-economy.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nExploring New Frontiers With the Quarterly Workforce Indicators\r\n\r\nThe \xe2\x80\x9cspace economy\xe2\x80\x9d continues to soar and younger workers are fueling the industry\xe2\x80\x99s upward trajectory.\r\n\r\nThe extraterrestrial industry accounted for $142.5 billion (0.5%) of U.S. GDP in 2023, combining activities from the Manufacturing, Transportation, and Information sectors, including Satellite Telecommunications and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing.'\r\n\r\nThe U.S. Census Bureau released today the first ever Quarterly Workforce Indicators (QWI) at the national industry level. These data will allow users to view and download economic indicators such as employment, job creation, earnings and other measures of employment flows for six-digit North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) codes.\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/space-economy.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\nThis level of detail opens new paths for analyzing parts of the economy that cross industry groups and provides unprecedented detail on the inner workings of our economy. The powerful new data enable us to boldly go where no one has gone before when examining this workforce of the future.\r\n\r\n*Continue reading [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/space-economy.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] *to learn how the space economy impacts GDP and is increasingly driven by younger workers.\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nStay Connected with the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nFollow us on our social media channels, Facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], LinkedIn [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Twitter/X [ https://x.com/uscensusbureau?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], and\xc2\xa0YouTube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], so you never miss an update.\r\n\r\nStay Connected With Us on Social Media [ https://www.census.gov/about/contact-us/social_media.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Follow Us* [ https://www.census.gov/about/contact-us/social_media.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nYou May Be Interested In\r\n\r\nU.S. Workforce is Aging, Especially in Some Firms\r\n\r\nA construction worker carries pipes at a job site. [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2025/12/older-workers.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nFirms in sectors like utilities and manufacturing and states like Maine are more likely to have a high share of workers over age 55.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2025/12/older-workers.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout America Counts [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nAmerica Counts features stories on various topics including:\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Families [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FFamilies ],\xc2\xa0Housing [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FHousing ],\xc2\xa0Employment [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FEmployment ], Business and Economy [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2Fbusiness-economy ] \r\n  * Education [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FEducation ], [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FEducation ] Health [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FHealth ], Population [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FThePopulation ], Income and Poverty [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FIncome-Poverty ] \r\n\r\n*For the Media:*\xc2\xa0Contact our\xc2\xa0Public Information Office [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/about.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0for inquiries or interviews.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nDon't miss an America Counts story!\xc2\xa0Use the button below to sign up and update your preferences.\r\n\r\nSubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/signup/34555 ] | Manage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] | Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] | Help [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/s/?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*Share This * [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/4043da3 ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260113aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n"
