[2026-04-27 10:32:56] Raw text/plain payload: b'If your email program has trouble displaying this email, view as a webpage [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/bulletins/4044180 ].\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nUS Food and Drug Administration\r\nFDA Issues Guidance on Modernizing Statistical Methods for Clinical Trials [ https://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-issues-guidance-modernizing-statistical-methods-clinical-trials?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nThe U.S. Food and Drug Administration published on Monday, January 12, 2025 a draft guidance [ https://www.fda.gov/regulatory-information/search-fda-guidance-documents/use-bayesian-methodology-clinical-trials-drug-and-biological-products?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0designed to facilitate the use of Bayesian methodologies in clinical trials of drugs and biologics, helping drug developers make better use of available data, conduct more efficient clinical trials, and deliver safe and effective treatments to patients sooner.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n"Bayesian methodologies help address two of the biggest problems of drug development: high costs and long timelines,\xe2\x80\x9d\xc2\xa0*said FDA Commissioner Marty Makary, M.D., M.P.H*. \xe2\x80\x9cProviding clarity around modern statistical methods will help sponsors bring more cures and meaningful treatments to patients faster and more affordably.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\nBayesian approaches use a different framework from traditional statistical approaches. In a Bayesian analysis, data from a study are combined with relevant prior information to form a new distribution that can be used for inference and to draw conclusions about safety and efficacy.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nExamples of Bayesian calculations used in various ways in clinical trials can include:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Determining futility or success earlier in adaptive trials. \r\n  * Informing design elements like dose selection in subsequent trials. \r\n  * Incorporating information from other sources, such as previous clinical study data, real-world evidence, and external or nonconcurrent controls. \r\n  * Facilitating subgroup analyses. \r\n  * Supporting primary inference in a trial. \r\n\r\nThe guidance provides recommendations on the appropriate use of Bayesian methods, with an emphasis on the use of these methods to support primary inference. Bayesian methods may be especially valuable for sponsors targeting rare or pediatric indications, where patient populations are smaller.\r\n\r\nThe publication of this guidance \xe2\x80\x94\xc2\xa0"Use of Bayesian Methodology in Clinical Trials of Drugs and Biologics Guidance for Industry" [ https://www.fda.gov/regulatory-information/search-fda-guidance-documents/use-bayesian-methodology-clinical-trials-drug-and-biological-products?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0\xe2\x80\x94 is intended to satisfy the FDA\xe2\x80\x99s commitment in the Prescription Drug User Fee Act (PDUFA) VII. As part of the sixth reauthorization of the PDUFA, the FDA and industry agreed to performance goals around enhancing the capacity to review complex innovative trial designs, including a commitment to publish draft guidance on the use of Bayesian methodology in clinical trials of drugs and biological products (see\xc2\xa0PDUFA VII Performance Goals Letter [ https://www.fda.gov/media/151712/download?attachment=&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Section I.L.4.f).\r\n\r\nThe FDA is seeking public comment on the draft guidance, titled\xc2\xa0"Use of Bayesian Methodology in Clinical Trials of Drugs and Biologics; Draft Guidance for Industry".\r\n\r\n###\r\n\r\nThe FDA, an agency within the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, protects the public health by assuring the safety, effectiveness, and security of human and veterinary drugs, vaccines and other biological products for human use, and medical devices. The agency also is responsible for the safety and security of our nation\xe2\x80\x99s food supply, cosmetics, dietary supplements, radiation-emitting electronic products, and for regulating tobacco products.\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nfeed [ https://www.fda.gov/about-fda/contact-fda/subscribe-podcasts-and-news-feeds?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://www.twitter.com/US_FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/USFoodandDrugAdmin?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]flickr [ https://www.flickr.com/photos/fdaphotos/albums/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\n*Manage Subscriptions* [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 *Unsubscribe All* [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.ee0243ee8741fe358146537aecf40e1e&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 *Help* [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} td {line-height:1;} \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: U.S. Food and Drug Administration \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\r\n10903 New Hampshire Ave\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0Silver Spring, MD \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0 20993-0002\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa01-888-INFO-FDA GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
