[2026-04-27 10:33:29] Raw text/plain payload: b'We take a look back at 10 years of the Taking Measure blog.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nn i s t  \r\n \r\n\r\nView as a Web Page [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/bulletins/4033f5a ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nTaking Measure Blog\r\n \r\nTaking Measure Celebrates 10 Years of Science and Stories\r\n\r\nTara Fortier is wearing safety glasses as she reaches into a box of circuitry and other equipment, which emits a green glow.  [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/taking-measure-celebrates-10-years-science-and-stories ] \r\n\r\nWhen Taking Measure launched\xc2\xa0on Jan. 14, 2016, then-NIST Director Willie May wrote\xc2\xa0in the\xc2\xa0inaugural post:\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cThrough this blog,\xc2\xa0we\xe2\x80\x99d\xc2\xa0like to share with you our excitement and passion for the work we do. I hope we can answer some of your questions about science and technology, and about\xe2\x80\xaf"why"\xe2\x80\xafwe do this work. This blog will give you a glimpse into our labs and show you where science is today and where it might take us tomorrow.\xe2\x80\x9d\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nOver the past 10 years,\xc2\xa0we\xe2\x80\x99ve\xc2\xa0done just that.\xc2\xa0We\xe2\x80\x99ve\xc2\xa0heard from\xc2\xa0dozens\xc2\xa0of researchers\xc2\xa0and delved into topics ranging from\xc2\xa0the metric system to microbiology\xc2\xa0in more than 400\xc2\xa0individual\xc2\xa0posts.\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nRead More [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/taking-measure-celebrates-10-years-science-and-stories ]\r\n \r\nIN CASE YOU MISSED IT\r\n \r\nPhotos of everyday objects like an iron, a gas can and a laptop along with high-tech items like an atomic clock and a mass balance. [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/safer-skies-fewer-fires-10-ways-nist-impacts-your-daily-life ] \r\nFrom Safer Skies to Fewer Fires: 10 Ways NIST Impacts Your Daily Life\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n"December 19, 2024"\r\n\r\nMuch of the work NIST does may seem far removed from your daily life. After all, how often do you find yourself trapping ions or measuring the nutrients in peanut butter?\r\n\r\nBut the reality is that there are many ways our work tangibly impacts \xe2\x80\x94 and improves \xe2\x80\x94 your daily life and the U.S. economy.\r\n\r\nRead More [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/safer-skies-fewer-fires-10-ways-nist-impacts-your-daily-life ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nConnect with us\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/NIST ]X [ https://twitter.com/NIST ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/NIST ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/nist ]flickr [ https://www.instagram.com/nist/ ]  \r\n\r\nReceived this email from a friend? Subscribe here [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/new?topic_id=USNIST_1 ].\r\n\r\n NIST [ https://www.nist.gov ] \r\n\r\nSubscriber services:\r\n\r\nManage Preferences [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIf you have questions or problems with the subscription service, please contact subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ].\r\nTechnical questions? Contact inquiries@nist.gov. (301) 975-NIST (6478).\r\n\r\nThis service is provided to you at no charge by National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST).\xc2\xa0100 Bureau Drive, Stop 1070\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7 Gaithersburg, MD 20899\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0301-975-6478\r\n\r\n GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
