[2026-04-27 10:34:53] Raw text/plain payload: b"The U.S. Census Bureau is scheduled to hold a webinar on methodology updates for the Vintage 2025 population estimates.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/webinar-methodology-updates.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios2&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nPopulation Estimates Methodology Webinar [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/webinar-methodology-updates.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios2&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nThe U.S. Census Bureau is scheduled to hold a webinar [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/2026/methodology-updates-vintage-2025-estimates.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios2&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] Tuesday, Jan. 20, at 1:30 p.m. ET, on methodology updates for the Vintage 2025 population estimates.\r\n\r\nThe Population Estimates Program (PEP) develops the official estimates of population and housing units for the Census Bureau. Every year, PEP builds a time series of estimates that starts at the date of the most recent decennial census and extends through the vintage year, which represents the latest year of estimates available.\r\n\r\nLearn more about the population estimates and updates to the methodology [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/blogs/random-samplings/2026/01/updates-data-methodology-population-estimates.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios2&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] for the Vintage 2025\xc2\xa0estimates series at this webinar.\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/webinar-methodology-updates.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios2&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHelp us spread the word about Census Bureau data!\r\n\r\nShare this on social media or forward it to a friend.\r\n\r\n*Share This* [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/4048e3b ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n??You May Be Interested In\r\n\r\n  * *Blog:* Annual Updates to the Data and Methodology Used to Produce Population Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/blogs/random-samplings/2026/01/updates-data-methodology-population-estimates.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios2&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  *  [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/2026/methodology-updates-vintage-2025-estimates.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios2&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*Schedule:* Population and Housing Unit Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/popest/about/schedule.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios2&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nWe serve as the nation\xe2\x80\x99s leading provider of quality data about its people and economy.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau is the federal government's largest statistical agency. As the world\xe2\x80\x99s premier statistical agency, we are dedicated to making our nation a better place. Policy-makers, businesses, and the public use our data to make informed decisions.\r\n\r\nResources for Media\r\n\r\nFor media interviews, please contact the\xc2\xa0Public Information Office [ https://lnks.gd/l/eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..p-5wpj2DTx0_qgyLiv6JuMTDOF_vZlHcwFpt971jIDs/s/866068797/br/124287751808-l?utm_campaign=20260115pios2&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Toll Free at 877-861-2010, 301-763-3030, or\xc2\xa0pio@census.gov.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n*Stay connected with us!*\r\n\r\nJoin the conversation on social media.\r\n\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260115pios2&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260115pios2&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260115pios2&utm_medium=email&utm_