[2026-04-27 10:35:03] Raw text/plain payload: b"Census Bureau to Host Prerelease Webinar on 2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-Year Estimates  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-estimates-webinar-embargo.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n2020-2024 ACS-5YR Prerelease Webinar [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-estimates-webinar-embargo.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nThe U.S. Census Bureau is scheduled to hold a prerelease webinar [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/2026/2020-2024-acs-5-year-prerelease.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] about the 2020-2024 American Community Survey [ http://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/about.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (ACS) 5-year estimates on Thursday, Jan. 22, at 1 p.m. ET. The webinar will explain how to access ACS data and give tips on comparing geographies and statistics over time.\r\n\r\nThe ACS [ http://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] provides a wide range of statistics about the nation\xe2\x80\x99s people and housing, such as language spoken at home, education, commuting, employment, mortgage status and rent, income, poverty, and health insurance coverage. It is the only source of local estimates for most of the 40-plus topics [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/guidance/subjects.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] it covers.\r\n\r\nStatistics will be available to embargo subscribers beginning Jan. 27, at 10 a.m. ET for a variety of geographic areas, including all states, the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico, congressional and state legislative districts, metropolitan and micropolitan statistical areas, counties, places, and other geographies down to census tracts and block groups.\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-estimates-webinar-embargo.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n*Embargo subscribers* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/releases/archives/embargoed_releases/?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]* will have access to the statistics from Tuesday, **Jan. 27, at 10 a.m. **ET, to Thursday, Jan. 29, at 12:01 a.m. ET. *Wire and distribution services are prohibited from distributing embargoed news stories and data files before the public release date and time. For more information, refer to the Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s\xc2\xa0embargo policy [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/embargo/embargo-policy.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]. *All datasets will be available to the public Thursday, Jan. 29, by 10 a.m. ET.*\r\n\r\nRegister for embargo access at: www.census.gov/newsroom/releases/archives/embargoed_releases [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/releases/archives/embargoed_releases?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*What: *\r\n\r\n2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-Year Estimates Prerelease Webinar\r\n\r\n*When*:\r\n\r\nThursday, Jan. 22, at 1 p.m. ET\r\n\r\n*Who*:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Gretchen Gooding [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/bios/gretchen-gooding.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], chief, American Community Survey Office Outreach and Education Branch \r\n  * Vicki Mack [ https://www2.census.gov/about/training-workshops/courses/discovering-the-acs/vicki-mack-bio.pdf?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], statistician, American Community Survey Office \r\n  * Jewel Jordan [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/bios/jewel-jordan.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], public affairs specialist, Public Information Office \r\n\r\n*Access*:\r\n\r\nThe webinar will consist of a simultaneous audio conference and online presentation. Attendees do not have to call into the webinar to hear the audio. Credentialed media and data users will be able to ask questions during the webinar utilizing the Q&A feature and after the presentation through audio.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nRegistration link:\r\n\r\nwww.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/2026/2020-2024-acs-5-year-prerelease.html\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHelp us spread the word about Census Bureau data!\r\n\r\nShare this on social media or forward it to a friend.\r\n\r\n*Share This* [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/404902f ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nYou May Be Interested In\r\n\r\n  * Press Kit: 2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-Year Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-kits/2026/acs-5-year-estimates.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nWe serve as the nation\xe2\x80\x99s leading provider of quality data about its people and economy.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau is the federal government's largest statistical agency. As the world\xe2\x80\x99s premier statistical agency, we are dedicated to making our nation a better place. Policy-makers, businesses, and the public use our data to make informed decisions.\r\n\r\nResources for Media\r\n\r\nFor media interviews, please contact the\xc2\xa0Public Information Office [ https://lnks.gd/l/eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..p-5wpj2DTx0_qgyLiv6JuMTDOF_vZlHcwFpt971jIDs/s/866068797/br/124287751808-l?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Toll Free at 877-861-2010, 301-763-3030, or\xc2\xa0pio@census.gov.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n*Stay connected with us!*\r\n\r\nJoin the conversation on social media.\r\n\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nSubscriber Settings [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Remove me from All Subscriptions  [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n&lt;!-- /* template top padding on mobile */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { table#flexible-abe-main-table { padding:0 !important; } } --&gt; ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260115pios4&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n"
