[2026-04-27 10:35:31] Raw text/plain payload: b"Bookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/bulletins/404bccd?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nIRS.gov Banner \r\n\r\nIRS Newswire\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nJanuary 16, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nIssue Number:\xc2\xa0 IR-2026-09\r\n\r\nInside This Issue\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*Treasury, IRS: Supplemental basic allowance for housing payments to members of the military are not taxable \xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\nIR-2026-09, Jan. 16, 2026\r\n\r\nWASHINGTON \xe2\x80\x94 The Department of the Treasury and the Internal Revenue Service today confirmed that supplemental basic allowance for housing payments made to members of the uniformed services in December 2025 are not to be included in income by those who received the payments; they are not taxable.\r\n\r\nIn the One, Big, Beautiful Bill enacted last July, Congress appropriated $2.9 billion to supplement the basic allowance for housing payable to members of the uniformed services. In December, President Donald J. Trump announced that 1,450,000 military service members would receive a special \xe2\x80\x9cWarrior Dividend\xe2\x80\x9d before Christmas.\r\n\r\nThe resulting one-time supplemental payments of $1,776 made primarily to active-duty members of the uniformed services in the pay grades of O-6 and below and eligible Reserve Component members as of Nov. 30, 2025, of the Army, Air Force, Navy, Marine Corps and Space Force were funded by this appropriation.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nFederal tax law specifically excludes from gross income a \xe2\x80\x9cqualified military benefit.\xe2\x80\x9d\xc2\xa0 The basic allowance for housing payments are qualified military benefits and, therefore, are not taxable.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ] \xc2\xa0Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ] \xc2\xa0LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to the IRS Newswire, an IRS e-mail service.\r\n\r\nIf you know someone who might want to subscribe to this mailing list, please forward this message to them so they can subscribe [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ].\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically from the mailing list IRS Newswire. *Please Do Not Reply To This Message.*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNews Essentials\r\n\r\nWhat's Hot [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/whats-hot ]\r\n\r\nNews Releases [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\nIRS - The Basics [ https://www.irs.gov/about-irs/irs-the-basics ]\r\n\r\nIRS Guidance [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/understanding-irs-guidance-a-brief-primer ]\r\n\r\nMedia Contacts [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-media-relations-office-contact-number ]\r\n\r\nFacts & Figures [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nAround The Nation [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/around-the-nation ]\r\n\r\ne-News Subscriptions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe Newsroom Topics\r\n\r\nMultimedia Center [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/multimedia-center ]\r\n\r\nNoticias en Espa\xc3\xb1ol [ https://www.irs.gov/es/spanish/noticias-en-espanol ]\r\n\r\nRadio PSAs [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-radio-psas ]\r\n\r\nTax Scams [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-scams-consumer-alerts ]\r\n\r\nThe Tax Gap [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/the-tax-gap ]\r\n\r\nFact Sheets [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nIRS Tax Tips [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-tax-tips ]\r\n\r\nArmed Forces [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-information-for-members-of-the-us-armed-forces ]\r\n\r\nLatest News Home [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIRS Resources\r\n\r\nContact My Local Office [ https://www.irs.gov/help/contact-your-local-irs-office ]\r\n\r\nFiling Options [ https://www.irs.gov/filing ]\r\n\r\nForms & Instructions [ https://www.irs.gov/forms-instructions ]\r\n\r\nFrequently Asked Questions [ https://www.irs.gov/help/telephone-assistance ]\r\n\r\nNews [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom ]\r\n\r\nTaxpayer Advocate [ https://www.irs.gov/taxpayer-advocate ]\r\n\r\nWhere to File [ https://www.irs.gov/filing/where-to-file-paper-tax-returns-with-or-without-a-payment ]\r\n\r\nIRS Social Media [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-new-media-1 ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n/*start reset css*/ div { line-height: 1; } body, table, td, p, a, li, blockquote { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; } body { -webkit-text-size-adjust: none; -ms-text-size-adjust: none; } table { border-spacing: 0; } table, td { mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; } img { -ms-interpolation-mode: bicubic; } body { margin: 0; padding: 0; } img { border: none !important; height: auto; line-height: 1; outline: none; text-decoration: none; } table td { border-collapse: collapse !important; } .preheader { display: none !important; visibility: hidden; opacity: 0; color: transparent; height: 0; width: 0; } /*end reset css*/ a[x-apple-data-detectors] { color: inherit !important; text-decoration: none !important; font-size: inherit !important; font-family: inherit !important; font-weight: inherit !important; line-height: inherit !important; } /* Sets the line height in everything but Outlook */ table#yahoo body, table#yahoo p, table#yahoo .gd_p, table#yahoo p span, table#yahoo li, table#yahoo li span { line-height: 1.4; } /* outlook.com line-height contr