[2026-04-27 10:35:45] Raw text/plain payload: b'Explore statistics on hires and separations to and from employment in the U.S. with a focus on worker reallocation across employers.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/data/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#j2j ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n2025 Q4 Job-to-Job Flows Release [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/data/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#j2j ] \r\n\r\nThe U.S. Census Bureau has completed the 2025 Q4 release of Job-to-Job Flows (J2J) data. J2J Flows are statistics on hires and separations to and from employment in the United States, with a focus on worker reallocation across employers. For release-specific data notices, please consult the Job-to-Job Flows Data Notices [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/doc/J2J_data_notices.pdf?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\xc2\xa0 \r\n\r\nJ2J data can be accessed via:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Data and Documentation [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/data/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#j2j ] \r\n  * Data Download [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/data/j2j/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * Explore the Data [ https://j2jexplorer.ces.census.gov/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * Data Extraction [ https://ledextract.ces.census.gov/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n"The latest available data in the 2025 Q4 release is 2024 Q4 for most states. In the event that data submission or data quality issues are encountered, J2J releases for a state may be delayed or skipped for one or several quarters, until the issue can be resolved."\r\n\r\nFor comments or questions, please contact CES.J2J.Feedback@census.gov.\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/data/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#j2j ] \r\n \r\n\r\nJ2J is a set of statistics on job mobility in the United States. J2J include statistics on: (1) the job-to-job transition rate, (2) hires and separations to and from employment, (3) earnings changes due to job change, and (4) characteristics of origin and destination jobs for job-to-job transitions. These statistics are available at the national, state, and metropolitan area levels and by worker and firm characteristics.\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHelp us spread the word about Census Bureau data!\r\n\r\nShare this on social media or forward it to a friend.\r\n\r\n*Share This* [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/404c3a3 ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nWe serve as the nation\xe2\x80\x99s leading provider of quality data about its people and economy.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau is the federal government\'s largest statistical agency. As the world\xe2\x80\x99s premier statistical agency, we are dedicated to making our nation a better place. Policy-makers, businesses, and the public use our data to make informed decisions.\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n*Stay connected with us!*\r\n\r\nJoin the conversation on social media.\r\n\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nSubscriber Settings [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Remove me from All Subscriptions  [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n&lt;!-- /* template top padding on mobile */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { table#flexible-abe-main-table { padding:0 !important; } } --&gt; ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260116cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
