[2026-04-27 10:35:46] Raw text/plain payload: b'If your email program has trouble displaying this email, view as a webpage [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/bulletins/404c4d9 ].\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUS Food and Drug Administration  \r\n \r\n*FDA Grants Full Approval of First Oral Treatment for Lymphoma in Dogs*\r\n\r\nJanuary 16, 2026\r\n\r\nThe U.S. Food and Drug Administration recently granted full approval of Laverdia (verdinexor tablets) to treat dogs with lymphoma, a type of cancer of the lymph nodes and lymphatic system. Laverdia prevents certain proteins from leaving the nucleus of cancer cells, thereby allowing these proteins to control the growth and prevent the spread of cancerous cells in dogs.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nThe FDA initially granted Laverdia\xc2\xa0conditional approval in January 2021 [ https://web.archive.org/web/20210202150059/https:/www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-conditionally-approves-first-oral-tablet-treat-lymphoma-dogs?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0through the\xc2\xa0Minor Use/Minor Species [ https://www.fda.gov/animal-veterinary/development-approval-process/minor-useminor-species?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0pathway, which is an option for drugs intended for minor uses in major species (dogs, cats, horses, cattle, pigs, turkeys and chickens) or for minor species. Canine lymphoma affects fewer than 80,000 dogs in the U.S. each year, which qualifies as a minor use in a major species.\r\n\r\nAfter four annual renewals of the conditional approval, the drug sponsor, Anivive Lifesciences, Inc., of Long Beach, California, generated the necessary effectiveness data to support a full approval.\r\n\r\nRead More Button [ https://www.fda.gov/animal-veterinary/cvm-updates/fda-grants-full-approval-first-oral-treatment-lymphoma-dogs?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n"*\r\nYou are subscribed to updates from FDA\'s Center for Veterinary Medicine.*"\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nfeed [ https://www.fda.gov/about-fda/contact-fda/subscribe-podcasts-and-news-feeds?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://www.twitter.com/US_FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/USFoodandDrugAdmin?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]flickr [ https://www.flickr.com/photos/fdaphotos/albums/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\n*Manage Subscriptions* [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 *Unsubscribe All* [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.ee0243ee8741fe358146537aecf40e1e&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 *Help* [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} td {line-height:1;} \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: U.S. Food and Drug Administration \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\r\n10903 New Hampshire Ave\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0Silver Spring, MD \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0 20993-0002\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa01-888-INFO-FDA GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
