[2026-04-27 10:35:54] Raw text/plain payload: b'This Communication is Part of the Medical Device Recalls and Early Alerts Program.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nIf your email program has trouble displaying this email, view as a webpage [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/bulletins/40427b2 ].\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nMedWatch Banner \r\n\r\nBookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/bulletins/40427b2?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nEarly Alert: Broselow Rainbow Tape Issue from AirLife\r\n\r\nThe FDA is aware that AirLife has issued a letter to affected customers recommending certain Broselow Rainbow Tapes be removed from where they are used or sold.\r\n\r\nAirLife stated that the affected product version contains three medication-related errors regarding doses. The clinical consequences for incorrect medication doses based on the printed information may be serious or life-threatening.\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.fda.gov/medical-devices/medical-device-recalls-and-early-alerts/early-alert-broselow-rainbow-tape-issue-airlife?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n*Questions?*\r\n\r\nCustomers in the U.S. with adverse reactions, quality problems, or questions about this issue should contact AirLife at productquality@myairlife.com or 1-800-433-2797.\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Follow us on X at @FDAMedWatch [ https://twitter.com/FDAMedWatch?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nfeed [ https://www.fda.gov/about-fda/contact-fda/subscribe-podcasts-and-news-feeds?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://www.twitter.com/US_FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/USFoodandDrugAdmin?utm