[2026-04-27 10:36:06] Raw text/plain payload: b"Having trouble viewing this email? View it as a Web page [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/bulletins/404dc6c ].\r\n\r\nBookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/bulletins/404dc6c?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nThank you for requesting to receive email notifications of updates to the Standards Incorporated by Reference database managed by NIST.\r\n\r\nThe following Incorporated by Reference records have been recently added or updated:\r\n\r\nSafety Standard for Toys: Requirements for Water Beads - Standard Consumer Safety Specification for Toy Safety, approved on August 1, 2023 (ASTM F963\xe2\x80\x9323) [ https://sibr.nist.gov/record/safety-standard-toys-requirements-water-beads-0 ] 01/14/2026 01:12 PM EST \r\nSection 106(a) of the Consumer Product Safety Improvement Act of 2008 (CPSIA) mandates that ASTM F963 shall be a mandatory toy safety standard. This safety standard sets forth requirements for water bead toys and toys that contain water beads. Under this statutory authority, the U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission (CPSC or Commission) is issuing a safety standard for water bead toys and toys that contain water beads. Safety Standard for Bassinets and Cradles - Standard Consumer Safety Specification for Bassinets and Cradles (ASTM F2194\xe2\x80\x9325) [ https://sibr.nist.gov/record/safety-standard-bassinets-and-cradles ] 01/14/2026 01:04 PM EST \r\nIn 2013, the U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission (CPSC) published a consumer product safety standard for bassinets and cradles under section 104 of the Consumer Product Safety Improvement Act of 2008 (CPSIA). The standard incorporated by reference ASTM F2194-13, Standard Consumer Safety Specification for Bassinets and Cradles, with modifications to make the standard more stringent. The CPSIA sets forth a process for updating mandatory standards for durable infant or toddler products that are based on a voluntary standard, when a voluntary standards organization revises the standard. Consistent with the CPSIA update process, this direct final rule updates the mandatory standard for bassinets and cradles to incorporate by reference ASTM's 2025 version of the voluntary standard. Safety Standard for Toys: Requirements for Water Beads - American National Standard for Product Safety Signs and Labels (approved December 14, 2023) (ANSI Z535.4\xe2\x80\x932023) [ https://sibr.nist.gov/record/safety-standard-toys-requirements-water-beads ] 01/14/2026 01:04 PM EST \r\nSection 106(a) of the Consumer Product Safety Improvement Act of 2008 (CPSIA) mandates that ASTM F963 shall be a mandatory toy safety standard. This safety standard sets forth requirements for water bead toys and toys that contain water beads. Under this statutory authority, the U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission (CPSC or Commission) is issuing a safety standard for water bead toys and toys that contain water beads. body { font-size: 1em; font-family: Arial, Verdana, sans-serif; font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; color: #333333; } \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nIf you believe you have subscribed to these notices in error or no longer want to hear from us, please click the link [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/unsubscribe_from_topic?verification=5.7268a8d7e31cfb6335ae8e42de52587e&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com&topic_id=USNIST_613 ] to unsubscribe at any time. Feel free to contact us with any comments or questions you may have about these notifications at standardsinfo@nist.gov.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nHaving trouble viewing this email? View it as a Web page [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/bulletins/404dc6c ].\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nNIST [ http://www.nist.gov/ ] \r\nQuestions?\xc2\xa0Contact Us [ http://www.nist.gov/public_affairs/contact.cfm ] \r\n\r\nSTAY CONNECTED:\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 [ https://www.facebook.com/NIST ]  \xc2\xa0X [ https://twitter.com/NIST ]  \xc2\xa0 [ https://www.youtube.com/NIST ]  instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/nist/ ] \xc2\xa0 [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/nist ]  \r\n \r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES: Manage Preferences [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIf you have questions or problems with the subscription service, please contact subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ].\r\nTechnical questions? Contact inquiries@nist.gov. (301) 975-NIST (6478).\r\n\r\nThis service is provided to you at no charge by National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST).\xc2\xa0100 Bureau Drive, Stop 1070\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7 Gaithersburg, MD 20899\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0301-975-6478\r\n\r\n GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n"
