[2026-04-27 10:37:16] Raw text/plain payload: b"Explore common energy storage practices across states and applications \xe2\x80\x94 February 24-26, 2026, from 2:00 PM to 4:00 PM ET.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nHaving trouble viewing this email? View it as a Web page [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOESNLEC/bulletins/40526c0 ].\r\n\r\nScandia National Laboratories [ https://www.sandia.gov/ ]  \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nPhoto: Aerial view of industrial battery units storing electricity in the desert. / Credit: Getty Images \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nEnergy storage practices across states and applications\r\n\r\n*Feb. 24, 25, 26, 2026, 2:00 PM-4:00 PM ET each day\xc2\xa0\r\n(Live online)*\r\n\r\nState energy regulators and utility commissioners can learn more about energy storage, accommodating data centers, and large loads at an upcoming NARUC-hosted professional development series. Sandia\xe2\x80\x99s Will McNamara, a technical systems analyst with a 30-year career in the energy and utilities industry, is one of the instructors. Course information derives in part from\xc2\xa0energy storage research [ https://energy.sandia.gov/programs/energy-storage/ ]\xc2\xa0at Sandia, supported by the Department of Energy\xe2\x80\x99s Office of Electricity energy storage program, and collaboration with the Energy Policy Design Institute, state officials, utilities, universities, technology developers, and other national laboratories.\r\n\r\nAmong other topics, the course will share the basics of energy storage technologies, including long-duration energy storage (LDES) and how these technologies integrate and serve the electric grid.\r\n\r\nThe course is provided through the National Association of Regulatory Utility Commissioners. To register,\xc2\xa0visit the NARUC website. [ https://www.naruc.org/events/all-events/designing-state-level-regulations-for-energy-storage/ ]\r\n\r\n*Register* [ https://www.naruc.org/events/all-events/designing-state-level-regulations-for-energy-storage/ ] \r\n \r\n\r\nLet's stay in touch\r\n\r\nWe're transitioning to a new email communications tool. To continue receiving our updates and invitations, please *sign up on our new list. [ https://hbeupdate.custhelp.com/ci/documents/detail/2/formOptIn_EnergyStorage ]*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nSandia National Laboratories is a multimission laboratory managed and operated by National Technology and Engineering Solutions of Sandia, LLC, a wholly owned subsidiary of Honeywell International, Inc., for the U.S. Department of Energy\xe2\x80\x99s National Nuclear Security Administration under contract DE-NA-0003525.\xc2\xa0\r\n\xc2\xa9 2026 National Technology & Engineering Solutions of Sandia, LLC\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\nManage Preferences [ http://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOESNLEC/subscribers/new?preferences=true ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOESNLEC/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.1385db987570cec7c53f0feb5a7d4a5b&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0Help [ subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com ]\r\n\r\nQuestions?\r\nContact Us [ https://www.sandia.gov/contact_us/index.html ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: Sandia National Laboratories \xc2\xb7 1515 Eubank SE \xc2\xb7 Albuquerque, NM 87123 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;} p, li, h1, h2, h3 { overflow-wrap: normal; word-wrap: