[2026-04-27 10:37:27] Raw text/plain payload: b'NIST  \r\n \r\n\r\nView As Web Page [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/bulletins/40538fb ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\nHeader  \r\n \r\n\r\nNIST Cybersecurity and Privacy Program\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*NIST First Call for Multi-Party Threshold Schemes: NIST IR 8214C*\r\n\r\nNIST has published *Internal Report (IR) 8214C*, NIST First Call for Multi-Party Threshold Schemes [ https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/ir/8214/c/final ], which calls for public submissions of *multi-party threshold schemes* and related crypto-systems. These systems enable the distribution of trust regarding the creation, storage, and use of private/secret keys needed by cryptographic primitives.\r\n\r\nThe scope of this NIST Threshold Call includes NIST-approved primitives (e.g., *signatures*, *encryption*, *symmetric-key* and *hashing*-related primitives, *key generation*), and others, such as *fully-homomorphic encryption* (FHE) and *zero-knowledge proofs* (ZKP).\r\n\r\nThe Threshold Call asks for submission packages with a *technical specification*, an open-source *reference implementation*, a *report on experimental evaluation*, and *notes on patent claims*. Additionally, this NIST Threshold Call:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Organizes the scope into two classes (N and S), each with multiple categories \r\n  * Discusses the vision of collecting a body of reference materials on advanced cryptography \r\n  * Organizes the process into three phases: Previews, Packages, and Analysis \r\n  * Outlines the required structure of a submission package \r\n  * Establishes security requirements and other requirements specific to each category \r\n\r\nThere will be three opportunities to present \xe2\x80\x9cpreviews\xe2\x80\x9d (plans of upcoming package submissions). The first opportunity will be hosted at MPTS 2026 [ https://csrc.nist.gov/events/2026/mpts2026 ], the NIST Workshop on Multi-Party Threshold Schemes.\r\n\r\nAdditional information can be found at https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/threshold-cryptography\r\n\r\nRead More [ https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/ir/8214/c/final ]\r\n \r\n\r\n*NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy Program*\r\nQuestions and comments can be directed to: nistir-8214C-comments@nist.gov\r\nCSRC Website questions:\xc2\xa0csrc-inquiry@nist.gov\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nConnect with us\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/NIST ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/NIST ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/NIST ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/nist ]flickr [ https://www.instagram.com/nist/ ]  \r\n\r\nReceived this email from a friend? Subscribe here [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/new?topic_id=USNIST_1 ].\r\n\r\n ITL NIST [ https://www.nist.gov/itl ] \r\n\r\nSubscriber services:\r\n\r\nManage Preferences [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIf you have questions or problems with the subscription service, please contact subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ].\r\nTechnical questions? Contact inquiries@nist.gov. (301) 975-NIST (6478).\r\n\r\nThis service is provided to you at no charge by National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST).\xc2\xa0100 Bureau Drive, Stop 1070\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7 Gaithersburg, MD 20899\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0301-975-6478\r\n\r\n GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
