[2026-04-27 10:37:41] Raw text/plain payload: b"Divorce can negatively affect children, even into adulthood. Read more on America Counts.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/divorce-affects-children.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAmerica Counts: Stories Behind the Numbers\r\n\r\nA man walks in a rural area holding two young children's hands. Farm equipment in the background.  [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/divorce-affects-children.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nThe Long-Term Effects of Divorce on Children\r\n\r\nNearly one-third of Americans born between 1988 and 1993 experienced their parents\xe2\x80\x99 divorce before reaching adulthood, a watershed event for a child that can negatively impact them throughout their life.\r\n\r\nA U.S. Census Bureau\xc2\xa0working paper\xc2\xa0linked parental divorce to lower income, reduced likelihood of living away from home while attending college, and higher rates of teen pregnancy, incarceration and mortality.\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/divorce-affects-children.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\nResearchers Maggie R. Jones (U.S. Census Bureau), Andrew C. Johnston (University of California Merced) and Nolan G. Pope (University of Maryland) analyzed Census Bureau data, federal tax records and Social Security Administration information to determine the long-term impact of divorce on children.\r\n\r\nThey traced parental marital histories and connected them to household and child outcome data.\r\n\r\n*Continue reading [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/divorce-affects-children.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] *to learn more about:\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Divorce outcomes \r\n  * Divorce across the U.S. population \r\n  * Trends across time \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nStay Connected with the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nFollow us on our social media channels, Facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], LinkedIn [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Twitter/X [ https://x.com/uscensusbureau?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], and\xc2\xa0YouTube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], so you never miss an update.\r\n\r\nStay Connected With Us on Social Media [ https://www.census.gov/about/contact-us/social_media.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Follow Us* [ https://www.census.gov/about/contact-us/social_media.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nYou May Be Interested In\r\n\r\nU.S. Divorce Rates Down, Marriage Rates Stagnant From 2012-2022\r\n\r\nU.S. Divorce Rates Down, Marriage Rates Stagnant From 2012-2022 [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2024/10/marriage-and-divorce.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nWashington, D.C., had among the highest marriage rates in 2022 and Arkansas had among the highest divorce rates. Explore marriage and divorce rates by state with our data visualization.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2024/10/marriage-and-divorce.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout America Counts [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nAmerica Counts features stories on various topics including:\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Families [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FFamilies ],\xc2\xa0Housing [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FHousing ],\xc2\xa0Employment [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FEmployment ], Business and Economy [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2Fbusiness-economy ] \r\n  * Education [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FEducation ], [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FEducation ] Health [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FHealth ], Population [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FThePopulation ], Income and Poverty [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&visual-list-fb55843e87%3Afilters=Census%3ATopic%2FIncome-Poverty ] \r\n\r\n*For the Media:*\xc2\xa0Contact our\xc2\xa0Public Information Office [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/about.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0for inquiries or interviews.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nDon't miss an America Counts story! Use the links below to sign up [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/signup/19707 ] and update your preferences.\r\n\r\nSubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/signup/19707 ] | Manage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] | Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] | Help [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/s/?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*Share This * [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/405464a ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260120aco&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n"
