[2026-04-27 10:38:05] Raw text/plain payload: b"Register Today  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nNIST  \r\n \r\n\r\nView As Web Page [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/bulletins/4053d71 ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\nHeader  \r\n \r\n\r\nNIST Cybersecurity and Privacy Program\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nJoin the Next NIST Small Business Cybersecurity Community of Interest Call! Topic: The Intersection of Cybersecurity and Privacy\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nSMB COI  [ https://www.nist.gov/itl/smallbusinesscyber/join-community-interest ]\r\n\r\n*Date:* February 18, 2026\r\n\r\n*Time:* 2:00 p.m. - 3:00 p.m. EST\r\n\r\n*Description:* NIST's Small Business (SMB) Cybersecurity Community of Interest (COI) has been established to convene the public and private sectors to share business insights, expertise, challenges, and perspectives to guide our work and assist NIST in addressing the cybersecurity needs of the SMB community. NIST SMB Cybersecurity COI calls meet quarterly to present recent updates in the NIST SMB program, to engage in topical discussions, and to answer audience questions.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Agenda:*\r\n\r\n\r\n  * 2:00 p.m. - 2:10 p.m.: Welcome and NIST Small Business Cybersecurity Program updates \r\n  * 2:10 p.m. - 2:45 p.m.: Guest Speaker: Meghan Anderson, NIST Privacy Engineering Program \r\n  * This topic is based on feedback from prior COI calls, where members wanted to learn more about the intersection of cybersecurity and privacy. Though cybersecurity and privacy are distinct disciplines, they both can have overlapping and complementary objectives. Meghan Anderson from NIST\xe2\x80\x99s Privacy Engineering Program will join the call for the first 40 minutes to highlight recent updates to the NIST Privacy Framework, discuss the intersection of cybersecurity and privacy, and engage in Q&A. \r\n\r\n  * 2:45 p.m. - 3:00 p.m.: Discussion\xc2\xa0 \r\n\r\nRegister [ https://www.nist.gov/news-events/events/2026/02/nist-small-business-community-interest-quarterly-calls ]\r\n \r\n\r\n*NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy Program*\r\nQuestions and comments can be directed to: smallbizsecurity@nist.gov\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nConnect with us\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/NIST ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/NIST ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/NIST ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/nist ]flickr [ https://www.instagram.com/nist/ ]  \r\n\r\nReceived this email from a friend? Subscribe here [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/new?topic_id=USNIST_1 ].\r\n\r\n ITL NIST [ https://www.nist.gov/itl ] \r\n\r\nSubscriber services:\r\n\r\nManage Preferences [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIf you have questions or problems with the subscription service, please contact subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ].\r\nTechnical questions? Contact inquiries@nist.gov. (301) 975-NIST (6478).\r\n\r\nThis service is provided to you at no charge by National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST).\xc2\xa0100 Bureau Drive, Stop 1070\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7 Gaithersburg, MD 20899\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0301-975-6478\r\n\r\n GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n"
