[2026-04-27 10:38:06] Raw text/plain payload: b'NIST develops and sells more than 1,300 standard reference materials to support American industry.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nNIST  \r\n\r\nView as a Web Page [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/bulletins/4054891 ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nTaking Measure Blog\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNIST\xe2\x80\x99s Most Popular Reference Materials and What They Tell Us About the Science of Measurement\r\nA man in a bright orange sweatshirt stands at the open door of a large lab freezer. [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/nists-most-popular-reference-materials-and-what-they-tell-us-about-science ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nMeasurement, in its most basic form, is about comparing the thing you want to measure with a reference. To measure the length of a table, you compare it to a tape measure. To measure flour for a birthday cake, you compare it to a measuring cup. Better references mean better measurements.\r\n\r\nIf you\xe2\x80\x99re baking a cake, it doesn\xe2\x80\x99t matter much if your measuring cup is a little off, but sometimes millions of dollars or even people\xe2\x80\x99s lives depend on precise measurements.\r\n\r\nThat\xe2\x80\x99s why NIST develops and sells more than 1,300 standard reference materials (SRMs) that are critical for supporting American industry, enforcing laws and conducting research.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/nists-most-popular-reference-materials-and-what-they-tell-us-about-science ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nIN CASE YOU MISSED IT\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nMelissa Phillips, wearing safety glasses, poses leaning over an open chest freezer, holding a plastic bag of spinach.  [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/organic-vegetarian-or-carnivore-whatever-you-eat-my-lab-working-keep-it-safe ] \r\nOrganic, Vegetarian or Carnivore: Whatever You Eat, My Lab Is Working to Keep It Safe\r\n\r\n"May 18, 2023"\r\nThe levels of contaminants in our food supply are, generally, decreasing. That\xe2\x80\x99s the good news. But we still need to measure those contaminants and make sure our food is safe. And measuring tiny things (and big things) is what we do best here at NIST. \r\n\r\nRead More [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/organic-vegetarian-or-carnivore-whatever-you-eat-my-lab-working-keep-it-safe ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nConnect with us\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/NIST ]X [ https://twitter.com/NIST ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/NIST ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/nist ]flickr [ https://www.instagram.com/nist/ ]  \r\n\r\nReceived this email from a friend? Subscribe here [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/new?topic_id=USNIST_1 ].\r\n\r\n NIST [ https://www.nist.gov ] \r\n\r\nSubscriber services:\r\n\r\nManage Preferences [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIf you have questions or problems with the subscription service, please contact subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ].\r\nTechnical questions? Contact inquiries@nist.gov. (301) 975-NIST (6478).\r\n\r\nThis service is provided to you at no charge by National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST).\xc2\xa0100 Bureau Drive, Stop 1070\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7 Gaithersburg, MD 20899\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0301-975-6478\r\n\r\n GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
