[2026-04-27 10:38:11] Raw text/plain payload: b'If your email program has trouble displaying this email, view as a webpage [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/bulletins/4056bc3 ].\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nUS Food and Drug Administration\r\nFDA Takes Steps to Improve Gluten Ingredient Disclosure in Foods [ https://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-takes-steps-improve-gluten-ingredient-disclosure-foods?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nBookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/bulletins/4056bc3?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nToday, the U.S. Food and Drug Administration issued a\xc2\xa0Request for Information [ https://www.federalregister.gov/public-inspection/2026-01121/request-for-information-labeling-and-preventing-cross-contact-of-gluten-for-packaged-foods?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0(RFI) regarding labeling and preventing cross-contact of gluten in packaged food. The FDA is taking this action as a first step to improve transparency in disclosures of ingredients that impact certain health conditions, such as gluten for those with celiac disease, and other established food allergens.\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cToday, we advance the MAHA Strategy\xe2\x80\x99s directive by demanding radical transparency in packaged food ingredients that affect health conditions and diet-related allergies,\xe2\x80\x9d\xc2\xa0*Health and Human Services Secretary Robert Kennedy Jr. said.*\xc2\xa0\xe2\x80\x9cAmericans deserve clear, reliable information about what\xe2\x80\x99s in their food and how it\xe2\x80\x99s made. Public input calling for honest labeling will protect consumers, prevent harm, and Make America Healthy Again.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\nThe agency is seeking information on adverse reactions due to \xe2\x80\x9cingredients of interest\xe2\x80\x9d (i.e., non-wheat gluten containing grains (GCGs) which are rye and barley, and oats due to cross-contact with GCGs) and on labeling issues or concerns with identifying these \xe2\x80\x9cingredients of interest\xe2\x80\x9d on packaged food products in the U.S.\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cPeople with celiac disease or gluten sensitives have had to tiptoe around food, and are often forced to guess about their food options,\xe2\x80\x9d\xc2\xa0*said FDA Commissioner Marty Makary, M.D., M.P.H.*\xc2\xa0\xe2\x80\x9cWe encourage all stakeholders to share their experiences and data to help us develop policies that will better protect Americans and support healthy food choices.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\nThe agency has received a citizen petition on this matter and has reviewed available data and reports including the most recent reports by the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations expert consultation. The FDA\xe2\x80\x99s review of this information indicates that there are several serious data gaps limiting our ability to fully evaluate the public health importance of these ingredients which includes limited U.S. data on adverse reactions to the \xe2\x80\x9cingredients of interest.\xe2\x80\x9d \xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nThe FDA seeks detailed information such as the prevalence of products where rye or barley are not currently disclosed; information on the severity of and potency of immunoglobulin E-mediated food allergy to rye and barley; concerns around the gluten content of oats due to cross-contact and other questions related to these issues. \xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nThe FDA is taking this action to help enhance transparency for consumers and inform the agency\xe2\x80\x99s gluten-related labeling priorities and next steps. The FDA intends to use the information to support a determination on what type(s) of future regulatory actions we should take to better protect consumers with celiac disease.\r\n\r\nHow to Submit Comments\r\n\r\n*Electronic Submissions*\r\n\r\nComments can be submitted via the\xc2\xa0Federal eRulemaking Portal [ https://www.regulations.gov/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0to Docket No FDA-2023-P-3942 (open for 60 days).\r\n\r\nFollow the instructions for submitting comments. \xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Written Submissions*\r\n\r\nWritten comments may be mailed to:\r\nDockets Management Staff (HFA-305)\r\nFood and Drug Administration\r\n5630 Fishers Lane, Rm. 1061\r\nRockville, MD 20852\r\n\r\n"Please ensure that all comments include Docket No. FDA-2023-P-3942. Confidential submissions should be appropriately marked."\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nfeed [ https://www.fda.gov/about-fda/contact-fda/subscribe-podcasts-and-news-feeds?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://www.twitter.com/US_FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/USFoodandDrugAdmin?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]flickr [ https://www.flickr.com/photos/fdaphotos/albums/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\n*Manage Subscriptions* [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 *Unsubscribe All* [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.ee0243ee8741fe358146537aecf40e1e&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 *Help* [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} td {line-height:1;} \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: U.S. Food and Drug Administration \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\r\n10903 New Hampshire Ave\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0Silver Spring, MD \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0 20993-0002\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa01-888-INFO-FDA GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
