[2026-04-27 10:40:18] Raw text/plain payload: b'As a valued partner and stakeholder, this newsletter is designed to keep you informed and engaged.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/partners.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nJanuary 2026 Issue\r\n\r\nAs a valued U.S. Census Bureau partner and stakeholder, this newsletter is designed to keep you informed and engaged.\r\n\r\nGray Divider\r\nJarmin blog: Revolutionizing Economic Measurement at the Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/blogs/deputy-director/2026/01/revolutionizing-economic-measurement.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nI recently had the privilege of speaking at conferences honoring two economists who\xe2\x80\x99ve made huge contributions to the profession and, most importantly for this blog, to the U.S. Census Bureau.\r\n\r\nMark Roberts of Penn State University and John Haltiwanger of the University of Maryland and their colleagues used Census Bureau data to change how economists and policymakers view the economy and how the Census Bureau measures it.\r\n\r\nBeyond their scientific contributions, both Mark and John have served the Census Bureau in a variety of roles.\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/blogs/deputy-director/2026/01/revolutionizing-economic-measurement.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nAmerica Counts: Exploring New Frontiers With the Quarterly Workforce Indicators [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/space-economy.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nThe \xe2\x80\x9cspace economy\xe2\x80\x9d continues to soar and younger workers are fueling the industry\xe2\x80\x99s upward trajectory.\r\n\r\nThe extraterrestrial industry accounted for $142.5 billion (0.5%) of U.S. GDP\xc2\xa0in 2023, combining activities from the Manufacturing, Transportation, and Information sectors, including\xc2\xa0Satellite Telecommunications and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing.\r\n\r\nThe Census Bureau recently released the first ever Quarterly Workforce Indicators (QWI) at the national industry level. These data will allow users to view and download economic indicators such as employment, job creation, earnings and other measures of employment flows for six-digit North American Industry Classification System codes.\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/space-economy.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nOTM_2023 [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2025/onthemap-update.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nOnTheMap Updated With 2023 Employment Data\r\n\r\nThe Census Bureau has updated the Longitudinal Employer-Household Dynamics (LEHD) Origin-Destination Employment Statistics (LODES) and the OnTheMap application to include:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * 2023 employment data \r\n  * Backfilled data for Mississippi from 2019 to 2022 \r\n  * Updated geography to the 2024 TIGER/Line vintage \r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2025/onthemap-update.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n?? America Counts\r\n\r\nAmerica Counts: Economic Census Highlights Variety of Products Many Industries Sell [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/napcs-economic-census.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nImagine you\xe2\x80\x99re an entrepreneur looking to establish a pet supply business.\r\n\r\nBefore setting up shop, you need to assess, among other things, the need and potential customer base \xe2\x80\x93 and size up the competition.\r\n\r\nThat means exploring such things as the number of establishments \xe2\x80\x93 grocery stores, retail outlets, convenience stores and the like \xe2\x80\x93 that sell pet food in your state as well as their revenue and employee count.\r\n\r\nA good place to start your search: the latest\xc2\xa02022 Economic Census Product Statistics\xc2\xa0tables\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/napcs-economic-census.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nMore from America Counts\r\n\r\nAmerica Counts: The Stories Behind Census Bureau Numbers in 2025 [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2025/12/2025-year-in-review.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nThe Stories Behind Census Bureau Numbers in 2025 [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2025/12/2025-year-in-review.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nRevenue and Employment Trends Reveal Shifts in U.S. Economy [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2025/12/economic-census-5-year-look.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nComing Soon: 2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-Year Estimates\r\n\r\nThe Census Bureau is scheduled to release new 2020-2024 American Community Survey (ACS) 5-year estimates on January 29.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nThe ACS provides statistics about the nation\xe2\x80\x99s people and housing, such as language spoken at home, education, commuting, employment, mortgage/rent status, income, poverty and health insurance coverage. It is the only source of local statistics for most of the 40-plus topics it covers.\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-kits/2026/acs-5-year-estimates.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nOther Recent Releases\r\n\r\n2024 Planning Database and New 2020 Census Operational Data [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2024-planning-database.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n2024 State-to-State Migration Flows Statistics [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2024-state-to-state-migration.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*Releases* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout Census Partnerships\r\n\r\nFrom corporations to policymakers, foundations and non-profits to software developers, the U.S. Census Bureau partners across sectors and industries to help America work better through data. Together we harness the power of our data, support each other\xe2\x80\x99s missions, and co-create solutions to increase data use and participation in Census Bureau surveys and programs.\r\n\r\nConnect with the Census Bureau partnerships team at\xc2\xa0census.partners@census.gov\xc2\xa0to learn more.\r\n\r\nSubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/signup/34555 ] | Manage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] | Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] | Help [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/s/?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*Share This * [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/405c888 ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n*Stay connected with us!*\r\n\r\nJoin the conversation on social media.\r\n\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nSubscriber Settings [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Remove me from All Subscriptions  [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n&lt;!-- /* template top padding on mobile */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { table#flexible-abe-main-table { padding:0 !important; } } --&gt; ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260123cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
