[2026-04-27 10:40:22] Raw text/plain payload: b"Bookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/bulletins/405c447?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nIRS.gov Banner \r\n\r\nIRS Newswire\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nJanuary 23, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nIssue Number: \xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0IR-2026-10\r\n\r\nInside This Issue\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*Treasury, IRS** issue FAQs to address the new deduction for qualified overtime compensation under the One, Big, Beautiful Bill*\r\n\r\nIR-2026-10, Jan. 23, 2026\r\n\r\nWASHINGTON \xe2\x80\x93 The Department of the Treasury and the Internal Revenue Service today issued frequently asked questions in Fact Sheet 2026-01 [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/questions-and-answers-about-the-new-deduction-for-qualified-overtime-compensation ] related to the new deduction for qualified overtime compensation under the One, Big, Beautiful Bill.\r\n\r\nFor tax years 2025 through 2028, individuals who receive qualified overtime compensation may deduct the amount that exceeds their regular rate of pay (generally, the \xe2\x80\x9chalf\xe2\x80\x9d portion of \xe2\x80\x9ctime-and-a-half\xe2\x80\x9d compensation) and is reported on a Form W-2 or Form 1099.\r\n\r\nThese FAQs contain additional information about the deduction, provide resources for employees (including federal employees) to assist them in determining whether they received qualified overtime compensation under the Fair Labor Standards Act, and contain useful information regarding the differences in reporting requirements for tax year 2025 and 2026-2028.\r\n\r\nTreasury and IRS previously issued Notice 2025-62 [ https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-drop/n-25-62.pdf ] providing penalty relief [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/treasury-irs-provide-penalty-relief-for-tax-year-2025-for-information-reporting-on-tips-and-overtime-under-the-one-big-beautiful-bill ] to employers and other payers for tax year 2025 regarding new information reporting requirements for qualified overtime compensation; and issued Notice 2025-69 [ https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-drop/n-25-69.pdf ] for workers eligible to claim the deduction [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/treasury-irs-provide-guidance-for-individuals-who-received-tips-or-overtime-during-tax-year-2025 ] for overtime compensation for tax year 2025.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nFor more information, see One, Big, Beautiful Bill Provisions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/one-big-beautiful-bill-provisions ] on IRS.gov.\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ] \xc2\xa0Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ] \xc2\xa0LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to the IRS Newswire, an IRS e-mail service.\r\n\r\nIf you know someone who might want to subscribe to this mailing list, please forward this message to them so they can subscribe [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ].\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically from the mailing list IRS Newswire. *Please Do Not Reply To This Message.*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNews Essentials\r\n\r\nWhat's Hot [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/whats-hot ]\r\n\r\nNews Releases [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\nIRS - The Basics [ https://www.irs.gov/about-irs/irs-the-basics ]\r\n\r\nIRS Guidance [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/understanding-irs-guidance-a-brief-primer ]\r\n\r\nMedia Contacts [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-media-relations-office-contact-number ]\r\n\r\nFacts & Figures [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nAround The Nation [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/around-the-nation ]\r\