[2026-04-27 10:40:25] Raw text/plain payload: b'Putting you in control  ssa.gov\r\n\r\nThe following program policy instructions were updated on 01/21/2026.\r\n\r\n*_Program Operations Manual System_*__ [ https://secure.ssa.gov/apps10/reference.nsf/lnx/01202026080137PM?opendocument=&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] __ *_DI 52755 TN 4_* [ https://secure.ssa.gov/apps10/reference.nsf/lnx/01202026080137PM?opendocument=&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\xc2\xa0- Chavez Acquiescence Ruling (AR)*\r\nSummary: This section describes necessary Field Office actions for claims falling within the purview of the Chavez AR. It instructs FO employees to obtain information from the OHAQ. This query was retired in or at the end of the 2024 fiscal year. Therefore, this section is out of date.\r\n\r\n*_DI 29505 TN 4_* [ https://secure.ssa.gov/apps10/reference.nsf/lnx/01202026080126PM?opendocument=&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\xc2\xa0- Other Special Assistance Requests*\r\nSummary: The DDS has always had jurisdiction for getting consultative examination on Railroad (RR) claims. Due to fiscal processing limitations, the Federal Disability Determination Division Chicago (FDDD) is no longer able to pay for MER requests for RRB Dual Eligibility (D/E) claims. As a result, we need to reach out to the local DDS via an assistance request for that DDS to request and pay for MER. When using our prior legacy system we only reached out to the local DDS to request and pay for CEs. This process and POMS update only applies to RRB D/E claims. The local DDS does not adjudicate the claim. \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n [ # ] \r\n\r\n [ # ]\r\n\r\n [ # ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nStay Connected with Social Security:\r\n\r\n \xc2\xa0 Like us on Facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/socialsecurity?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] Find us on X [ https://twitter.com/socialsecurity?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] Watch us on Youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/socialsecurityonline?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/socialsecurity/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] Social Security Matters Blog [ http://blog.ssa.gov?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] Govdelivery [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USSSA/subscriber/new ] \xc2\xa0 \r\n\r\nJoin the millions and discover your benefits!\r\nOpen a my Social Security [ http://www.socialsecurity.gov/myaccount/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] account.\r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\nManage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USSSA/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0Unsubscribe All [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USSSA/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.26af423df56cba5a19f63c28ecad2176&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com by the Social Security Administration, and was produced and disseminated at U.S. taxpayer expense. GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;}\r\n'
