[2026-04-27 10:40:26] Raw text/plain payload: b'Census Bureau Upcoming and Recently Released Products  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/tip-sheets/2026/tp26-02.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nTip Sheet (TP26-02)\r\n\r\n*Upcoming\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0 *\r\n\r\n*Online Product Calendar* \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau provides anticipated release dates for its regular and recurring statistical products through its online product calendar [ https://www.census.gov/about/event-calendar.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]. This calendar is regularly updated to reflect the most current information.\r\n\r\n*2024 Community Resilience Estimates *\xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau will release new community resilience estimates by social vulnerability to natural disasters. This product helps local governments and community stakeholders plan mitigation and recovery strategies in the event of a disaster. Estimates will be released for the nation, states, counties, core-based statistical areas and tracts. (Scheduled for release Jan. 29.)\r\n\r\n*American Community Survey*\r\n\r\n*2020-2024 American Community Survey\xc2\xa0*\xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau will release the remaining 2024 American Community Survey (ACS) estimates in the coming months. The next data release is Jan. 29, and will include the 2020-2024 ACS 5-year estimates and\xc2\xa05-year Variance Replicate Estimates. The 5-year estimates will be available to embargo subscribers Jan. 27. The last release of 2020-2024 ACS 5-year PUMS (Public Use Microdata Sample) files is set for March 5. The updated\xc2\xa0release schedule [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/news/data-releases/2024/release-schedule.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0is available online.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/tip-sheets/2026/tp26-02.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n*Demographic**\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*New Data Tables on Characteristics of Same-Sex Couple Households *\xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau will release new data tables from the 2024 American Community Survey 1-year estimates on Characteristics of Same-Sex Couple Households: 2005 to Present. The annual release explores demographic and economic characteristics of Same-sex Couple Households by age, race, ethnicity, educational attainment, employment status, income and home tenure. (Scheduled for release Jan. 26.)*\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*Energy and Rental Assistance Fact Sheet *\xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau will release a new fact sheet on energy and rental assistance based on data from the Survey of Income and Program Participation (SIPP). SIPP is a nationally representative longitudinal survey that provides comprehensive information on the dynamics of income, employment, household composition and government program participation. The fact sheet provides a quick and easy way to get statistics on recipients of energy and rental assistance for calendar year 2023. (Scheduled for release Jan. 26.)\r\n\r\n*Child Support Received Fact Sheet\xc2\xa0*\xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau will release a new fact sheet on child support received based on data from the Survey of Income and Program Participation (SIPP). SIPP is a nationally representative longitudinal survey that provides comprehensive information on the dynamics of income, employment, household composition and government program participation. The fact sheet provides a quick and easy way to get statistics on parents who received child support in calendar year 2023. (Scheduled for release Jan. 26.)\r\n\r\n*Small Area Income and Poverty Estimates for States, Counties and School Districts *\xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau will release new data on small area income and poverty estimates for states, counties and school districts. The new data come from the 2024\xc2\xa0Small Area Income and Poverty Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/saipe.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0(SAIPE), which provides the only up-to-date, single-year income and poverty statistics for the nation\xe2\x80\x99s 3,143\xc2\xa0counties and 13,126\xc2\xa0school districts. (Scheduled for release Jan. 27.)\r\n\r\n*Vintage 2025\xc2\xa0Population Estimates, Components of Change\xc2\xa0and Voting-Age Population for the Nation, States\xc2\xa0and Puerto Rico\xc2\xa0*\xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau will release July 1, 2025, estimates of total population and voting-age population for the nation, states and Puerto Rico, as well as corresponding annual estimates and components of change since the 2020 Census.\xc2\xa0(Scheduled for release Jan. 27.)\r\n\r\n*Social and Economic Characteristics of Currently Unmarried Women With a Recent Birth: 2023 *\xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau will release a new report that explores social and economic characteristics of unmarried women who gave birth in 2023. The report uses American Community Survey [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (ACS) data and makes comparisons, when possible, to an earlier report [ https://www2.census.gov/library/publications/2013/acs/acs-21.pdf?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] that used 2011 ACS 1-year estimates. (Scheduled for release Jan. 28.)\r\n\r\n*2024 Rental Housing Finance Survey *\xe2\x80\x94 The U. S. Census Bureau and the Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) will release the 2024 Rental Housing Finance Survey (RHFS) summary tables in the RHFS Table Creator, public use files and codebook on census.gov. The RHFS Table Creator is an interactive data tool that allows users to create custom tables of financial, mortgage, and property characteristics of single-family and multifamily residential properties for rent in the United States. Data available include property, residential structure(s), mortgage characteristics, ownership status, commercial use of space, benefits received and more. Visit Data [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/rhfs/data.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/rhfs/data/puf.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]for the latest RHFS data and Rental Housing Finance Survey (RHFS) [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/rhfs.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] for more information about the survey. (Scheduled for release Feb. 19.)\r\n\r\n*Economic*\r\n\r\n*New Post-Secondary Employment Outcomes Data *\xe2\x80\x94\xc2\xa0The U.S. Census Bureau will release new data on outcomes of graduates. PSEO\xc2\xa0tabulations [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/data/pseo_experimental.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0show earnings and employment outcomes for graduates of U.S. post-secondary institutions and are generated by linking graduate transcript records to Longitudinal Employer-Household Dynamics\xc2\xa0 [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]wage data. This offers prospective students a comprehensive assessment tool to find out how much they could potentially earn by degree and institution.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau conducts the PSEO\xc2\xa0in cooperation with higher education institutional systems to examine college degree attainment and graduate earnings. (Scheduled for release Feb. 12.)\r\n\r\n*Call for Presentations for the 2026 Local Employment Dynamics (LED) Partnership Virtual Workshop* \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau invites you to submit a proposal to*\xc2\xa0*present virtually at the 2026 LED Partnership Hybrid Workshop on May 12-13, 2026. This year\xe2\x80\x99s theme is"\xc2\xa0\xe2\x80\x9cNumbers to Narratives: Data for Better Decisions.\xe2\x80\x9d"\xc2\xa0The event will highlight the useful applications of data made possible through the LED State/Federal partnership including\xc2\xa0the Quarterly Workforce Indicators (QWI), the Longitudinal Employer-Household Dynamics (LEHD) Origin-Destination Employee Statistics (LODES), OnTheMap or OnTheMap for Emergency Management, Job-to-Job Flows (J2J), Post-Secondary Employment Outcomes (PSEO) and Veteran Employment Outcomes (VEO). Please visit\xc2\xa0LEHD [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0for proposal guidance. Additional details will be posted when available. Information on previous workshops can be found at\xc2\xa0Workshops and Webinars - Longitudinal Employer-Household Dynamics [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/workshops_webinars/?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\xc2\xa0Please email\xc2\xa0CES.Local.Employment.Dynamics@census.gov\xc2\xa0for questions about the workshop. (Deadline to submit proposal: Feb. 18.)\r\n\r\n*\xe2\x80\x9cUnlocking NAICS 5- and 6-Digit Details in the Quarterly Workforce Indicators (QWI) Data Set [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/2026/unlocking-naics-5-6-digit-details.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xe2\x80\x9d*\xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau and the Local Employment Dynamics (LED) Partnership in collaboration with the Council for Community and Economic Research (C2ER) and the Labor Market Information (LMI) Institute, welcomes Andrew Foote as he presents, \xe2\x80\x9cUnlocking NAICS 5- and 6- Digit Details in the Quarterly Workforce Indicators (QWI).\xe2\x80\x9d This presentation will introduce the newly released North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) 5- and 6- digit QWI tabulations and the available demographic and firm level crossings, including sex, age, race and ethnicity, education, firm age, and firm size at the state level. (Feb. 18.)\r\n\r\n*Business Trends and Outlook Survey* [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/btos.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x94 The Business Trends and Outlook Survey (BTOS) measures business conditions on an ongoing basis. BTOS experimental data products are representative of all employer businesses other than farms in the U.S. economy. The data allow greater insight into the state of the economy by providing continuous, timely information for key economic measures. Data are released biweekly and are available by sector, state, employment size and the 25 most populous metropolitan statistical areas. New questions on artificial intelligence were added Nov. 17 and will be released in 2026.\r\n\r\n*Federal Register Notices*\r\n\r\nThe U.S. Census Bureau publishes updates in the Federal Register to keep the public informed about surveys, censuses and related activities. Some notices include a comment period during which the public can provide feedback. For more information on Census Bureau Federal Register notices (FRNs), check out Collections of Information and Federal Register Notices [ https://www.census.gov/about/policies/collections.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\r\n\r\nCurrent FRNs include:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Generic Clearance for Questionnaire Pretesting Research [ https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/12/30/2025-23979/agency-information-collection-activities-submission-to-the-office-of-management-and-budget-omb-for?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0(Comment period ends Jan. 29). \r\n  * National Survey of Children\xe2\x80\x99s Health [ https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/12/05/2025-22134/agency-information-collection-activities-submission-to-the-office-of-management-and-budget-omb-for?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0(Comment period ends Feb. 3). \r\n  * American Community Survey and Puerto Rico Community Survey [ https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/12/19/2025-23329/agency-information-collection-activities-submission-to-the-office-of-management-and-budget-omb-for?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0(Comment period ends Feb. 17). \r\n  * Annual Integrated Economic Survey [ https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/01/20/2026-00924/agency-information-collection-activities-submission-to-the-office-of-management-and-budget-omb-for?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (Comment period ends Feb. 19).*\xc2\xa0* \r\n\r\n*Recently Released*\r\n\r\n*(Released since Jan. 9, 2026)**\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*2024 Planning Database* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2024-planning-database.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 22 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released the 2024 Planning Database (PDB), which includes the Low Response Score (LRS) and other new 2020 Census operational data. The 2024 PDB contains a selection of housing, demographic, socioeconomic and operational data for block groups and census tracts from the 2020 Census Redistricting Data (Public Law 94-171) Summary File, 2020 Census Demographic and Housing Characteristics File, and 2018-2022 American Community Survey 5-year estimates.*\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*Demographic**\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*State-to-State Migration Flows Table Package* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2024-state-to-state-migration.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 21 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released the latest version of the State-to-State Migration Flows table package. Tables come from the 2024\xc2\xa0American Community Survey 1-year estimates. The\xc2\xa0State-to-State Migration Flows [ https://www.census.gov/data/tables/time-series/demo/geographic-mobility/state-to-state-migration.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0table provides estimates of the number of people moving between origin and destination geographies.\xc2\xa0The\xc2\xa0State of Residence by Place of Birth [ https://www.census.gov/data/tables/time-series/demo/geographic-mobility/state-of-residence-place-of-birth-acs.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0table provide estimates of the number of people living in their current state of residence by place of birth.*\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*Webinar on Methodology Updates for the Vintage 2025 Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-kits/2026/acs-5-year-estimates.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] *\xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 20 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau held a webinar [ https://www2.census.gov/about/training-workshops/2026/2026-01-22-2020-2024-acs-5-year-prerelease-presentation.pdf?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] on methodology updates for the Vintage 2025\xc2\xa0estimates. The Population Estimates Program (PEP) develops the official estimates of population and housing units for the Census Bureau. Every year, PEP builds a time series of estimates that starts at the date of the most recent decennial census and extends through the vintage year, which represents the latest year of estimates available. Learn more about the population estimates, particularly how the estimates methodology has been updated for the forthcoming Vintage 2025\xc2\xa0estimates series, at this webinar.\r\n\r\n*Economic**\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*Release of Expanded NAICS Industry Tabulations in the QWI*\xc2\xa0 [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/data/?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#qwi ]\xe2\x80\x94\xc2\xa0Jan. 13 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released NAICS\xc2\xa05- and 6-digit tabulations\xc2\xa0for the\xc2\xa0Quarterly Workforce Indicators\xc2\xa0(QWI) [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/data/?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#qwi ]\xc2\xa0data product. These new state-level tabulations provide the ability to analyze the inner workings of our economy in unprecedented industry detail. An analysis of these new data are available in an America Counts [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/space-economy.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] story. Please send questions and comments to\xc2\xa0CES.QWI.Feedback@census.gov. <CES.QWI.Feedback@census.gov>\xc2\xa0*\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*America Counts: Stories Behind the Numbers**\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*America Counts* [ https://www.census.gov/AmericaCounts?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] tells the stories behind the numbers in a new and inviting way. We feature stories on various topics such as families, housing, employment, business, education, the economy, emergency preparedness and the population.\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Who Are the Inventors and Firms That Generate the Most Patents? [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/inventors-and-patents.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (Jan. 22) \r\n  * The Long-Term Effects of Divorce on Children [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/divorce-affects-children.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (Jan. 20) \r\n  * Exploring New Frontiers With the Quarterly Workforce Indicators [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/space-economy.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (Jan. 13) \r\n\r\n*Stats for Stories**\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*Stats for Stories* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] provides links to timely story ideas highlighting the U.S. Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s newsworthy statistics that relate to current events, observances, holidays and anniversaries. The story ideas are intended to assist the media in story mining and producing content for their respective audiences.\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Small Business Saturday: Nov. 29, 2025 [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/stories/small-business-saturday.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Blogs*\r\n\r\n*Annual Updates to the Data and Methodology for Population Estimates* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/blogs/random-samplings/2026/01/updates-data-methodology-population-estimates.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 15 \xe2\x80\x94 Written by: Eric Jensen, Senior Research Scientist for Population Estimates and Coverage Measurement, Population Division; Christine Hartley, Assistant Division Chief for Estimates and Projections, Population Division \xe2\x80\x94 Each year, the population of the United States grows and evolves. Births, deaths and migration are the three components of population change. A myriad of factors can affect the magnitude and speed of the changes. For example, economic uncertainty can affect attitudes toward fertility and mobility, a global pandemic can cause mortality to spike and policy changes can shape the number of people moving in or out of the country.\r\n\r\n*Resources**\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*Emergency Management/Disaster Resources* \xe2\x80\x94 When major disasters strike, visit our Emergency Management webpage [ https://www.census.gov/topics/preparedness.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] for demographic and economic data on impacted areas. Each disaster will include data from our key emergency management tools: OnTheMap for Emergency Management, Community Resilience Estimates, Census Business Builder: Regional Analyst Edition and other useful resources.\r\n\r\n*Learn What Surveys Are Being Conducted in Your Community* \xe2\x80\x94 Discover which of the U.S. Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s annual surveys [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/surveyhelp.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] are being conducted in your community [ http://www.census.gov/regions/?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]. In a variety of surveys and censuses, evolving from the first census in 1790 [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/decennial-census/decade/1790/about-1790.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], the Census Bureau provides official information about America\xe2\x80\x99s people, businesses, industries and institutions. Learn more about surveys currently being conducted in each Census Bureau region:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Atlanta [ https://www.census.gov/about/regions/atlanta/surveys-programs.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * Chicago [ https://www.census.gov/about/regions/chicago/surveys-programs.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * Denver [ https://www.census.gov/about/regions/denver/surveys-programs.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * Los Angeles [ https://www.census.gov/about/regions/los-angeles/surveys-programs.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * New York [ https://www.census.gov/about/regions/new-york/surveys-programs.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * Philadelphia [ https://www.census.gov/about/regions/philadelphia/surveys-programs.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * All Surveys [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/surveyhelp/list-of-surveys.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Data Tools*\r\n\r\nThe U.S. Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s interactive applications used to access statistics from our 130-plus annual surveys and programs. A complete list can be accessed on the Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s Data Tools and Apps [ https://www.census.gov/data/data-tools.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] webpage.\r\n\r\n*Training Opportunities*\r\n\r\n*U.S. Census Bureau Training Opportunities* \xe2\x80\x94 Webinars are available on a regular basis to help the public access and use Census Bureau statistics. These free sessions, which are 60 to 90 minutes each, show users how to navigate Census Bureau databases and mapping tools and find demographic and economic statistics at the local or national level. Descriptions of upcoming sessions are available on our Census Academy [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/upcoming.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] webpage. Login details are provided at least one week before a webinar.\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Essential Skills for Finding ACS Data on data.census.gov [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/upcoming.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (Tuesday, Jan. 27, 2-3 p.m. ET) \r\n\r\n  * Introduction to the ACS Public Use Microdata Sample (PUMS) Files [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/upcoming.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (Wednesday, Feb. 25, 2-3 p.m. ET) \r\n\r\n*Archived Training Resources* \xe2\x80\x94 Visit the U.S. Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s Educational Resource Library [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] for previously recorded, free training available at your convenience. The library includes presentations, recorded webinars, tutorials and other helpful materials.\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHelp us spread the word about Census Bureau data!\r\n\r\nShare this on social media or forward it to a friend.\r\n\r\n*Share This* [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/405c446 ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nWe serve as the nation\xe2\x80\x99s leading provider of quality data about its people and economy.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau is the federal government\'s largest statistical agency. As the world\xe2\x80\x99s premier statistical agency, we are dedicated to making our nation a better place. Policy-makers, businesses, and the public use our data to make informed decisions.\r\n\r\nResources for Media\r\n\r\nFor media interviews, please contact the\xc2\xa0Public Information Office [ https://lnks.gd/l/eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..p-5wpj2DTx0_qgyLiv6JuMTDOF_vZlHcwFpt971jIDs/s/866068797/br/124287751808-l?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Toll Free at 877-861-2010, 301-763-3030, or\xc2\xa0pio@census.gov.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n*Stay connected with us!*\r\n\r\nJoin the conversation on social media.\r\n\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nSubscriber Settings [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Remove me from All Subscriptions  [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n&lt;!-- /* template top padding on mobile */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { table#flexible-abe-main-table { padding:0 !important; } } --&gt; ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260123pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
