[2026-04-27 10:40:36] Raw text/plain payload: b'Bookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/bulletins/405d007?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nIRS.gov Banner \r\n\r\nIRS Newswire\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nJanuary 23, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n [ #Fifteenth ] \r\n\r\nIssue Number: \xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0IR-2026-11\r\n\r\nInside This Issue\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*IRS joins national partners to launch EITC Awareness Day*\r\n\r\nIR-2026-11, Jan. 23, 2026\r\n\r\nWASHINGTON \xe2\x80\x94 The Internal Revenue Service and partners nationwide today launched the annual Earned Income Tax Credit Awareness Day [ https://www.irs.gov/tax-professionals/eitc-central/eitc-awareness-day ] outreach campaign to help millions of eligible low-to- moderate-income, working Americans claim the Earned Income Tax Credit [ https://www.irs.gov/credits-deductions/individuals/earned-income-tax-credit-eitc ].\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cThe Earned Income Tax Credit is vital to supporting working American families and rewarding them for their hard work,\xe2\x80\x9d said IRS Chief Executive Officer Frank J. Bisignano. \xe2\x80\x9cThe IRS encourages every taxpayer who qualifies for the credit to claim the full amount they are due under the Internal Revenue Code.\xe2\x80\x9d\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nFor the past 20 years, the IRS has invited community organizations, elected officials, state and local governments, schools, employers, and other interested parties to join this national grassroots effort. This year, IRS leaders and partners across the nation are participating in local events highlighting the importance of the EITC, which helps millions of taxpayers each year.\r\n\r\nIn total, 23.5 million workers and families benefited from approximately $68.5 billion in EITC payments nationwide. The average EITC amount received nationwide for tax year 2024 was $2,916. \r\n\r\nThe IRS estimates that about one in five EITC-eligible taxpayers don\xe2\x80\x99t claim this valuable credit, underscoring the importance of the annual EITC Awareness Day outreach campaign.\r\n\r\nThe IRS encourages workers to use the EITC Assistant [ https://www.irs.gov/credits-deductions/individuals/earned-income-tax-credit/use-the-eitc-assistant ] to check eligibility or to visit the\xc2\xa0child-related tax benefits comparison [ https://www.eitc.irs.gov/eitc-central/child-related-tax-benefits-comparison/child-related-tax-benefits-comparison ]"\xc2\xa0"for basic eligibility rules.\r\n\r\nTo get the EITC, workers must file a tax return and claim the credit. The IRS also reminds taxpayers that the quickest way to get a tax refund is to file an accurate tax return electronically [ https://www.irs.gov/filing/individuals/how-to-file ] and choose direct deposit [ https://www.irs.gov/refunds/get-your-refund-faster-tell-irs-to-direct-deposit-your-refund-to-one-two-or-three-accounts ].\r\n\r\n*When to expect EITC refunds*\r\n\r\nThe IRS expects most early Earned Income Tax Credit or Additional Child Tax Credit refunds to be available in taxpayer bank accounts or debit card by March 2, 2026, if they choose direct deposit and there are no other issues with the return. Some taxpayers may have access to their refunds sooner depending on their financial institution\xe2\x80\x99s process. Where\xe2\x80\x99s My Refund? [ https://www.irs.gov/wheres-my-refund ] will be updated with projected deposit dates for most early EITC/ACTC refund filers by Feb. 21, 2026.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ] \xc2\xa0Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ] \xc2\xa0LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to the IRS Newswire, an IRS e-mail service.\r\n\r\nIf you know someone who might want to subscribe to this mailing list, please forward this message to them so they can subscribe [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ].\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically from the mailing list IRS Newswire. *Please Do Not Reply To This Message.*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNews Essentials\r\n\r\nWhat\'s Hot [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/whats-hot ]\r\n\r\nNews Releases [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\nIRS - The Basics [ https://www.irs.gov/about-irs/irs-the-basics ]\r\n\r\nIRS Guidance [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/understanding-irs-guidance-a-brief-primer ]\r\n\r\nMedia Contacts [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-media-relations-office-contact-number ]\r\n\r\nFacts & Figures [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nAround The Nation [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/around-the-nation ]\r\n\r\ne-News Subscriptions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe Newsroom Topics\r\n\r\nMultimedia Center [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/multimedia-center ]\r\n\r\nNoticias en Espa\xc3\xb1ol [ https://www.irs.gov/es/spanish/noticias-en-espanol ]\r\n\r\nRadio PSAs [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-radio-psas ]\r\n\r\nTax Scams [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-scams-consumer-alerts ]\r\n\r\nThe Tax Gap [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/the-tax-gap ]\r\n\r\nFact Sheets [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nIRS Tax Tips [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-tax-tips ]\r\n\r\nArmed Forces [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-information-for-members-of-the-us-armed-forces ]\r\n\r\nLatest News Home [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIRS Resources\r\n\r\nContact My Local