 Range, 300 Iven Ave\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Skateboarding Spring Clinic with Ramp up!* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30297&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n*Sundays, April 19- May 24\r\n*Beginner (Ages 5-10), 8:30- 9:30 AM\r\nSkate Club (Ages 6-12), 9:45- 10:45 AM\r\nRadnor Skatepark, 301 Iven Avenue\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn more about these programs!* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/default.aspx?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nADULT & SENIOR PROGRAMS\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nad [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30271&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Men\'s Winter Pick Up Basketball [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30286&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n*Mondays, December 1- March 9*\r\n*8:00 PM- 10:00 PM\r\nAges: 18+\r\nRadnor Activity Center\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Indoor Open-Play Pickleball- Winter & Spring 2026 [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30292&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n*Mondays, Tuesdays, Thursdays, Saturdays\r\nJanuary 5- April 2\r\nAges: 18+\r\nRadnor Activity Center\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Radnor Steps  [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30075&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n*Every Friday on the Radnor Trail\r\nAll ages\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Winter Indoor Tennis with Pamela Rende [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30290&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\r\nSundays, Sundays, January 25- March 22*\r\n*Session for Adult and Teens from 7-8:00 PM\r\nRadnor Racquet Club, 175 King of Prussia Road\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Pickleball Clinics with Universal Rackets [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30256&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\r\n*Indoor Winter 1*: January 16th- February 13th\r\n*Indoor Winter 2:* February 20th- March 20th\r\nRadnor Activity Center\r\nAges 18+\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn more about these programs!* [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/default.aspx?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHealth & Wellness\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHello Winter\r\n\r\nThis section includes winter wellness tips.\r\n\r\nClock \r\n\r\nRegulating Your Circadian Rhythm in the Winter\r\n\r\nWinter has a sneaky way of throwing our internal clocks completely off. Shorter days, longer nights, and less sunlight can confuse your *circadian rhythm*\xe2\x80\x94the internal system that tells your body when to sleep, wake, and feel alert. If you\xe2\x80\x99ve been feeling groggier, moodier, or wide awake at midnight, you\xe2\x80\x99re not alone.\r\n\r\nThe biggest culprit is light (or the lack of it). Our circadian rhythm is heavily regulated by natural sunlight, so when mornings are dark and evenings arrive early, the body struggles to stay in sync. One of the simplest fixes is *getting light as early as possible*. Open your curtains right when you wake up, step outside for a short walk, or consider using a light therapy lamp if mornings are especially dark where you live.\r\n\r\nConsistency also matters more in winter than ever. Try to *wake up and go to bed at the same time every day*, even on weekends. Sleeping in might feel tempting, but it can actually make your rhythm drift further off course. Think of your schedule as an anchor\xe2\x80\x94it keeps your body steady when the environment changes.\r\n\r\nMovement helps too. Gentle morning exercise can signal to your body that the day has started, while calming evening routines\xe2\x80\x94like reading, stretching, or dimming lights\xe2\x80\x94help cue sleep. Avoid bright screens late at night if you can; blue light tells your brain it\xe2\x80\x99s still daytime, which is the last message you want before bed.\r\n\r\nFinally, be kind to yourself. Winter is naturally slower, and your body may need a little extra rest. Regulating your circadian rhythm isn\xe2\x80\x99t about forcing productivity\xe2\x80\x94it\xe2\x80\x99s about working "with" your biology so you feel more balanced, energized, and human during the darker months.\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*NAMI Mainline PA* [ https://namimainlinepa.org/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nWhether you\xe2\x80\x99re thriving, surviving, or somewhere in between \xe2\x80\x94 your feelings are valid, and you are not alone. NAMI Mainline PA is an affiliate of the National Alliance on Mental Illness and provides information and support to people with mental illness, their families and friends. All of their services are FREE of Charge. Contact Lisa Parker at lisa@namimainlinepa.org or 267-251-6240 for more information.\r\n\r\n  Nami \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n2026 Board Meetings\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nThursday, February 12\r\n\r\nThursday, March 12\r\n\r\nThursday, April 9\r\n\r\nThursday, May 14\r\n\r\nThursday, June 11\r\n\r\nThursday, July 9\r\n\r\nThursday, September 10\r\n\r\nThursday, October 8\r\n\r\nThursday, November 12\r\n\r\nThursday, December 10\r\n\r\n6:30 PM | Radnor Township Building\r\n\r\n*Parks & Recreation Board Website* [ https://www.radnor.com/government/boards-and-commissions/parks-recreation-board?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Current Parks & Trails Projects* [ https://www.radnor.com/government/departments/parks-recreation/park-trails-projects?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n*_Fenimore Woods Park Improvements Project \xe2\x80\x93 Stable Renovation are underway._*\r\n\r\nThe\xc2\xa0Fenimore Woods Improvement Project continues to advance steadily and is well underway. In addition to the fencing improvements taking place around the park, the stable will be renovated into park restrooms and storage - as part of the overall improvement project. Following on the heels of the stable renovation beginning, the park pavilion replacement will also start in mid-fall.\xc2\xa0 Please contact Tammy Cohen, Director of Parks & Recreation, at tcohen@radnor.org\xc2\xa0or 610-688-5600.\r\n\r\n*_Important Notice to Park Users_**: *The main parking lot will be closed. **We kindly ask that all park visitors observe and adhere to posted signage, fencing, and established area closures as various phases of the project continue to unfold.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n  Fenimore Stable \r\n\r\nAny questions or concerns regarding park projects, please contact Tammy Cohen, Director of Parks & Recreation, at tcohen@radnor.org.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nRECURRING NEWS\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*"The following section includes recurring, ongoing information.\xc2\xa0"*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nemployment [ https://content.govdelivery.com/landing_pages/54152/a1d1f7f5e35134e15d44cd5a504fb3d6 ]\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nparks [ https://content.govdelivery.com/landing_pages/54154/c4b9ae6bf3cab426371459f1bcc8be2b ]\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\ndogs [ https://content.govdelivery.com/landing_pages/54131/baa90887fe82ebd5554a3455b2034fc3 ]\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nEnvironmental Awareness [ https://content.govdelivery.com/landing_pages/54148/2d570d84e32eb40f3f7ec1f629f5fe79 ]\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nCOMMUNITY INFO\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*Wayne Senior Center*\r\n\r\nThe mission of the Wayne Senior Center is to provide community, friendship, and resources which enrich the lives of older adults.\r\n\r\nWould you like to be added to the WSC Connect Newsletter to get a weekly update on programming offered?\r\n\r\nEmail: info@wayneseniorcenter.org\r\n\r\n  wayne senior center \r\n\r\n*WSC Website* [ https://wayneseniorcenter.org/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Wayne Cares* is committed to providing and maintaining a network of people providing food and other material support to people in need.\r\n\r\nFood donations are accepted Monday-Friday 8am- 4pm at 210 S. Wayne Ave. Monetary donations and a link to their Amazon wish list can be found here:\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nFood Pantry Wish List [ https://www.amazon.com/hz/wishlist/ls/13NRW6MSJNT0/ref=hz_ls_biz_ex?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n  Wayne Cares Logo \r\n\r\n*Wayne Cares Website* [ https://waynecares.org/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nmansion \r\n\r\n*The Willows Park Preserve*\r\n\r\nRadnor Township operates and maintains the Willows Park, a 47.5 - acre estate purchased in 1973. This irresistible combination of quiet elegance within the unsurpassed beauty of the landscaped grounds includes a picturesque pond with flowing fountains, sweeping panoramas of stately trees, and flowering plants. The grounds are great for a hike, lunch in the picnic area, or just to sit on a bench and take in the scenery.\r\n\r\n"*Reserve the Willows Picnic Grove for your next event! Reservation requests can be made at www.radnorrecreation.com!*"\r\n\r\nThe Willows Park Preserve (WPP) has been established with a vision and passion for preserving the Willows Park Mansion The WPP is a nonprofit organization whose mission is to physically restore the Mansion and to make it available for community use. In 2019, the WPP signed a 25-year lease with Radnor Township to restore, maintain and operate the Willows Mansion, bringing the Mansion to life for all to enjoy!\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More about the Willows Park Preserve* [ https://willowsparkpreserve.org/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Radnor Township Civic Association*\r\n\r\nLocated at 248 highland Ave in Wayne\r\n\r\nThe RTCA has a main hall with a seating capacity of approximately 150 people. For more information on rentals and reservations, please contact:\r\n\r\nHoward Childs; 267-562-9793\r\nPamela Deans; 484-431-3044\r\nCharles Marshall; 610-420-1538\r\n\r\n  RTCA building \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nsports \r\n\r\n*Community Sport Organizations*\r\n\r\nRadnor Township offers a variety of sport and civic organizations for our youth and adult community members to join.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://radnor.prod.govaccess.org/government/departments/parks-recreation/community-organizations?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nManage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/PARADNOR/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe All [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/PARADNOR/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.8df60fc98d8610bdd9ee8a9e391652de&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n__________________________________________