[2026-04-27 10:41:18] Raw text/plain payload: b'If your email program has trouble displaying this email, view as a webpage [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/bulletins/406132a ].\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nUS Food and Drug Administration\r\nFDA Releases Human Food Program (HFP) 2026 Priority Deliverables \r\n\r\n*View on the FDA Website [ https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.fda.gov%2Ffood%2Fhfp-constituent-updates%2Ffda-releases-2026-deliverables-human-foods-program%3Futm_medium=email%26utm_source=govdelivery/1/0101019bec3df28e-e2335b2c-8930-41b0-a0b6-84a2bac773ff-000000/5PIILlgD1gJSXDRJ2DuKfPG4ZjUNLve85RwDzFU9dAQ=441 ]*\r\n\r\nJanuary 23, 2026\r\n\r\nToday, FDA\xe2\x80\x99s Human Foods Program (HFP) released its\xc2\xa0priority deliverables for 2026 [ https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.fda.gov%2Fabout-fda%2Fhuman-foods-program%2Fhuman-foods-program-2026-priority-deliverables%3Futm_medium=email%26utm_source=govdelivery/1/0101019bec3df28e-e2335b2c-8930-41b0-a0b6-84a2bac773ff-000000/YpOaDX7Ga1ERNIkoF7h4xuPIvdZbmptehAYE-rpGzmM=441 ], as HFP continues to advance its mission, vision, and implementation of its\xc2\xa0Make America Healthy Again [ https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.hhs.gov%2Fmaha%2Findex.html%3Futm_medium=email%26utm_source=govdelivery/1/0101019bec3df28e-e2335b2c-8930-41b0-a0b6-84a2bac773ff-000000/ocqJPdszt7_aXI2MGMJCatjeRTdttVl1DZrrhKkHSMU=441 ]\xc2\xa0agenda. As part of HFP\xe2\x80\x99s comprehensive plan, these targeted deliverables represent more than incremental progress; they signal a transformation in how HFP fulfills its mission to protect and enhance public health.\r\n\r\nIn 2026, HFP will build on significant accomplishments in 2025, guided by the\xc2\xa0three risk pillars [ https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.fda.gov%2Fabout-fda%2Fhuman-foods-program%2Foverview-human-foods-program-hfp-operating-model%3Futm_medium=email%26utm_source=govdelivery/1/0101019bec3df28e-e2335b2c-8930-41b0-a0b6-84a2bac773ff-000000/aZqCdDjLdLEHEkhg0GhBLjzWJlPhS6zf8KZbJ15WNhI=441 ]\xc2\xa0at the core of our work, to strengthen and shape the next phase of our efforts. Throughout this year, FDA intends to provide periodic updates on our progress.\r\n\r\nAt a high level, a few of our planned activities include:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * *Food Chemical Safety*: Improving the safety of food ingredients by systematically reviewing and, where appropriate, banning additives from the food supply. \r\n  * *Nutrition*: Helping to reduce the prevalence of diet-related chronic disease by increasing transparency and empowering consumers to make informed choices through enhanced food labeling, such as front-of-package nutrition labeling; and expanding options for safe, reliable, and nutritious infant formula for American families through\xc2\xa0Operation Stork Speed [ https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.fda.gov%2Fnews-events%2Fpress-announcements%2Fhhs-fda-announce-operation-stork-speed-expand-options-safe-reliable-and-nutritious-infant-formula%3Futm_medium=email%26utm_source=govdelivery/1/0101019bec3df28e-e2335b2c-8930-41b0-a0b6-84a2bac773ff-000000/F64RSQJ67jFgQ0VUrcbyJsF393_4YUlAlOlibQsUsqA=441 ]\xc2\xa0initiatives. \r\n  * *Microbiological Food Safety*: Enhancing food safety by advancing strategies and best practices for preventing contamination in human foods, strengthening protection by leveraging state oversight to complement FDA\xe2\x80\x99s resources, and improving transparency of FDA\xe2\x80\x99s regulatory and enforcement decisions. \r\n\r\nIn line with these 2026 priorities, HFP is also publishing its proposed\xc2\xa02026 guidance agenda [ https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.fda.gov%2Ffood%2Fguidance-documents-regulatory-information-topic-food-and-dietary-supplements%2Ffoods-program-guidance-under-development%3Futm_medium=email%26utm_source=govdelivery/1/0101019bec3df28e-e2335b2c-8930-41b0-a0b6-84a2bac773ff-000000/tcJWV2KFqdPG7TVUg2AWI34CqFkHUP60hzlilmu2Sco=441 ]\xc2\xa0to increase transparency of our work and processes, enhance food safety, and empower consumer nutrition choices, including the following impactful public health actions:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Establishing action levels for cadmium and inorganic arsenic in infant and young children\'s foods, plus issuing guidance on preventive controls for chemical hazards. \r\n  * Issuing guidance to assist industry in implementing effective sanitation controls consistent with the Preventive Controls for Human Food rule. \r\n  * Issuing guidance to assist with food labeling for online grocery store platforms to give consumers access to nutrition information wherever they shop. \xc2\xa0 \r\n\r\nOur goals for 2026 are ambitious, but HFP has the dedication, knowledge, and experience to tackle them. These priorities carry us towards a future of better protecting and promoting public health through science-based approaches aimed at preventing foodborne illness, reducing diet-related chronic disease, and ensuring the safety of chemicals in food.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nAn unofficial translation of this announcement is provided below.\r\n\r\n\xe7\xbf\xbb\xe8\xaf\x91\xe5\x8f\x82\xe8\x80\x83\xef\xbc\x9a\r\n\r\n*FDA **\xe5\x8f\x91\xe5\xb8\x83** 2026 **\xe5\xb9\xb4\xe4\xba\xba\xe7\xb1\xbb\xe9\xa3\x9f\xe5\x93\x81\xe5\xae\x89\xe5\x85\xa8\xe4\xb8\xad\xe5\xbf\x83** (HFP) **\xe7\x9a\x84\xe4\xbc\x98\xe5\x85\x88\xe4\xba\x8b\xe9\xa1\xb9* \r\n\r\n*\xe5\x9c\xa8** FDA **\xe7\xbd\x91\xe7\xab\x99\xe4\xb8\x8a\xe6\x9f\xa5\xe7\x9c\x8b* [ https://links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Flinks-2.govdelivery.com%2FCL0%2Fhttps:%252F%252Fwww.fda.gov%252Ffood%252Fhfp-constituent-updates%252Ffda-releases-2026-deliverables-human-foods-program%253Futm_medium=email%2526utm_source=govdelivery%2F1%2F0101019bec3df28e-e2335b2c-8930-41b0-a0b6-84a2bac773ff-000000%2F5PIILlgD1gJSXDRJ2DuKfPG4ZjUNLve85RwDzFU9dAQ=441/2/0101019bf96049de-fd28ddaa-f45e-4055-af73-6d0acc01c249-000000/pi4Q8Q21f3w7zzxuEhXYSH0g