[2026-04-27 10:41:24] Raw text/plain payload: b"Census Bureau Upcoming and Recently Released Products  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/en.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nCity Population Estimates \r\n\r\nVintage 2025\xc2\xa0Population Estimates, Components of Change\xc2\xa0and Voting-Age Population for the Nation, States\xc2\xa0and Puerto Rico\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nOn Jan. 27, the U.S. Census Bureau will release July 1, 2025, estimates of total population and voting-age population for the nation, states and Puerto Rico, as well as corresponding annual estimates and components of change since the 2020 Census.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n2020-2024 Embargo ACS \r\n\r\n2020-2024 American Community Survey\r\n\r\nOn Jan. 27, the U.S. Census Bureau will make available the remaining 2024 American Community Survey (ACS) 5-year estimates to embargo subscribers. *The data will be released publicly on Jan. 29*, and will include the 2020-2024 ACS 5-year estimates and 5-year Variance Replicate Estimates. The last release of 2020-2024 ACS 5-year PUMS files is set for March 5. The updated release schedule [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/news/data-releases/2024/release-schedule.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0is available online.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSAIPE \r\n\r\nOn Jan. 27, the U.S. Census Bureau will release new data on small area income and poverty estimates for states, counties and school districts. The new data come from the 2024 Small Area Income and Poverty Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/saipe.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (SAIPE), which provides the only up-to-date, single-year income and poverty statistics for the nation\xe2\x80\x99s 3,143\xc2\xa0counties and 13,126\xc2\xa0school districts.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSocial and Economic Characteristics of Currently Unmarried Women With a Recent Birth: 2023\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nOn Jan. 28, the U.S. Census Bureau will release a new report that explores social and economic characteristics of unmarried women who gave birth in 2023. The report uses American Community Survey [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (ACS) data and makes comparisons, when possible, to an earlier report [ https://www2.census.gov/library/publications/2013/acs/acs-21.pdf?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] that used 2011 ACS 1-year estimates.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n2024 Community Resilience Estimates\r\n\r\nOn Jan. 29, the U.S. Census Bureau will release new community resilience estimates by social vulnerability to natural disasters. This product helps local governments and community stakeholders plan mitigation and recovery strategies in the event of a disaster. Estimates will be released for the nation, states, counties, core-based statistical areas and tracts.\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nBTOS \r\n\r\nOn Jan. 29, the U.S. Census Bureau will release The Business Trends and Outlook Survey (BTOS) [ https://www.census.gov/hfp/btos/data?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]. BTOS measures business conditions on an ongoing basis. BTOS experimental data products are representative of all employer businesses other than farms in the U.S. economy. The data allow greater insight into the state of the economy by providing continuous, timely information for key economic measures.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*?? In Case You Missed It*\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nPopulation Estimates Methodology Webinar [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/webinar-methodology-updates.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nThe U.S. Census Bureau held a webinar [ https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?data=05%7C02%7CDonna.E.Tillery%40census.gov%7C3319d2aed84a41500d2e08de54642452%7C3aa716f1e55941cea53047d18313c603%7C0%7C0%7C639040986271958824%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&reserved=0&sdata=uteoGlFEkoOHJfcW%2F59Bq%2B0Fxav6Zgglqk5U5CIpSxI%3D&url=https%3A%2F%2Flinks-1.govdelivery.com%2FCL0%2Fhttps%3A%252F%252Fwww.census.gov%252Fdata%252Facademy%252Fwebinars%252F2026%252Fmethodology-updates-vintage-2025-estimates.html%253Futm_campaign%3D20260115pios2%2526utm_medium%3Demail%2526utm_source%3Dgovdelivery%2F1%2F0100019bc2eb6b62-a9196d0d-b303-4453-ba4f-9fc93ac16be7-000000%2FNkOfOLOFLsGr2Acuq2QmG3mYh-0CkxTIdjCUE1VgRrI%3D440%3Futm_campaign%3D20260126mspios1ccpupnl%26utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dgovdelivery&utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] Tuesday, Jan. 20,\xc2\xa0 on methodology updates for the Vintage 2025 population estimates.\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/webinar-methodology-updates.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nCensus Bureau: American Community Survey 2020-2024 5-year estimates pre-release webinar [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-estimates-webinar-embargo.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nOn Jan. 22, the U.S. Census Bureau held a prerelease webinar [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/2026/2020-2024-acs-5-year-prerelease.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] about the 2020-2024 American Community Survey [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/about.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (ACS) 5-year estimates. The webinar explained how to access ACS data and give tips on comparing geographies and statistics over time.\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-estimates-webinar-embargo.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nA family of four unpacking a moving truck outside of a new home. [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2024-state-to-state-migration.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nOn Jan. 21, the U.S. Census Bureau released the latest version of the State-to-State Migration Flows table package. Tables come from the 2024 American Community Survey 1-year estimates. The State-to-State Migration Flows [ https://www.census.gov/data/tables/time-series/demo/geographic-mobility/state-to-state-migration.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0table will provide estimates of the number of people moving between origin and destination geographies.\xc2\xa0The\xc2\xa0State of Residence by Place of Birth [ https://www.census.gov/data/tables/time-series/demo/geographic-mobility/state-of-residence-place-of-birth-acs.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] table will provide estimates of the number of people living in their current state of residence by place of birth.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2024-state-to-state-migration.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n2024 Planning Database\r\n\r\nOn Jan, 22, the U.S. Census Bureau is scheduled to release the 2024 Planning Database (PDB), which includes the Low Response Score (LRS) and other new 2020 Census operational data.\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2024-planning-database.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nPublic Information Office\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nUpcoming Events and News Releases:\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*_Monday, Jan. 26_*\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Media Advisory:* 2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-year Estimates Embargo (resend from Jan. 22) (English/Spanish)\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Biweekly Tip Sheet only: *New Data Tables on Characteristics of Same-Sex Couple Households\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Biweekly Tip Sheet only: *Energy and Rental Assistance Fact Sheet\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Biweekly Tip Sheet only: *Child Support Received Fact Sheet\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Economic Indicator:* (8:30 a.m.) Advance Report on Durable Goods [ http://www.census.gov/manufacturing/m3/?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x94 Manufacturers\xe2\x80\x99 Shipments, Inventories and Orders \xe2\x80\x93 November 2025\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*_Tuesday, Jan. 27_*\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************News Release:* Vintage 2025 Population Estimates for Total Population and Components of Change Estimates for the Nation, States, and Puerto Rico; Voting-age Population Estimates for the Nation, States, and Puerto Rico Commonwealth (English/Spanish)\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Embargoed News Release: *2020-2024 ACS 5-year data and 2020-2024 ACS 5-year Variance Replicate Estimates (English/Spanish)__\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Random Samplings Blog: *Net International Migration Changes in Population Estimates__\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Extended Tip Sheet: *2024 Small Area Income and Poverty Estimates__\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0__\r\n\r\n*_Wednesday, Jan. 28_*\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Extended Tip Sheet: *Social and Economic Characteristics of Currently Unmarried Women With a Recent Birth: 2023__\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*_Thursday, Jan. 29_*\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************News Release: *2020-2024 ACS 5-year data and 2020-2024 ACS 5-year Variance Replicate Estimates (English/Spanish)\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Tip Sheet: *2024 Community Resilience Estimates\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Tip Sheet: *Business Trends and Outlook Survey Data Release\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Economic Indicator:* (10 a.m.) Full Report \xe2\x80\x94 Manufacturers\xe2\x80\x99 Shipments, Inventories and Orders [ http://www.census.gov/manufacturing/m3/?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x93 November 2025\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Economic Indicator:* (8:30 a.m.) S. International Trade in Goods and Services [ https://www.census.gov/foreign-trade/index.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x93 November 2025\r\n\r\n**********************\xe2\x80\xa2 *********************Economic Indicator:* (10 a.m.) Monthly Wholesale Trade [ http://www.census.gov/wholesale/index.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]: Sales and Inventories \xe2\x80\x93 November 2025\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Newsroom* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nNews media: 301-763-3030 or 877-861-2010 or\xc2\xa0pio@census.gov\r\n\r\nNon-media: 1-800-923-8282 or\xc2\xa0ask.census.gov [ https://ask.census.gov/?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nSubscribe now [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/new? ]\xc2\xa0to receive Census Bureau releases and information via e-mail or SMS.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nWe serve as the nation\xe2\x80\x99s leading provider of quality data about its people and economy.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau is the federal government's largest statistical agency. As the world\xe2\x80\x99s premier statistical agency, we are dedicated to making our nation a better place. Policy-makers, businesses, and the public use our data to make informed decisions.\r\n\r\n*Resources for Media*\r\n\r\nFor media interviews, please contact the\xc2\xa0Public Information Office [ https://lnks.gd/l/eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..p-5wpj2DTx0_qgyLiv6JuMTDOF_vZlHcwFpt971jIDs/s/866068797/br/124287751808-l?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Toll Free at 877-861-2010, 301-763-3030, or\xc2\xa0pio@census.gov.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n*Stay connected with us!*\r\n\r\nJoin the conversation on social media.\r\n\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nSubscriber Settings [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Remove me from All Subscriptions  [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n&lt;!-- /* template top padding on mobile */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { table#flexible-abe-main-table { padding:0 !important; } } --&gt; ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260126mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-