[2026-04-27 10:41:29] Raw text/plain payload: b"Bookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/bulletins/40619f4?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nIRS.gov Banner \r\n\r\nIRS Newswire\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nJanuary 26, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n [ #Fifteenth ] \r\n\r\nIssue Number: \xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0IR-2026-12\r\n\r\nInside This Issue\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*IRS opens 2026 filing season* \r\n\r\nIR-2026-12, Jan. 26, 2026\r\n\r\nWASHINGTON \xe2\x80\x94 The Internal Revenue Service today opened the 2026 tax filing season and began accepting and processing federal individual income tax returns for tax year 2025. \r\n\r\nThe IRS expects about 164 million individual tax returns for tax year 2025 to be filed ahead of the Wednesday, April 15, federal deadline. Taxpayers can find a range of tools and filing options on IRS.gov to help them prepare and file their returns. \r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cAs America celebrates its 250th anniversary, the IRS and its employees are excited to once again serve American taxpayers in meeting their tax filing obligations during the 2026 filing season,\xe2\x80\x9d said IRS Chief Executive Officer Frank J. Bisignano. \r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cNot only does 2026 commemorate the 250th anniversary of the signing of the Declaration of Independence, but it also coincides with the 40th anniversary of electronic filing,\xe2\x80\x9d Bisignano said. \xe2\x80\x9cJust as we did back in 1986, today the IRS encourages taxpayers to speed the processing of their returns by using e-file, instead of paper. And to speed the processing of any refund due, we also encourage the use of direct deposit,\xe2\x80\x9d he added.\r\n\r\n*Get help preparing and filing electronically*\r\n\r\nFiling electronically and choosing direct deposit remains the fastest way to receive a refund.\r\n\r\n\r\n  * IRS Free File [ https://www.irs.gov/filing/irs-free-file-do-your-taxes-for-free ] offers eligible taxpayers brand-name tax preparation software at no cost. \r\n  * Free File Fillable Forms [ https://www.irs.gov/e-file-providers/free-file-fillable-forms ] are available to taxpayers who are comfortable preparing and filing their own returns, regardless of income level. \r\n  * Volunteer Income Tax Assistance and Tax Counseling for the Elderly [ https://www.irs.gov/individuals/free-tax-return-preparation-for-qualifying-taxpayers ] programs offer free basic tax return preparation to qualified individuals. \r\n\r\nMore than half of taxpayers use a tax professional to prepare and file their tax returns. The IRS encourages taxpayers to review tips for choosing a tax preparer [ https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc254 ] and learn how to avoid unethical \xe2\x80\x9cghost\xe2\x80\x9d return preparers [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/dirty-dozen-irs-urges-taxpayers-to-not-fall-prey-to-untrustworthy-tax-preparers-ghost-preparers-can-disappear-with-taxpayer-cash-information ].\r\n\r\n*Most refunds are issued within 21 days *\r\n\r\nDirect deposit is the fastest way to receive a refund. Additionally, in accordance with Executive Order 14247 [ https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/03/modernizing-payments-to-and-from-americas-bank-account/ ], the IRS began phasing out paper tax refund checks on Sept. 30, 2025, meaning most taxpayers must provide their routing and account numbers to receive refunds directly deposited into their bank accounts.\r\n\r\nTaxpayers can track refund status using Where\xe2\x80\x99s My Refund? [ https://www.irs.gov/wheres-my-refund ], the IRS2Go [ https://www.irs.gov/help/irs2goapp ] app, or their IRS Individual Online Account [ https://www.irs.gov/payments/online-account-for-individuals ].\r\n\r\nWhile the IRS issues most refunds in fewer than 21 days, some returns require additional review and may take longer. \r\n\r\n*EITC and ACTC refunds available by March 2*\r\n\r\nThe IRS expects most refunds for the Earned Income Tax Credit and the Additional Child Tax Credit to be available in bank accounts or on debit cards by March 2, 2026, for taxpayers who chose direct deposit and have no other issues with their returns. Some taxpayers may receive their refund earlier, depending on their financial institution. Where\xe2\x80\x99s My Refund? will provide projected deposit dates for most early EITC/ACTC refund filers by Feb. 21, 2026.\r\n\r\nFor more information and tools to help file a complete and accurate return [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/follow-key-filing-guidelines-to-speed-refunds-avoid-errors ] and avoid errors that can delay refunds, visit IRS.gov.\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ] \xc2\xa0Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ] \xc2\xa0LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to the IRS Newswire, an IRS e-mail service.\r\n\r\nIf you know someone who might want to subscribe to this mailing list, please forward this message to them so they can subscribe [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ].\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically from the mailing list IRS Newswire. *Please Do Not Reply To This Message.*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNews Essentials\r\n\r\nWhat's Hot [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/whats-hot ]\r\n\r\nNews Releases [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\nIRS - The Basics [ https://www.irs.gov/about-irs/irs-the-basics ]\r\n\r\nIRS Guidance [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/understanding-irs-guidance-a-brief-primer ]\r\n\r\nMedia Contacts [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-media-relations-office-contact-number ]\r\n\r\nFacts & Figures [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nAround The Nation [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/around-the-nation ]\r\n\r\ne-News Subscriptions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe Newsroom Topics\r\n\r\nMultimedia Center [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/multimedia-center ]\r\n\r\nNoticias en Espa\xc3\xb1ol [ https://www.irs.gov/es/spanish/noticias-en-espanol ]\r\n\r\nRadio PSAs [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-radio-psas ]\r\n\r\nTax Scams [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-scams-consumer-alerts ]\r\n\r\nThe Tax Gap [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/the-tax-gap ]\r\n\r\nFact Sheets [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nIRS Tax Tips [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-tax-tips ]\r\n\r\nArmed Forces [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-information-for-members-of-the-us-armed-forces ]\r\n\r\nLatest News Home [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIRS Resources\r\n\r\nContact My Local Office [ https://www.irs.gov/help/contact-your-local-irs-office ]\r\n\r\nFiling Options [ https://www.irs.gov/filing ]\r\n\r\nForms & Instructions [ https://www.irs.gov/forms-instructions ]\r\n\r\nFrequently Asked Questions [ https://www.irs.gov/help/telephone-assistance ]\r\n\r\nNews [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom ]\r\n\r\nTaxpayer Advocate [ https://www.irs.gov/taxpayer-advocate ]\r\n\r\nWhere to File [ https://www.irs.gov/filing/where-to-file-paper-tax-returns-with-or-without-a-payment ]\r\n\r\nIRS Social Media [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-new-media-1 ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n/*start reset css*/ div { line-height: 1; } body, table, td, p, a, li, blockquote { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; } body { -webkit-text-size-adjust: none; -ms-text-size-adjust: non