[2026-04-27 10:56:31] Raw text/plain payload: b'Bookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/bulletins/4064fa4?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nIRS.gov Banner \r\n\r\nIRS Newswire\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nJanuary 27, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nIssue Number: \xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0IR-2026-13\r\n\r\nInside This Issue\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*IRS issues frequently asked questions about Executive Order 14247: Modernizing Payments To and From America\xe2\x80\x99s Bank Account*\r\n\r\nIR-2026-13, Jan. 27, 2026\r\n\r\nWASHINGTON \xe2\x80\x94 The Internal Revenue Service today issued frequently asked questions in Fact Sheet 2026-02 [ https://www.irs.gov/pub/taxpros/fs-2026-02.pdf ] to help taxpayers, businesses, and other stakeholders understand the changes under Executive Order 14247: Modernizing Payment To and From America\xe2\x80\x99s Bank Account [ https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/03/modernizing-payments-to-and-from-americas-bank-account/ ]. \r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cThese FAQs support the Executive Order in its effort to reduce fraud, improve security, lower costs, and make payments to and from the IRS faster and more reliable," IRS Chief Executive Officer Frank J. Bisignano said.\r\n\r\n*Background*\r\n\r\nThe U.S. Department of the Treasury, in collaboration with the IRS and other federal agencies, is transitioning federal payments to and from the government to electronic methods pursuant to Executive Order 14247, signed March 25, 2025.\xc2\xa0 \r\n\r\nThese changes apply to:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Payments sent by the federal government, including tax refunds, benefits, grants, and vendor or contractor payments; and \r\n  * Payments made to the federal government, including tax balances due, fees, penalties, and other payments from individuals, businesses, nonprofit organizations, and state or local partners. \r\n\r\nElectronic payments are generally processed faster, cost less to handle, and reduce errors compared to paper payments. Limited exceptions to electronic payment requirements will be available in specific situations, such as those involving hardship and/or legal or procedural requirements.\r\n\r\n*Filing tax returns is not changing*\r\n\r\nThe Executive Order does not change how taxpayers file their tax returns. Taxpayers will continue to file their returns in the same manner as they have in the past. The change affects how refunds are issued and how payments are made, not how returns are prepared or submitted, beginning with the 2026 filing season. For now, checks and money orders will still be accepted.\xc2\xa0 \r\n\r\n*What taxpayers should do now*\r\n\r\nTo prepare for these changes, the IRS encourages taxpayers to:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Use direct deposit [ https://www.irs.gov/refunds/get-your-refund-faster-tell-irs-to-direct-deposit-your-refund-to-one-two-or-three-accounts ] for refunds by providing accurate bank or prepaid debit card information when filing. \r\n  * Choose electronic payment options when paying taxes, such as IRS Direct Pay [ https://www.irs.gov/payments/direct-pay-with-bank-account ], Electronic Federal Tax Payment System [ https://www.irs.gov/payments/eftps-the-electronic-federal-tax-payment-system ], or other approved methods. \r\n  * Review account information to ensure bank details are current and correct. \r\n  * Visit IRS.gov to learn about electronic payment [ https://www.irs.gov/payments ] options and available resources for taxpayers without a bank account. \r\n\r\nFor more information about how the IRS is implementing the Executive Order, visit Modernizing Payments To and From America\xe2\x80\x99s Bank Account [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/modernizing-payments-to-and-from-americas-bank-account ] on IRS.gov.\r\n\r\nMore information about\xc2\xa0reliance [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/general-overview-of-taxpayer-reliance-on-guidance-published-in-the-internal-revenue-bulletin-and-faqs ] is available\xc2\xa0on IRS.gov.\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ] \xc2\xa0Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ] \xc2\xa0LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to the IRS Newswire, an IRS e-mail service.\r\n\r\nIf you know someone who might want to subscribe to this mailing list, please forward this message to them so they can subscribe [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ].\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically from the mailing list IRS Newswire. *Please Do Not Reply To This Message.*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNews Essentials\r\n\r\nWhat\'s Hot [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/whats-hot ]\r\n\r\nNews Releases [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\nIRS - The Basics [ https://www.irs.gov/about-irs/irs-the-basics ]\r\n\r\nIRS Guidance [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/understanding-irs-guidance-a-brief-primer ]\r\n\r\nMedia Contacts [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-media-relations-office-contact-number ]\r\n\r\nFacts & Figures [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nAround The Nation [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/around-the-nation ]\r\n\r\ne-News Subscriptions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe Newsroom Topics\r\n\r\nMultimedia Center [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/multimedia-center ]\r\n\r\nNoticias en Espa\xc3\xb1ol [ https://www.irs.gov/es/spanish/noticias-en-espanol ]\r\n\r\nRadio PSAs [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-radio-psas ]\r\n\r\nTax Scams [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-scams-consumer-alerts ]\r\n\r\nT