[2026-04-27 10:56:43] Raw text/plain payload: b'Bookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/bulletins/4064f10?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nIRS.gov Banner \r\n\r\nIRS Newswire\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nJanuary 27, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nIssue Number:\xc2\xa0 IR-2026-14\r\n\r\nInside This Issue\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*Taxpayer Advocate Service announces 2026 funding for Low Income Taxpayer Clinic grant recipients*\r\n\r\nIR-2026-14, Jan. 27, 2026\r\n\r\nWASHINGTON \xe2\x80\x94 The Taxpayer Advocate Service today announced the award of more than $22.5 million in matching grants to 145 qualified Low Income Taxpayer Clinics nationwide for the 2026 grant year, which runs from Jan. 1, 2026, to Dec. 31, 2026.\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cLITCs continue to be a lifeline for taxpayers who need help the most,\xe2\x80\x9d said National Taxpayer Advocate Erin M. Collins. \xe2\x80\x9cThese grants will strengthen the clinics\xe2\x80\x99 ability to provide expert assistance, protect taxpayer rights, and ensure vulnerable taxpayers are not left to navigate complex tax issues alone. The remarkable impact of the LITC Program is made possible by the clinicians, volunteers, advocates, and members of Congress who champion this work. Their dedication has transformed countless lives, and this funding helps ensure that mission endures and grows.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\nThrough the LITC Program, the IRS awards matching grants of up to $200,000 per year to qualifying organizations. The program is administered by TAS, an independent organization within the IRS, led by the National Taxpayer Advocate. Although LITCs receive partial funding from the IRS, LITCs and their employees and volunteers operate independently from the IRS.\r\n\r\n*Low Income Taxpayer Clinics help ensure fairness and integrity in the tax system*\r\n\r\nLITCs support taxpayers through a wide range of services, including:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Providing\xc2\xa0"pro bono"\xc2\xa0representation to assist low-income taxpayers in resolving tax disputes with the IRS; \r\n  * Educating taxpayers for whom English is a second language about their rights and responsibilities as taxpayers; and \r\n  * Identifying and advocating for issues that impact these taxpayers. \r\n\r\nA list of 2026 grant recipients [ https://www.taxpayeradvocate.irs.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/2026LITC_GrantRecipients-final.pdf ] is available on the LITC Grant Information [ https://www.taxpayeradvocate.irs.gov/about-us/litc-grants/ ] page on the Taxpayer Advocate Service [ https://www.taxpayeradvocate.irs.gov/ ] website.\r\n\r\nAdditional information about LITCs and their work is available in IRS Publication 5066-A [ https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-pdf/p5066a.pdf ], Low Income Taxpayer Clinic Program.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ] \xc2\xa0Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ] \xc2\xa0LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to the IRS Newswire, an IRS e-mail service.\r\n\r\nIf you know someone who might want to subscribe to this mailing list, please forward this message to them so they can subscribe [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ].\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically from the mailing list IRS Newswire. *Please Do Not Reply To This Message.*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNews Essentials\r\n\r\nWhat\'s Hot [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/whats-hot ]\r\n\r\nNews Releases [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\nIRS - The Basics [ https://www.irs.gov/about-irs/irs-the-basics ]\r\n\r\nIRS Guidance [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/understanding-irs-guidance-a-brief-primer ]\r\n\r\nMedia Contacts [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-media-relations-office-contact-number ]\r\n\r\nFacts & Figures [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nAround The Nation [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/around-the-nation ]\r\n\r\ne-News Subscriptions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe Newsroom Topics\r\n\r\nMultimedia Center [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/multimedia-center ]\r\n\r\nNoticias en Espa\xc3\xb1ol [ https://www.irs.gov/es/spanish/noticias-en-espanol ]\r\n\r\nRadio PSAs [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-radio-psas ]\r\n\r\nTax Scams [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-scams-consumer-alerts ]\r\n\r\nThe Tax Gap [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/the-tax-gap ]\r\n\r\nFact Sheets [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nIRS Tax Tips [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-tax-tips ]\r\n\r\nArmed Forces [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-information-for-members-of-the-us-armed-forces ]\r\n\r\nLatest News Home [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIRS Resources\r\n\r\nContact My Local Office [ https://www.irs.gov/help/contact-your-local-irs-office ]\r\n\r\nFiling Options [ https://www.irs.gov/filing ]\r\n\r\nForms & Instructions [ https://www.irs.gov/forms-instructions ]\r\n\r\nFrequently Asked Questions [ https://www.irs.gov/help/telephone-assistance ]\r\n\r\nNews [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom ]\r\n\r\nTaxpayer Advocate [ https://www.irs.gov/taxpayer-advocate ]\r\n\r\nWhere to File [ https://www.irs.gov/filing/where-to-file-paper-tax-returns-with-or-without-a-payment ]\r\n\r\nIRS Social Media [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-new-media-1 ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n/*start reset css*/ div { line-height: 1; } body, table, td, p, a, 