[2026-04-27 10:57:22] Raw text/plain payload: b'New report examines the social and economic characteristics of unmarried women with a recent birth.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/births-to-unmarried-women-declined.html?utm_campaign=20260128pio&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNew Data Show Fewer Women Gave Birth While Unmarried in the Past Decade  [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/births-to-unmarried-women-declined.html?utm_campaign=20260128pio&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*JAN. 28, 2026 *\xe2\x80\x94 The percentage of women with a recent birth who were unmarried decreased by 4.8 percentage points, from 35.7% (or under 1.5 million) in 2011 to 30.9% (or 1.2 million) in 2023, according to a new U.S. Census Bureau report titled "Social and Economic Characteristics of Currently Unmarried Women With a Recent Birth: 2023."\r\n\r\nIn 2023, four million women ages 15 to 50 gave birth in the last year. Of the 1.2 million women with a recent birth who were unmarried, 35.5% (or around 450,000) lived with an unmarried partner.\r\n\r\nThe report uses 2023 American Community Survey (ACS) data to explore social and economic characteristics of unmarried women with a recent birth and makes comparisons, when possible, to an earlier report that used 2011 ACS 1-year estimates.\r\n\r\n*Highlights* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/births-to-unmarried-women-declined.html?utm_campaign=20260128pio&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHelp us spread the word about Census Bureau data!\r\n\r\nShare this on social media or forward it to a friend.\r\n\r\n*Share This* [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/4067b52 ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nWe serve as the nation\xe2\x80\x99s leading provider of quality data about its people and economy.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau is the federal government\'s largest statistical agency. As the world\xe2\x80\x99s premier statistical agency, we are dedicated to making our nation a better place. Policy-makers, businesses, and the public use our data to make informed decisions.\r\n\r\nResources for Media\r\n\r\nFor media interviews, please contact the\xc2\xa0Public Information Office [ https://lnks.gd/l/eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..p-5wpj2DTx0_qgyLiv6JuMTDOF_vZlHcwFpt971jIDs/s/866068797/br/124287751808-l?utm_campaign=20260128pio&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Toll Free at 877-861-2010, 301-763-3030, or\xc2\xa0pio@census.gov.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n*Stay connected with us!*\r\n\r\nJoin the conversation on social media.\r\n\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260128pio&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260128pio&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260128pio&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260128pio&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260128pio&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260128pio&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nSubscriber Settings [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Remove me from All Subscriptions  [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n&lt;!-- /* template top padding on mobile */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { table#flexible-abe-main-table { padding:0 !important; } } --&gt; ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260128pio&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
