[2026-04-27 10:57:26] Raw text/plain payload: b'Driven by recent demand, the DOE IRP has reestablished the capability to provide Bismuth-207.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nHaving trouble viewing this email?\xc2\xa0 [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOEOS/bulletins/0 ]View it as a Web page [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOEOS/bulletins/3eaef81 ].\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNIDC 2025 header \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nDOE Strengthens Domestic Isotope Supply with Bismuth-207\r\n\r\nDriven by recent demand, the U.S. Department of Energy Office of Isotope R&D and Production, within the Office of Science, has reestablished the capability to provide Bismuth-207 (Bi-207) and is currently the only domestic producer of this isotope.\r\n\r\nBi-207, with a half-life of 31.55 years, is a radioisotope commonly used as a gamma calibration source across the nuclear industry and in scientific research applications. Bi-207 is produced at the Isotope Production Facility at Los Alamos National Laboratory through proton bombardment of a natural lead target with a radionuclide purity of >99%.\r\n\r\nBi-207 can be ordered in mCi quantities as Bismuth (III) in 4 M HNO\xe2\x82\x83. For further inquiries about Bi-207, please contact the NIDC at\xc2\xa0*contact@isotopes.gov <contact@isotopes.gov?subject=Selenium-75>*\xc2\xa0or click the link below to request a quote.\r\n\r\n*Request a quote for bismuth-207* [ https://isotopes.gov/products/bismuth?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nDOE IP LOGO [ https://science.osti.gov/Isotope-Research-Development-and-Production?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\nNIDC white logo  [ https://www.isotopes.gov/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nYoutube [ https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCC6lZCOqy1YnyRq81TlCKuA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xc2\xa0 Twitter [ https://twitter.com/NIDCIsotopes?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xc2\xa0 Website [ https://www.isotopes.gov?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] Website [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/national-isotope-development-center?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] [ https://www.isotopes.gov?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nCopyright 2026\xc2\xa9 National Isotope Development Center, All Rights Reserved\r\n\r\n*Contact NIDC:\r\n*contact@isotopes.gov\r\nwww.isotopes.gov [ https://www.isotopes.gov/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nWant to change how you receive these emails?\r\nUpdate your preferences [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOEOS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] or unsubscribe from the list [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOEOS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.f79aa68a3024cd2fce56df538b9b073f&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nStay Connected with US Department of Energy Office of Science: Office of Science Website [ https://www.energy.gov/science/office-science?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0Twitter [ https://twitter.com/doescience?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0LinkedIn Icon [ https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/office-of-science?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0Youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/doescience?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  SUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\nManage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOEOS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe All [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOEOS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.f79aa68a3024cd2fce56df538b9b073f&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]  \r\nbody .abe-sectio