[2026-04-27 10:57:35] Raw text/plain payload: b"The Census Bureau has released updated housing unit and group quarters counts for the nation.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/geography.html?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAddress Count Listing Files and Related Map Viewer Updates\r\n\r\nNow Available: New Geospatial Data [ https://www.census.gov/geographies/reference-files/time-series/geo/addcountlisting.html?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nThe Census Bureau has released updated housing unit and group quarters counts for the nation. These counts are released twice a year to provide information on the evolving changes of our nation's residential housing units and group quarters. The housing unit counts are released for each census block in the nation within state-based, pipe-delimited files that are available for download here [ https://www.census.gov/geographies/reference-files/time-series/geo/addcountlisting.html?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\r\n\r\nThe Current Address Count Listing Files Viewer [ https://mtgis-portal.geo.census.gov/arcgis/apps/webappviewer/index.html?id=c754be823d6342949a4c50e519eb87be&utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] enables users to interact with a map application to view the current housing unit and group quarters counts for the census block that the user selects. The Housing Unit Change Viewer [ https://mtgis-portal.geo.census.gov/arcgis/apps/experiencebuilder/experience/?id=3a87e24a2ec54e01ab277a12d467e7d9&utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] enables users to interact with a map application to view the percent change and numeric change in housing units from the 2020 Census through November 2025 by state, county, census tract, census block group, and census block. When a user selects a specific geographic area within the viewer, a pop-up window details the housing unit change counts and provides a historical snapshot of housing unit and group quarters counts from 2020, 2023, 2024, and 2025. \xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Access Files and Viewers* [ https://www.census.gov/geographies/reference-files/time-series/geo/addcountlisting.html?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nHousing Unit Change Viewer Data Gem [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/data-gems/2025/tracking-housing-trends-with-housing-unit-change-viewer.html?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\n*Data Gem: Tracking Housing Trends with the Housing Unit Change Viewer [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/data-gems/2025/tracking-housing-trends-with-housing-unit-change-viewer.html?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nAddress Count Listing Files Viewer Data Gem [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/data-gems/2025/census-address-map-viewer.html?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\n*Data Gem: Discover Your Neighborhood with the Census Address Count Listing Files Viewer [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/data-gems/2025/census-address-map-viewer.html?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Geography Program\r\n\r\nGeography Division Logo [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/geography.html?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nGeography is central to the work of the Census Bureau, providing the framework for survey design, sample selection, data collection, tabulation, and dissemination. Geography provides meaning and context to statistical data.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nUse of the latest and best geographic methodologies is critical to the Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s ability to serve as the leading provider of statistical and geospatial data. Our geographic area concepts, information, and statistical data [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/geography.html?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] must keep pace with the needs of the researchers and analysts who work to understand the changing distribution and characteristics of our people, places, and economy.\r\n\r\n*Share This* [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/4065f52 ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n*Stay connected with us!*\r\n\r\nJoin the conversation on social media.\r\n\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nSubscriber Settings [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Remove me from All Subscriptions  [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n&lt;!-- /* template top padding on mobile */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { table#flexible-abe-main-table { padding:0 !important; } } --&gt; ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260128cnmp&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n"
