[2026-04-27 10:57:52] Raw text/plain payload: b'\r\n[DigitalOcean logo. This image is linked to the DigitalOcean homepage.](https://www.digitalocean.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026&utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026)\r\n\r\nThe DigitalOcean Newsletter\r\n\r\nYour monthly deep dive into all things DigitalOcean, including product updates, new tutorials, upcoming events, and more.\r\n\r\nDeploy 2026: The Production Inference Era\r\n\r\nDeploy 2026 is focused on the real-world work of production AI. Every session is grounded in systems running AI in production today with real traffic, real cost constraints, and real operational tradeoffs.\r\n\r\nJoin the technical leaders and executives who are leaving hyperscaler complexity behind to build the next generation of AI-native companies.\r\n\r\nMarch 31, 2026 \xe2\x80\xa2 Convene 100 Stockton \xe2\x80\xa2 12pm \xe2\x80\x93 8pm PT\r\n\r\n[Secure your spot](https://www.digitalocean.com/deploy?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026)\r\n\r\nProduct Announcements\r\n\r\n[Per-second billing for Droplets to slash costs for ephemeral workloads](https://www.digitalocean.com/blog/dropletplans-persecbilling-byoip-natgateway?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026#droplets-per-second-billing-slashes-costs-for-ephemeral-workloads)\r\nEffective January 1, 2026, we moved to per-second billing (with a 60-second minimum) for Droplets. This offers truly granular cost control, drastically reducing spending on short-lived workloads, such as running batch jobs and automated testing. The monthly cap remains in place for budget predictability on sustained tasks.\r\n\r\n[Usage-based backups to meet aggressive RPOs and slash costs](https://www.digitalocean.com/blog/nfs-cold-storage-backups?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026#usage-based-backups-to-meet-aggressive-rpos)\r\n\r\nOur new usage-based backup service is now generally available, allowing you to schedule high-frequency backups for your Droplets and GPUs every 4, 6, or 12 hours to meet strict Recovery Point Objectives (RPOs). This feature comes with transparent, consumption-based billing, meaning you only pay for the amount of restorable data you use, drastically reducing costs for high-change environments like CI/CD pipelines and AI/ML data protection.\r\n\r\n[Spaces cold storage for infrequently accessed data and archives](https://www.digitalocean.com/blog/nfs-cold-storage-backups?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026#spaces-cold-storage-for-infrequently-accessed-data)\r\n\r\nSpaces cold storage is now generally available as a low-cost, S3-compatible solution for petabyte-scale datasets that are rarely accessed. Store your backups, archives, and application logs for just $0.007/GiB per month. Our simple pricing includes instant retrieval and one retrieval per month at no extra cost, providing predictable, cost-effective scaling for all your retention and compliance needs.\r\n\r\n[Network File Storage (NFS) for high-performance AI workloads](https://www.digitalocean.com/blog/nfs-cold-storage-backups?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026#network-file-storage-nfs-for-high-performance-ai-workloads)\r\n\r\nWe launched Network File Storage, a managed, high-performance shared file system optimized for AI/ML. It enables concurrent access to shared datasets for multi-node GPU/CPU workloads. Provisioning is simple, starting at cost-effective 50 GiB increments, and it meets high-throughput, low-latency demands. This NFS solution is now available in our ATL1 and NYC2 data centers.\r\n\r\n[DigitalOcean Agent Development Kit (ADK) Now in Public Preview](https://www.digitalocean.com/blog/agent-development-kit?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026)\r\n\r\nThe ADK is a Python SDK and CLI that lets you deploy existing agent code as a hosted, production-ready service, all without re-architecting your workflow. Go from local prototypes to reliable, observable agents running on real infrastructure in minutes, with free hosting during the public preview.\r\n\r\n[Automate Your Workflows: n8n Template is Now Available on DigitalOcean App Platform](https://www.digitalocean.com/blog/whats-new-on-app-platform?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026#week-of-january-19th)\r\n\r\nWorkflow automation has become essential for modern development teams looking to eliminate repetitive tasks and connect their favorite tools. n8n is a powerful, fair-code licensed automation platform that gives full control over your data and workflows. With over 400 integrations and a visual workflow builder, n8n is a top request from developers who want automation without vendor lock-in. Now you can deploy a production-ready n8n instance with one click, complete with managed PostgreSQL, SSL/TLS encryption, and automatic health monitoring.\r\n\r\n[See all of our release notes and subscribe to the RSS feed here.](https://docs.digitalocean.com/release-notes/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026&utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=may-2024)\r\n\r\nSimplify, scale, and save: Join our Sail to Success webinar series!\r\n\r\nRunning your cloud workloads shouldn\xe2\x80\x99t be complex or expensive. That\xe2\x80\x99s why we\xe2\x80\x99re bringing you Sail to Success, a webinar series designed to help you simplify, scale, and save with DigitalOcean.\r\n\r\nRegister for our February 2026 webinars\r\n\r\n- February 17: [Dedicated Inference Workloads: How to Master Them](https://streamyard.com/watch/4UBju344b4AW?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026)\r\n- February 25: [Cut your Cloud storage costs](https://streamyard.com/watch/cDRuptCt7T6N?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026)\r\n\r\nCheck out our webinars in our [YouTube playlist](https://youtube.com/playlist?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026&list=PLseEp7p6EwibRYM-4yo_FX5cTMa6qDv3m&si=pv_ue6kM1Ss3npn7).\r\n\r\nResources & Tutorials\r\n\r\n- If you\xe2\x80\x99re new to MoltBot or evaluating whether it\xe2\x80\x99s the right tool for your use case, [this overview explains what MoltBot is](https://www.digitalocean.com/resources/articles/what-is-moltbot?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026), how it works, and where it\xe2\x80\x99s most useful. You\xe2\x80\x99ll get a breakdown of core concepts, key capabilities, and common use cases to help you understand how MoltBot can support automation and application development. You can also learn more about [how Moltbot works behind the scenes in this explainer](https://www.digitalocean.com/community/conceptual-articles/moltbot-behind-the-scenes?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026).\r\n- If you\xe2\x80\x99re getting started with MoltBot, [this quickstart guide](https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/moltbot-quickstart-guide?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026) walks through deploying and configuring MoltBot on a DigitalOcean Droplet step by step. You\xe2\x80\x99ll learn how to create and secure a Droplet, install the MoltBot gateway, connect your LLM provider, and run an always-on personal assistant in the cloud that you can interact with through WhatsApp, the terminal, or a web dashboard.\r\n-\r\n\r\nThe updated [Pricing calculator](https://www.digitalocean.com/pricing/calculator?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026), [regional availability](https://docs.digitalocean.com/platform/regional-availability/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026) and [SLAs](https://www.digitalocean.com/sla?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026) now include our latest networking and storage products. For your 2026 cloud infrastructure planning and budgeting, please utilize the key tools, resources, and product information available on our [website](https://www.digitalocean.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026). If you are looking to [optimize your cloud architecture](https://www.digitalocean.com/blog/optimize-cloud-architecture-for-business-growth?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026) and need help to migrate additional workloads to DigitalOcean, you can [get expert guidance](https://www.digitalocean.com/landing/get-expert-guidance?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026&utm_medium=event&utm_source=virtual&utm_campaign=sailtosuccess_cloudarchitecturereview).\r\n\r\n-\r\n\r\nIf you\xe2\x80\x99re evaluating your [object storage infrastructure](https://www.digitalocean.com/resources/articles/object-storage-solutions-cloud-data?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026) for 2026, explore industry offerings designed for all cloud data use cases and application requirements. You\xe2\x80\x99ll get a side-by-side comparison of DigitalOcean and options from Cloudflare, Microsoft, AWS, and more.\r\n\r\n-\r\n\r\nLooking for [Amazon EC2 alternatives](https://www.digitalocean.com/resources/articles/amazon-ec2-alternatives?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026)? Get information about how to evaluate possible providers, what features they provide, and some frequently asked questions about EC2 competitors. Then you\xe2\x80\x99ll be ready to select the right option to scale your infrastructure without production snafus or unexpected costs.\r\n\r\n-\r\n\r\nThe market for virtual private servers is growing\xe2\x80\x94and expected to reach $14.1 billion by 2033. This means more vendors are popping up with VPS offerings and increasing capabilities to optimize performance, security, and control. Read about how [DigitalOcean compares to AWS Lightsail](https://www.digitalocean.com/resources/articles/digitalocean-vs-awslightsail?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026) to learn more about VPS options.\r\n\r\n-\r\n\r\n[Vercel](https://www.digitalocean.com/resources/articles/vercel-alternatives?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026) is one Platform-as-a-Service offering that streamlines application creation, deployment, and hosting. But it\xe2\x80\x99s not the only option on the market designed to fit developers\xe2\x80\x99 needs. Explore PaaS options (designed for more than front-end development) from DigitalOcean, Netlify, Cloudflare, and AWS.\r\n\r\n-\r\n\r\nFor developers curious about [vision-language-action models](https://www.digitalocean.com/community/conceptual-articles/vision-language-action-models?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026), we\xe2\x80\x99ve got a comprehensive overview designed to explain key examples, elements, and foundational concepts. Get information about RT-1, RT-2, RT2X, and OpenVLA and their architectures (along with some additional references and reading material).\r\n\r\nFeatured & New Marketplace Solutions\r\n\r\nThe [DigitalOcean Marketplace](https://marketplace.digitalocean.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026&utm_medium=&utm_source=&utm_campaign=PAR-2025-newsletters&utm_targeting=--&utm_content=) offers 1-Click apps and tools to help you build faster\xe2\x80\x94no setup hassle. Check out the newest solutions and see what\xe2\x80\x99s fresh this month.\r\n\r\n[n8n](https://marketplace.digitalocean.com/apps/n8n?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026) is a flexible workflow automation tool that enables you to connect and automate tasks between your favorite apps, services, and APIs. With the Droplet 1-Click, you can quickly set up n8n to build powerful, customized workflows using an intuitive, visual interface, enabling seamless integrations tailored to your needs.\r\n\r\ncPanel provides a reliable, intuitive platform that simplifies server and site management, allowing users to focus on growing their business. When paired with DigitalOcean\xe2\x80\x99s powerful cloud infrastructure, customers can seamlessly deploy cPanel on [Ubuntu](https://marketplace.digitalocean.com/apps/cpanel-whm-for-ubuntu?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026) or [AlmaLinux](https://docs.digitalocean.com/products/marketplace/catalog/cpanel-whm-r-for-almalinux-9/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026), combining automation, easy configuration, and robust security. Together, DigitalOcean and cPanel make it effortless to monitor, protect, transfer, and back up data with just a few clicks. With a rich feature set\xe2\x80\x94including email, backups, WordPress management (staging and cloning), and 24/7 technical support\xe2\x80\x94cPanel delivers all the tools needed for secure, scalable, high-performance server management. Trusted by over 20 million users worldwide, it\xe2\x80\x99s the go-to solution for everything from single-site projects to enterprise deployments, offering unmatched control and reliability.\r\n\r\nHave something you\xe2\x80\x99d like to see added to the Marketplace? [Submit your ideas to our ideas portal!](https://ideas.digitalocean.com/marketplace?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026&utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=may-2024)\r\n\r\nFollow us:\r\n\r\n[Twitter](https://twitter.com/digitalocean?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026)\r\n[Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/DigitalOceanCloudHosting?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026)\r\n[YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCaPX53JLxxSbwZz_Ra_cL0g?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026)\r\n[Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/thedigitalocean?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026)\r\n[Linkedin](https://linkedin.com/company/digitalocean?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026)\r\n[Twitch](https://www.twitch.tv/digitaloceantv?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026)\r\n\r\nGive $200, get $25. [Refer a friend](https://cloud.digitalocean.com/account/referrals?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026&utm_medium=email&utm_source=footer&utm_campaign=referral).\r\nTrouble seeing this email? [View it as a web page](https://anchor.digitalocean.com/index.php/email/emailWebview?utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_campaign=Jan-2026).\r\n\r\nCopyright DigitalOcean. All rights reserved.\r\n105 Edgeview Dr., Suite 425, Broomfield, CO 80021\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com. You can update your email subscription preferences here: https://anchor.digitalocean.com/Email_Preferences.html?mkt_unsubscribe=1&mkt_tok=MTEzLURUTi0yNjYAAAGfpdTMix52kWxdzUpcRJDqDPheZ5oC60qVPznNfzASf5QbCZqKu6HI83zCm6pCVCasS9e8sEd-DN_C_NqYajRPK1EAn5F4a9xYP31UGUVLvzqx.\r\n'
