[2026-04-27 10:58:18] Raw text/plain payload: b"Bookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/bulletins/406a105?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nIRS.gov Banner \r\n\r\nIRS Newswire\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nJanuary 29, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nIssue Number: \xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0IR-2026-17\r\n\r\nInside This Issue\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*Tax Pros: Get Ready for the filing season and save time with Tax Pro Account; encourage clients to use their IRS individual online account*\r\n\r\nIR-2026-17, Jan 29, 2026\r\n\r\nWASHINGTON \xe2\x80\x94 With the 2026 filing season fast approaching, the Internal Revenue Service encourages tax professionals to help their clients prepare now by sharing helpful tips and tools available at IRS.gov/GetReady [ http://www.irs.gov/getready ].\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cTax professionals can play a key role in furthering IRS\xe2\x80\x99s mission to ensure taxpayers understand and meet their tax responsibilities,\xe2\x80\x9d said IRS Chief Executive Officer Frank J. Bisignano. \xe2\x80\x9cThe IRS appreciates the support from the tax professional community for its effort to remind the tax paying public about IRS tax tips and tools.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\nThe IRS urges qualified tax professionals to set up an IRS Tax Pro Account [ https://www.irs.gov/tax-professionals/tax-pro-account ] and encourages taxpayers to access their IRS Individual Online Account [ https://www.irs.gov/payments/online-account-for-individuals ]. When both have accounts, they can complete online third-party authorizations [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/power-of-attorney-and-other-authorizations ], such as powers of attorney and tax information authorizations, entirely online. This helps reduce processing times and eliminates the need to fax, mail, or upload documents.\r\n\r\nTo approve an authorization request, the taxpayer logs into their IRS Individual Online Account [ https://www.irs.gov/payments/online-account-for-individuals ], checks a box, and submits the authorization request to the IRS. Most authorizations are processed immediately, though some may take up to 48 hours.\r\n\r\n*Tax Pro Account*\r\n\r\nThrough TPA, the tax professional can also view their client\xe2\x80\x99s individual tax information and act on behalf of them. Using TPA, tax professionals can:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Request and receive an individual CAF number online, in real time. \r\n  * Withdraw active authorizations instantly. \r\n  * Make payments, set up or manage payment plans, and view taxpayer information within the scope of an authorization. \r\n\r\n*IRS Individual Online Account*\r\n\r\nWith an IRS Individual Online Account [ https://www.irs.gov/payments/online-account-for-individuals ], taxpayers can securely access their federal tax information and receive notifications from their tax professional. Taxpayers can: \r\n\r\n\r\n  * View tax records, including adjusted gross income and transcripts. \r\n  * Make, schedule, and view payments. \r\n  * Check the status of a refund. \r\n  * Get or view their Identity Protection PIN [ https://www.irs.gov/identity-theft-fraud-scams/get-an-identity-protection-pin ]. \r\n  * Authorize a tax professional to access their tax records digitally. \r\n  * View available Forms W-2 and certain 1099s. \r\n\r\n*Get ready now*\r\n\r\nTax professionals should take a few other steps today, such as reviewing tax law changes like those in the One, Big, Beautiful Bill [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/one-big-beautiful-bill-news ], gathering documents and sharing online tools with their clients, to help ensure a smoother filing for both themselves and their clients during the 2026 filing season.\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ] \xc2\xa0Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ] \xc2\xa0LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to the IRS Newswire, an IRS e-mail service.\r\n\r\nIf you know someone who might want to subscribe to this mailing list, please forward this message to them so they can subscribe [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ].\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically from the mailing list IRS Newswire. *Please Do Not Reply To This Message.*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNews Essentials\r\n\r\nWhat's Hot [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/whats-hot ]\r\n\r\nNews Releases [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\nIRS - The Basics [ https://www.irs.gov/about-irs/irs-the-basics ]\r\n\r\nIRS Guidance [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/understanding-irs-guidance-a-brief-primer ]\r\n\r\nMedia Contacts [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-media-relations-office-contact-number ]\r\n\r\nFacts & Figures [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nAround The Nation [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/around-the-nation ]\r\n\r\ne-News Subscriptions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe Newsroom Topics\r\n\r\nMultimedia Center [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/multimedia-center ]\r\n\r\nNoticias en Espa\xc3\xb1ol [ https://www.irs.gov/es/spanish/noticias-en-espanol ]\r\n\r\nRadio PSAs [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-radio-psas ]\r\n\r\nTax Scams [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-scams-consumer-alerts ]\r\n\r\nThe Tax Gap [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/the-tax-gap ]\r\n\r\nFact Sheets [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nIRS Tax Tips [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-tax-tips ]\r\n\r\nArmed Forces [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-information-for-members-of-the-us-armed-forces ]\r\n\r\nLatest News Home [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIRS Resources\r\n\r\nContact My Local Office [ https://www.irs.gov/help/contact-your-local-irs-office ]\r\n\r\nFiling Options [ https://www.irs.gov/filing ]\r\n\r\nForms & Instructions [ https://www.irs.gov/forms-instructions ]\r\n\r\nFrequently Asked Questions [ https://www.irs.gov/help/telephone-assistance ]\r\n\r\nNews [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom ]\r\n\r\nTaxpayer Advocate [ https://www.irs.gov/taxpayer-advocate ]\r\n\r\nWhere to File [ https://www.irs.gov/filing/where-to-file-paper-tax-returns-with-or-without-a-payment ]\r\n\r\nIRS Social Media [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-new-media-1 ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n/*start reset css*/ div { line-height: 1; } body, table, td, p, a, li, blockquote { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; } body { -webkit-text-size-adjust: none; -ms-text-size-adjust: none; } table { border-spacing: 0; } table, td { mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; } img { -ms-interpolation-mode: bicubic; } body { margin: 0; padding: 0; } img { border: none !important; height: auto; line-height: 1; outline: none; text-decoration: none; } table td { border-collapse: collapse !important; } .preheader { display: none !important; visibility: hidden; opacity: 0; color: transparent; height: 0; width: 0; } /*end reset css*/ a[x-apple-data-detectors] { color: inherit !important; text-decoration: none !important; font-size: inherit !important; font-family: inherit !important; font-weight: inherit !important; line-height: inherit !important; } /* Sets the line height in everything but Outlook */ table#yahoo body, table#yahoo p, table#yahoo .gd_p, table#yahoo p span, table#yahoo li, table#yahoo li span { line-height: 1.4; } /* 