[2026-04-27 10:58:34] Raw text/plain payload: b'Metropolitan statistical areas saw increases in the percentage of adults age 25 and over with a bachelor\xe2\x80\x99s degree or higher.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-gains-educational-attainment.html?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-Year Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-gains-educational-attainment.html?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nCensus Bureau Data Show Large Gains in Educational Attainment in Metropolitan and Micropolitan Statistical Areas\r\n\r\n*JAN. 29, 2026* \xe2\x80\x94 The percentage of adults age 25 and over with a bachelor\xe2\x80\x99s degree or higher increased significantly in metropolitan statistical areas (metro areas), up from 34.2% during the 2015-2019 period to 37.8% during the 2020-2024 period, according to new American Community Survey (ACS) 5-year estimates released today by the U.S. Census Bureau.\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cOver the last five years, we\xe2\x80\x99ve noticed a significant increase in the percentage of adults completing higher education,\xe2\x80\x9d said Erik Hernandez, a Census Bureau statistician. \xe2\x80\x9cApproximately 89% of metro areas experienced an increase in the percentage of population 25 years and over with a bachelor\xe2\x80\x99s degree or higher when compared to the 2015-2019 period.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\n"Continue reading for more data on educational attainment, income, poverty, households and families, and more.\xc2\xa0"\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-gains-educational-attainment.html?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\nGray Divider \r\n\r\n?? New on America Counts\r\n\r\nAmerica Counts: Rental Costs Up, Mortgages Stayed Flat [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nNew 2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-year estimates are now available. Explore highlights in three new stories on America Counts.\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Rental Costs Up, Mortgages Stayed Flat [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/housing-costs.html?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * How Income Varies by Race and Geography [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/household-income-by-race-and-state.html?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * Share of Owner-Occupied, Mortgage-Free Homes Up in 2024 [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/mortgage-free-homes.html?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHelp us spread the word about Census Bureau data!\r\n\r\nShare this on social media or forward it to a friend.\r\n\r\n*Share This* [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/406a65d ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n?? You May Be Interested In\r\n\r\n  * Press Kit: 2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-Year Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-kits/2026/acs-5-year-estimates.html?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nWe serve as the nation\xe2\x80\x99s leading provider of quality data about its people and economy.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau is the federal government\'s largest statistical agency. As the world\xe2\x80\x99s premier statistical agency, we are dedicated to making our nation a better place. Policy-makers, businesses, and the public use our data to make informed decisions.\r\n\r\nResources for Media\r\n\r\nFor media interviews, please contact the\xc2\xa0Public Information Office [ https://lnks.gd/l/eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..p-5wpj2DTx0_qgyLiv6JuMTDOF_vZlHcwFpt971jIDs/s/866068797/br/124287751808-l?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Toll Free at 877-861-2010, 301-763-3030, or\xc2\xa0pio@census.gov.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n*Stay connected with us!*\r\n\r\nJoin the conversation on social media.\r\n\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nSubscriber Settings [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Remove me from All Subscriptions  [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n&lt;!-- /* template top padding on mobile */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { table#flexible-abe-main-table { padding:0 !important; } } --&gt; ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260129pios1&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
