[2026-04-27 10:58:38] Raw text/plain payload: b'Blue Acres Banner \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nBlue Acres Bulletin - January 2026\r\n\r\n*In this issue:*\r\n\r\n  * New State Funding Allocated for Buyouts [ #link_1 ] \r\n  * Blue Acres: a National Model for Flood Resilience [ #link_3 ] \r\n  * Regional Flood Resilience Planning Projects Announced - More Funding Coming Soon! [ #link_4 ] \r\n  * State Funds and Local Partnership Critical to Blue Acres Success, per Georgetown Climate Center Release [ #link_5 ] \r\nSection Divider  \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNew State Funding Allocated for Buyouts\r\n\r\napproval \r\n\r\nOn December 23, 2025,\xc2\xa0Bill A6275 [ https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fwww.njleg.state.nj.us*2Fbill-search*2F2024*2FA6275*3Futm_medium=email*26utm_source=govdelivery/1/0101019c09ed2466-a28532f9-cb71-49f9-8c3e-90329193fe01-000000/zz14WRNCV1hlL03QadKV61TS2cbFCe-v0abb4C4JvzY=442__;JSUlJSUlJQ!!J30X0ZrnC1oQtbA!OorwpSeZ4rUY0L4PmtUGRZm82-GpD0gUh9kKtuzftP9oeMSzQPejOAg7TFoSvUuPQTApBOy_eA9-o1acAKWBG1vAn6eJO5s%24?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] was signed by Governor Murphy appropriating $44.4 million to DEP for State acquisition of lands for recreation and conservation, including over $21 million for Blue Acres voluntary flood buyouts.\xc2\xa0 Historically, Blue Acres has been funded primarily through Federal grants, but in the past two years, there have been substantial state allocations. State funding enables\xc2\xa0buyouts\xc2\xa0to\xc2\xa0proceed\xc2\xa0with increased flexibility and speed,\xc2\xa0and\xc2\xa0more directly\xc2\xa0meet the needs of New Jersey homeowners that experience repetitive flooding. These funds come from dedicated Corporate Business Tax revenues and are disbursed through the Garden State Preservation Trust Fund.\r\n\r\nBlue Acres continues to accept voluntary buyout applications from interested homeowners on a rolling basis. For buyout details, FAQs, and to apply, visit\xc2\xa0dep.nj.gov/blueacres [ https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fdep.nj.gov*2Fblueacres*2F*3Futm_medium=email*26utm_source=govdelivery/1/0101019c09ed2466-a28532f9-cb71-49f9-8c3e-90329193fe01-000000/CElrF-X-f73QV9_oVQ-2t_xDp8MnL58xLjROF1FwYJ0=442__;JSUlJSUl!!J30X0ZrnC1oQtbA!OorwpSeZ4rUY0L4PmtUGRZm82-GpD0gUh9kKtuzftP9oeMSzQPejOAg7TFoSvUuPQTApBOy_eA9-o1acAKWBG1vAi0g2AUk%24?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nBlue Acres: a National Model for Flood Resilience\r\n\r\nRecently featured in\xc2\xa0Inside Climate News [ https://insideclimatenews.org/news/25122025/new-jersey-flood-prone-homes-buyout-program/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ],\xc2\xa0Blue Acres continues to serve as a national model for transforming flood-prone properties into resilient landscapes\xc2\xa0while\xc2\xa0giving flood-impacted homeowners a fresh start. Since\xc2\xa0our\xc2\xa0inception\xc2\xa0in 1995,\xc2\xa0Blue Acres\xc2\xa0has\xc2\xa0acquired\xc2\xa0and demolished approximately 1,200\xc2\xa0flood-damaged\xc2\xa0properties, converting them into\xc2\xa0natural flood storage and public open space.\xc2\xa0The article highlights Blue Acres\xe2\x80\x99 streamlined funding,\xc2\xa0municipal engagement, and supportive approach to\xc2\xa0assisting\xc2\xa0homeowners through difficult transitions.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nBlue Acres continues to\xc2\xa0provide a critical mitigation option for NJ homeowners\xc2\xa0facing repetitive flood loss. Read the full article to discover how Blue Acres has combined innovative funding, coordination with local leadership,\xc2\xa0and a homeowner-first approach to help New Jersey build stronger, more flood-resilient communities.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nICN Blue Acres Cover\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nRegional Flood Resilience Planning Projects Announced - More Funding Coming Soon!\r\n\r\nResilient NJ [ https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fdep.nj.gov*2Focr*2Fresilientnj*2F*3Futm_medium=email*26utm_source=govdelivery/1/0101019c09ed2466-a28532f9-cb71-49f9-8c3e-90329193fe01-000000/rTwhVl7azlo1OuwDkE_gTAXEdbFELqvQghrl44Iieu4=442__;JSUlJSUlJQ!!J30X0ZrnC1oQtbA!OorwpSeZ4rUY0L4PmtUGRZm82-GpD0gUh9kKtuzftP9oeMSzQPejOAg7TFoSvUuPQTApBOy_eA9-o1acAKWBG1vAHk-YF-M%24?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ],\xc2\xa0the state\xe2\x80\x99s flagship planning and technical assistance\xc2\xa0program,\xc2\xa0has selected two new regional resilience planning projects for 2026. With support from DEP and experienced consultant teams, the selected regions will develop a community-led comprehensive resilience action plan to address current and increasing impacts from climate change. Montclair Township will lead seven other municipalities and Essex County in creating a regional resilience action plan that addresses stormwater management, climate adaptation, and water-quality restoration strategies\xc2\xa0within the Lower Passaic River Region. In Monmouth County [ https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fwww.tapinto.net*2Ftowns*2Fmiddletown*2Farticles*2Fmonmouth-county-awarded-a-resilient-nj-grant-for-shark-river-basin-and-the-surrounding-area*3Futm_medium=email*26utm_source=govdelivery/1/0101019c09ed2466-a28532f9-cb71-49f9-8c3e-90329193fe01-000000/8kPea9h4olaRMrXyST1Q29SW3QvZTOVp5yvizp2A_tA=442__;JSUlJSUlJSU!!J30X0ZrnC1oQtbA!OorwpSeZ4rUY0L4PmtUGRZm82-GpD0gUh9kKtuzftP9oeMSzQPejOAg7TFoSvUuPQTApBOy_eA9-o1acAKWBG1vArtj34x4%24?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], a County-led climate resilience planning study will focus on the Shark River Basin, in partnership with five municipalities and several community organizations. The resulting climate resilience action plan will assess anticipated climate-driven flood and storm damages and identify viable strategies to protect environmental, economic, and private assets in the study area.\r\n\r\nResilient NJ supports local resilience planning by providing resources, direct technical assistance, and funding. Early this year, the program will open grant applications so that additional teams (each of which must include at least three contiguous municipalities and one community-based organization) may be awarded up to $300,000 each to improve climate resilience. Selected teams will be matched with a multidisciplinary team of experienced contractors to aid in the development of a regional resilience action plan. Keep an eye on the Resilient NJ website [ https://dep.nj.gov/ocr/resilientnj/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#:~:text=Application%20Resources ]\xc2\xa0for the coming open application period!\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nState Funds and Local Partnership Critical to Blue Acres Success, per Georgetown Climate Center Release\r\n\r\nIn December 2025,\xc2\xa0Georgetown Climate Center [ https://www.georgetownclimate.org/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0(GCC) highlighted Blue Acres in the first issue of its new\xc2\xa0Adaptation Policy in Practice\xc2\xa0series [ https://www.georgetownclimate.org/articles/adaptation-policy-in-practice-blue-acres.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], which\xc2\xa0explores\xc2\xa0innovative\xc2\xa0state-level climate adaptation initiatives. The brief [ https://www.georgetownclimate.org/files/GCC_APP_Blue_Acres.pdf?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] examines nationwide challenges in addressing flood risk and outlines Federal programs and their limitations, which can delay and restrict assistance.\xc2\xa0Blue Acres\xe2\x80\x99 success, Adaptation Program Director Joshua Saks writes, lies in the combination of strategically\xc2\xa0utilizing\xc2\xa0State funds\xc2\xa0and treating buyouts as partnerships with local governments.\xc2\xa0The brief\xc2\xa0also\xc2\xa0includes a framework and suggestions for other states looking to emulate the Blue Acres program model.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nWishing you a happy, healthy, resilient 2026!\r\n2026\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the DEP Blue Acres program\r\n\r\nBlue Acres [ http://www.dep.nj.gov/blueacres?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0safeguards public safety and the environment by relocating flood-affected New Jersey families and acquiring land for flood storage, parks, and open space. Our *two core missions: *\r\n\r\n*Disaster Recovery:* Assisting New Jersey residents affected by flooding events, such as those impacted by Tropical Storm Ida in September 2021; *Preparedness:* Contributing to New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s Climate Change Resilience Strategy by strategically acquiring lands damaged or prone to future damage due to sea-level rise, storms, or flooding, enhancing community resilience.\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the DEP Office of Climate Resilience\r\n\r\nThe Office of Climate Resilience (OCR) at NJDEP helps New Jersey communities make informed decisions about climate resilience. Learn more about resilience resources, tools, and core programs run by OCR using the links below and keep an eye out for additional content in future NJDEP Weekly Updates!\r\n\r\n\r\n  * "Resilient NJ [ http://resilient.nj.gov/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]" \r\n  * "Blue Acres [ https://dep.nj.gov/blueacres/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]" \r\n  * "The Interagency Council on Climate Resilience [ https://www.nj.gov/dep/climatechange/resilience-council.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0" \r\n  * "NJ Coastal Management Program [ https://nj.gov/dep/cmp/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]" \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nSection Divider\r\nContact Blue Acres\r\n\r\n"DEP Blue Acres helps New Jersey residents and communities identify and avoid risks of flooding through strategic climate resilience planning and the state-led acquisition of flood-prone property."\r\n\r\nEmail: **BlueAcres@dep.nj.gov\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0**Phone: **(609) 940-4140** \r\nSection Divider  \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n"The New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection is dedicated to protecting New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s environment and public health. The agency prioritizes addressing climate change, protecting New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s water, revitalizing its communities and managing and promoting its natural and historic resources."\r\n\r\n"For the most recent information, follow the DEP on Twitter @NewJerseyDEP [ https:/www.twitter.com/NewJerseyDEP?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Facebook @newjerseydep, Instagram @nj.dep, and LinkedIn @newjerseydep, or visit dep.nj.gov [ https://dep.nj.gov/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]."\r\n\r\n Like and Follow DEP*\r\n*Facebook [ https://www.nj.gov/dep/facebook.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Twitter-X [ https://twitter.com/NewJerseyDEP?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0LinkedIn [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/nj-department-of-environmental-protection/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&viewAsMember=true ]\xc2\xa0Instagram [ https://www.nj.gov/dep/instagram.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] YouTube [ https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC2C01lO4mVInYzqqwevFvSw?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nManage Preferences [ http://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n"\xc2\xa0"\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection \xc2\xb7 401 E. State St. \xc2\xb7 Trenton, NJ 08625 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
