[2026-04-27 10:59:04] Raw text/plain payload: b'Also in this issue: why we need standards  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nn i s t  \r\n \r\n\r\nView as a Web Page [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/bulletins/405c910 ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\ntech beat  \r\nA biweekly news digest from the\r\nNational Institute of Standards and Technology\r\n \r\n\r\nJANUARY 29, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n   [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/disaster-preparedness-how-measurement-science-can-help-your-community ]\r\n\r\nDisaster Preparedness: How Measurement Science Can Help Your Community\r\n\r\nFirsthand experience with natural disasters inspired a NIST researcher to study how communities can prepare for \xe2\x80\x94 and recover from \xe2\x80\x94 disasters.\r\n\r\nREAD MORE [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/disaster-preparedness-how-measurement-science-can-help-your-community ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nMelissa Phillips, wearing safety glasses, poses leaning over an open chest freezer, holding a plastic bag of spinach.  [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/nists-most-popular-reference-materials-and-what-they-tell-us-about-science ] \r\n\r\nNIST\xe2\x80\x99s Most Popular Reference Materials and What They Tell Us About the Science of Measurement\r\n\r\nNIST develops and sells more than 1,300 standard reference materials that are critical to conducting scientific research and supporting American industry.\r\n\r\nREAD MORE [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/nists-most-popular-reference-materials-and-what-they-tell-us-about-science ]\r\n  \r\nClose-up of round dial of a grocery store scale with out-of-focus grocery workers in the background. [ https://www.nist.gov/nist-work ] \r\n \r\n\r\nNIST Works for You\r\n\r\nWhether it\xe2\x80\x99s fair food pricing, improved cybersecurity, or safe medical imaging, NIST\xe2\x80\x99s experts are working for you every day.\r\n\r\nREAD MORE [ https://www.nist.gov/nist-work ]\r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n\r\nPaper  \r\nMORE NEWS FROM NIST\r\n \r\n\r\nScientists Can Now Measure Laser Power Using HALO [ https://www.nist.gov/news-events/news/2026/01/spotlight-scientists-can-measure-laser-power-using-halo ]\r\n\r\nA new device developed by NIST scientists proved to be even more sensitive than they realized, as shown by some unexpected results.\r\n\r\nSpotlight: Electromagnetic Proton Trap at the NIST Center for Neutron Research (NCNR) [ https://www.nist.gov/news-events/news/2026/01/spotlight-electromagnetic-proton-trap-nist-center-neutron-research-ncnr ]\r\n\r\nJust how long do free-floating neutrons live on average? This experiment at the NCNR is part of an effort to answer that question.\r\n\r\n  \r\n Colorful photo collage includes tape measure, Kibble balance, gas can, grapes, scale. [ https://www.nist.gov/feature-stories/why-you-need-standards ]\r\n\r\nWhen we talk about having standards in our personal lives, we might think about the quality we expect at restaurants or on first dates. But the standards that exist in science and technology have an even greater impact on our lives. Read more about why we need standards. [ https://www.nist.gov/feature-stories/why-you-need-standards ]\r\n\r\n \r\nFor Good Measure\r\n\r\nGood measurements and standards are critical for all areas of science and technology, so it\xe2\x80\x99s no surprise that NIST\xe2\x80\x99s work covers an ultrawide breadth of topics. A new place to sample our agency\xe2\x80\x99s range of subject areas is our NIST Works for You [ https://www.nist.gov/nist-work?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_id=techbeat_01292026&utm_content=editor_note ] section, which includes such topics as next-generation MRIs, fair fuel transactions and nuclear security. Another way to see the variety of NIST activity is through our blog post on our most popular reference materials [ https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/nists-most-popular-reference-materials-and-what-they-tell-us-about-science?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_id=techbeat_01292026&utm_content=editor_note ], from Charpy steel bars to engineered antibodies. To learn more about how standards tie all this work together, check out our feature story on why we need standards [ https://www.nist.gov/feature-stories/why-you-need-standards?utm_source=govdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_id=techbeat_01292026&utm_content=editor_note ].\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x94Ben P. Stein, Managing Editor\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nConnect with us\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/NIST ]X [ https://twitter.com/NIST ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/NIST ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/nist ]flickr [ https://www.instagram.com/nist/ ]  \r\n\r\nReceived this email from a friend? Subscribe here [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/new?topic_id=USNIST_1 ].\r\n\r\nPrivacy Policy [ https://www.nist.gov/privacy-policy#privpolicy ]\r\n\r\n NIST [ http://www.nist.gov/ ] \r\n\r\n*You are subscribed to receive updates from the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST).*\r\n\r\n*Subscriber services:*\r\n\r\n*Manage Preferences [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIf you have questions or problems with the subscription service, please contact subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ].\r\nTechnical questions? Contact inquiries@nist.gov. (301) 975-NIST (6478).\r\n\r\nThis service is provided to you at no charge by National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST).\xc2\xa0100 Bureau Drive, Stop 1070\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7 Gaithersburg, MD 20899\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0301-975-6478\r\n\r\n GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
