[2026-04-27 10:59:33] Raw text/plain payload: b"Bookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/bulletins/406b03d?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nIRS.gov Banner \r\n\r\nIRS Newswire\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nJanuary 29, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nIssue Number:\xc2\xa0 IR-2026-18\r\n\r\nInside This Issue\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*IRS requests applications for 2026 ETAAC membership*\r\n\r\nIR-2026-18, Jan. 29, 2026\r\n\r\nWASHINGTON \xe2\x80\x94 The Internal Revenue Service is accepting applications for the\xc2\xa0Electronic Tax Administration Advisory Committee [ https://www.irs.gov/tax-professionals/electronic-tax-administration-advisory-committee-etaac ]\xc2\xa0through Feb. 28, 2026.\r\n\r\nThe ETAAC is an organized public forum for discussing issues in electronic tax administration, such as the prevention of identity theft and refund fraud. The committee supports the overriding goal that paperless filing should be the preferred and most convenient method of filing tax and information returns.\r\n\r\nETAAC members work closely with the\xc2\xa0Security Summit [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/security-summit ], a joint effort of the IRS, state tax administrators, and private-sector tax partners to fight electronic fraud and tax-related identity theft.\r\n\r\nThe IRS is seeking qualified individuals to serve three-year terms, beginning in September 2026. Applicants should have experience in areas such as state tax administration, cybersecurity and information security, tax software development, tax preparation, payroll and tax financial product processing, systems management and improvement, and implementing customer service initiatives. The IRS also strongly encourages applications from people representing the viewpoints of average taxpayers, including consumer advocates and others with an interest in tax issues.\r\n\r\nNominations of qualified individuals may be made by letter and received from organizations or the individuals themselves. Applicants need to complete the\xc2\xa0ETAAC application\xc2\xa0 [ https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-pdf/f13768.pdf ]and include a statement of interest and a resume. Applicants should describe and document their qualifications, including past and current affiliations, as well as their experience with cybersecurity and electronic tax administration.\r\n\r\nApplicants must complete and submit a tax check waiver form and undergo an IRS practitioner background check. Applicants deemed \xe2\x80\x9cbest qualified\xe2\x80\x9d will also undergo an FBI background check. Information on the tax check waiver will be provided upon receipt of the application.\r\n\r\nETAAC is a Federal Advisory Committee established by the Internal Revenue Service Restructuring and Reform Act of 1998.\r\n\r\nQuestions about the ETAAC and the application process can be emailed to\xc2\xa0publicliaison@irs.gov.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ] \xc2\xa0Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ] \xc2\xa0LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to the IRS Newswire, an IRS e-mail service.\r\n\r\nIf you know someone who might want to subscribe to this mailing list, please forward this message to them so they can subscribe [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ].\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically from the mailing list IRS Newswire. *Please Do Not Reply To This Message.*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNews Essentials\r\n\r\nWhat's Hot [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/whats-hot ]\r\n\r\nNews Releases [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\nIRS - The Basics [ https://www.irs.gov/about-irs/irs-the-basics ]\r\n\r\nIRS Guidance [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/understanding-irs-guidance-a-brief-primer ]\r\n\r\nMedia Contacts [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-media-relations-office-contact-number ]\r\n\r\nFacts & Figures [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nAround The Nation [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/around-the-nation ]\r\n\r\ne-News Subscriptions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe Newsroom Topics\r\n\r\nMultimedia Center [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/multimedia-center ]\r\n\r\nNoticias en Espa\xc3\xb1ol [ https://www.irs.gov/es/spanish/noticias-en-espanol ]\r\n\r\nRadio PSAs [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-radio-psas ]\r\n\r\nTax Scams [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-scams-consumer-alerts ]\r\n\r\nThe Tax Gap [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/the-tax-gap ]\r\n\r\nFact Sheets [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nIRS Tax Tips [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-tax-tips ]\r\n\r\nArmed Forces [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-information-for-members-of-the-us-armed-forces ]\r\n\r\nLatest News Home [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIRS Resources\r\n\r\nContact My Local Office [ https://www.irs.gov/help/contact-your-local-irs-office ]\r\n\r\nFiling Options [ https://www.irs.gov/filing ]\r\n\r\nForms & Instructions [ https://www.irs.gov/forms-instructions ]\r\n\r\nFrequently Asked Questions [ https://www.irs.gov/help/telephone-assistance ]\r\n\r\nNews [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom ]\r\n\r\nTaxpayer Advocate [ https://www.irs.gov/taxpayer-advocate ]\r\n\r\nWhere to File [ https://www.irs.gov/filing/where-to-file-paper-tax-returns-with-or-without-a-payment ]\r\n\r\nIRS Social Media [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-new-media-1 ]\r\n\r\n____________________________________________________________________