[2026-04-27 11:01:42] Raw text/plain payload: b'NJDEP Logo \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNJDEP Grants and Loans Updates\r\n\r\nWelcome to the latest New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection\xe2\x80\x99s (NJDEP)\xc2\xa0Grants\xc2\xa0and\xc2\xa0Loans update.\r\n\r\nYou can learn more about all the NJDEP\xe2\x80\x99s grant\xc2\xa0and\xc2\xa0loan\xc2\xa0programs\xc2\xa0and\xc2\xa0find resources\xc2\xa0here [ https://dep.nj.gov/grantandloanprograms/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\nFreshwater Wetlands Mitigation Council RFP [ https://dep.nj.gov/wlm/mitigation/wetlands-mitigation-council/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nFreshwater Wetlands Mitigation Council RFP [ https://dep.nj.gov/wlm/mitigation/wetlands-mitigation-council/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nThe Freshwater Wetlands Mitigation Council will be re-releasing an RFP late February. The Freshwater Wetlands Mitigation Council Grant Program provides funding for projects focused on the creation, restoration, or enhancement of wetlands.\xc2\xa0 The Wetland Mitigation Fund is broken up by water regions which consists of 5 regions: Atlantic, Raritan, Lower Delaware, Upper Delaware, and Northeast. Eligible applicants include nonprofit organizations, county, state, and federal agencies, and other appropriate organizations.\xc2\xa0Current RFP\xe2\x80\x99s will be posted to the Council\xe2\x80\x99s website at dep.nj.gov/wlm/mitigation/wetlands-mitigation-council/ [ https://dep.nj.gov/wlm/mitigation/wetlands-mitigation-council/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nElectric School Bus Grant Program [ https://dep.nj.gov/stopthesoot/electric-school-bus-program/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nElectric School Bus Grant Program [ https://dep.nj.gov/stopthesoot/electric-school-bus-program/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nRound 3 of the Electric School Bus Grant is expected to open this summer. The Electric School Bus Grant Program supports the statewide transition from fossil fuel-powered to electric school buses, aiming to reduce emissions and improve public health, especially for students and residents of the communities in which school buses operate. With more than 99% of New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s 21,700 school buses currently running on fossil fuels, this program promotes cleaner alternatives by offering grants to eligible applicants. School districts that own their own buses, as well as school bus contractors (in partnership with specific schools or districts), may apply. A single school bus contractor may apply in conjunction with multiple schools or school districts, although they must submit a separate application for each individual school or school district they are applying with.\r\n\r\nIn each year of funding, at least half of those selected for award must operate within an Overburdened Community, and selections aim for geographic balance across northern, central, and southern regions of the state.\r\n\r\nA total of three yearly rounds were authorized and are dependent upon funding availability. For details on past Rounds 1 and 2 of the program, including recorded webinars and links to various resources, visit https://dep.nj.gov/stopthesoot/electric-school-bus-program/ [ https://dep.nj.gov/stopthesoot/electric-school-bus-program/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nResilient NJ: Regional Assistance Program- Regional Planning Grants [ https://dep.nj.gov/ocr/resilientnj/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nResilient NJ: Regional Assistance Program- Regional Planning Grants [ https://dep.nj.gov/ocr/resilientnj/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nGrant applications for The Resilient NJ: Regional Assistance Program \xe2\x80\x93 Regional Planning Grants will be available in early 2026. The Resilient NJ: Regional Assistance Program \xe2\x80\x93 Regional Planning Grants provides funding to local government entities to support collaborative regional planning efforts that result in regional resilience action plans. These plans are designed to increase resilience, build local capacity, and enable local governments to address their unique needs while also protecting the ecological, economic, recreational, and natural resources within their communities.\r\n\r\nThe program\xe2\x80\x99s purpose is to support regions and municipalities shape the future of their community character and vision by strengthening the region\xe2\x80\x99s understanding of climate change impacts based on the best available data and science, and using innovative and transformational strategies, design standards, and solutions to address those impacts. The program structure has been established to alleviate capacity constraints often cited by local governments, particularly related to the administrative burdens of complying with state contract and federal funding requirements.\r\n\r\nThis collaborative opportunity calls for local government entities to self-organize into a regional team of at least 3 local governments with adjacent or overlapping administrative boundaries, and 1 or more community-based organizations. With the assistance of dynamic multi-disciplinary Consultant Teams of planners, engineers, ecologists, designers, and other experts (selected through a separate opportunity), the regional team will work together to address climate-related hazards at a regional scale, where through a community-drive process they will develop and implement resilience actions to reduce risk and increase the region\xe2\x80\x99s overall resilience in the short-, mid-, and long term. The products that are created throughout the project period are meant to support the planning and decision-making of the region and are based on the region\xe2\x80\x99s goals, vision, and preferences, within the guidelines of the Resilient NJ program requirements. Action plans may also support successful applications for other state and federal grant opportunities.\r\n\r\nThe Resilient NJ: Regional Planning Grants are selected and awarded based on criteria set forth by DEP and funding source requirements. For more information on available opportunities, please visit dep.nj.gov/ocr/resilientnj. [ https://dep.nj.gov/ocr/resilientnj/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nOther State Agencies\r\n\r\nGMO Logo [ https://www.nj.gov/treasury/grants-management/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nThe New Jersey Treasury\'s Grants Management Office [ https://www.nj.gov/treasury/grants-management/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] has identified a new tool that automates the discovery and identification of federal grant opportunities for our stakeholders. The US Digital Response\xe2\x80\x99s Federal Grant Finder is a free software that enables organizations to optimize federal funding opportunities through advanced search and collaboration tools to help organizations like yours uncover and pursue more opportunities than ever before.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Grant Name*\r\n \r\n*Deadline*\r\n \r\n\r\nGreen Acres Local & Nonprofit Program [ https://dep.nj.gov/grantandloanprograms/green-acres-local-and-nonprofit-program/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nFebruary 27, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nHistoric Preservation Certified Local Government Grants  [ https://dep.nj.gov/grantandloanprograms/historic-preservation-certified-local-government-grants/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nMarch 31, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSolid Waste Recycling Enhancement Act (REA) Higher Education Research Grant Program [ https://dep.nj.gov/grantandloanprograms/solid-waste-recycling-enhancement-act-rea-higher-education-research-grant-program/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nApril 24, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nYouth Inclusion Initiative [ https://dep.nj.gov/grantandloanprograms/youth-inclusion-initiative/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nMarch 12, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nNJDEP also has\xc2\xa0numerous\xc2\xa0grants that are available on a rolling basis. Check the Grant and Loan Programs website for the latest information on all available grants.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Explore All Grants and Loans* [ https://dep.nj.gov/grantandloanprograms/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nGet in Touch\r\n\r\nEmail Icon  \r\n\r\nHave a question about the NJDEP\'s funding opportunities?\r\n\r\nReach out to the Uniting Financial Resources team at\xc2\xa0unitingfinancialresources@dep.nj.gov.\r\n\r\n"The Uniting Financial Resources team is housed under the NJDEP\'s Community Investment & Economic Revitalization program area."\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n"The New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection is dedicated to protecting New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s environment and public health. The agency prioritizes addressing climate change, protecting New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s water, revitalizing its communities and managing and promoting its natural and historic resources."\r\n\r\n"For the most recent information, follow the DEP on Twitter @NewJerseyDEP [ https:/www.twitter.com/NewJerseyDEP?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Facebook @newjerseydep, Instagram @nj.dep, and LinkedIn @newjerseydep, or visit dep.nj.gov [ https://dep.nj.gov/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]."\r\n\r\n Like and Follow DEP*\r\n*Facebook [ https://www.nj.gov/dep/facebook.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Twitter-X [ https://twitter.com/NewJerseyDEP?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0LinkedIn [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/nj-department-of-environmental-protection/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&viewAsMember=true ]\xc2\xa0Instagram [ https://www.nj.gov/dep/instagram.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] YouTube [ https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC2C01lO4mVInYzqqwevFvSw?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nManage Preferences [ http://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n"\xc2\xa0"\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection \xc2\xb7 401 E. State St. \xc2\xb7 Trenton, NJ 08625 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
