[2026-04-27 11:02:23] Raw text/plain payload: b"Bookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/bulletins/406d342?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nIRS.gov Banner \r\n\r\nIRS Newswire\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nJanuary 30, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nIssue Number:\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 IR-2026-19\r\n\r\nInside This Issue\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nWASHINGTON \xe2\x80\x94 The Internal Revenue Service announced today the award of $53 million in Tax Counseling for the Elderly and Volunteer Income Tax Assistance grants to organizations that provide federal tax return preparation at no cost.\r\n\r\nThis year, the IRS awarded grants to 48 TCE and 315 VITA applicants [ https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-wi/2025-tce-vita-grant-recipients.pdf ]. The IRS received 479 applications requesting over $79 million in funding.\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cThese grants ensure that VITA and elderly tax-counseling organizations have sufficient funding to provide assistance to individuals in need at local centers across the nation,\xe2\x80\x9d said Chief Executive Officer Frank J. Bisignano. \xe2\x80\x9cThe IRS recognizes the important work these organizations do and salutes their efforts.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\nThe TCE program, established in 1978, provides no-cost tax counseling and federal return preparation to individuals who are age 60 or older. Volunteers receive training and technical assistance to help at community locations across the nation.\r\n\r\nThe VITA program, created in 1969, assists underserved communities, such as low- and moderate-income individuals and limited English proficient taxpayers. VITA grant recipients provide no-cost federal tax return preparation and electronic filing. The grant program helps to expand VITA services to underserved populations.\r\n\r\nThe IRS maintains partnerships with a wide variety of organizations across the country to develop VITA and TCE programs. Community partners include non-profit agencies, faith-based organizations, community centers and large employers. The IRS provides tax law training, certification and oversight to these organizations, assisting their efforts to prepare accurate returns.\r\n\r\nFor information on applying for the TCE or VITA programs visit Tax Counseling for the Elderly [ https://www.irs.gov/individuals/tax-counseling-for-the-elderly ] or IRS VITA Grant Program [ https://www.irs.gov/individuals/irs-vita-grant-program ] on IRS.gov. A current list of grant recipients will be available on these pages beginning January 31, 2026. For details on becoming a TCE or VITA volunteer, visit IRS Tax Volunteers [ https://www.irs.gov/individuals/irs-tax-volunteers ].\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ] \xc2\xa0Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ] \xc2\xa0LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to the IRS Newswire, an IRS e-mail service.\r\n\r\nIf you know someone who might want to subscribe to this mailing list, please forward this message to them so they can subscribe [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ].\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically from the mailing list IRS Newswire. *Please Do Not Reply To This Message.*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNews Essentials\r\n\r\nWhat's Hot [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/whats-hot ]\r\n\r\nNews Releases [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\nIRS - The Basics [ https://www.irs.gov/about-irs/irs-the-basics ]\r\n\r\nIRS Guidance [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/understanding-irs-guidance-a-brief-primer ]\r\n\r\nMedia Contacts [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-med