ls [ https://www.irs.gov/tax-professionals ]\r\n\r\nForms, Instructions & Publications [ https://www.irs.gov/forms-instructions ]\r\n\r\nQuickAlerts Article [ https://www.irs.gov/e-file-providers/quickalerts-more-e-file-benefits-for-tax-professionals ]\r\n\r\nQuickAlerts Brochure [ https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-pdf/p4003.pdf ]\r\n\r\ne-file for Tax Pros [ https://www.irs.gov/e-file-providers/efile-for-tax-professionals ]\r\n\r\ne-Services [ https://www.irs.gov/tax-professionals/e-services-online-tools-for-tax-professionals ]\r\n\r\nSoftware Developers [ https://www.irs.gov/e-file-providers/modernized-e-file-overview ]\r\n\r\nIRS.gov [ https://www.irs.gov/ ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Subject: *Information Returns Intake System (IRIS) Working Group Meeting\r\n\r\n*Attention:* Software Developers and Information Return Transmitters\r\n\r\nPlease join us for an Information Returns Intake System (IRIS) Working Group Meeting. This meeting is intended for software developers, transmitters, and state participants who are interested in or currently using the IRIS system.\r\n\r\nThe purpose of the meeting is to share IRIS-related information to help users avoid common filing errors, address known issues and available workarounds, and highlight important filing dates and deadlines. We encourage all interested participants to attend.\r\n\r\n*Information Returns Intake System (IRIS) Working Group Meeting [ https://events.gcc.teams.microsoft.com/event/816da9d2-bca4-4e9e-a0c9-ab3c3986f061@f2372b85-8802-490c-b196-7b96c73fee3b ]*\r\n\r\n*Date:* Wednesday, February 11, 2026\r\n*Time:* 1:00 PM \xe2\x80\x93 2:00 PM Eastern Time\r\n*Location:* Online event\r\n\r\nBack to top [ #top ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ] \xc2\xa0Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ] \xc2\xa0LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to QuickAlerts for Information Returns Intake System (IRIS), an IRS e-mail service.\r\n\r\nIf you have an idea or a question related to QuickAlerts you can contact us by e-mail <QuickAlerts@irs.gov>. Submissions which are not related to QuickAlerts will not be processed. If you have tax related questions you should pursue normal customer service channels provided on\xc2\xa0IRS.gov [ https://www.irs.gov/ ].\r\n\r\nIf you know someone who might want to subscribe to this mailing list, please forward this message to them so they can subscribe [ https://www.irs.gov/e-file-providers/subscribe-to-quick-alerts ].\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically. *Please Do Not Reply To This Message.*\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nUpdate your subscriptions, modify your password or email address, or stop subscriptions at any time on your Subscriber Preferences Page [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ]. You will need your email address to log in. If you have questions or problems with the subscription service, visit subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ].\r\n\r\nThis service is provided to you at no charge by the Internal Revenue Service (IRS) [ https://www.irs.gov/ ].\r\n\r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com by: Internal Revenue Service (IRS) \xc2\xb7 Internal Revenue Service \xc2\xb7 1111 Constitution Ave. N.W. \xc2\xb7 Washington, D.C. 20535 GovDelivery logo [ https: