[2026-04-27 11:03:13] Raw text/plain payload: b'table {border-collapse: collapse;} &lt;!-- /* Make columns expand to 100% on small screens */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { .abe-column-block { min-width: 100%; } } /* Disables Apple clients adding blue color and underline to links and other text */ a[x-apple-data-detectors] { color: inherit !important; text-decoration: none !important; font-size: inherit !important; font-family: inherit !important; font-weight: inherit !important; line-height: inherit !important; } --&gt; \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0 \r\n\r\nFTC Logo [ https://www.ftc.gov?utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nFTC Announces Agenda for Workshop on Informational Injuries [ https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/news/press-releases/2026/01/ftc-announces-agenda-workshop-informational-injuries?utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n"The February 26 event will be held online and in-person with registration required" \r\n\r\nThe Federal Trade Commission announced the agenda [ https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/events/2026/02/consumer-injuries-benefits-data-driven-economy?utm_source=govdelivery ] for its February 26 workshop that will focus on how the agency can better understand and measure consumer injuries and benefits that may result from the collection, use, or disclosure of consumer data.\r\n\r\nView Press Release [ https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/news/press-releases/2026/01/ftc-announces-agenda-workshop-informational-injuries?utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*More news from the FTC* [ https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/news/press-releases?utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\xc2\xa0 \r\nFacebook [ https://www.facebook.com/federaltradecommission?utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nTwitter [ https://twitter.com/FTC?utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nLinkedIn [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/163780?u