[2026-04-27 11:03:24] Raw text/plain payload: b'table {border-collapse: collapse;} &lt;!-- /* Make columns expand to 100% on small screens */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { .abe-column-block { min-width: 100%; } } /* Disables Apple clients adding blue color and underline to links and other text */ a[x-apple-data-detectors] { color: inherit !important; text-decoration: none !important; font-size: inherit !important; font-family: inherit !important; font-weight: inherit !important; line-height: inherit !important; } --&gt; \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0 \r\n\r\nFTC Logo [ https://www.ftc.gov?utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nFTC Submits Draft ANPRM Related to Rental Housing Fees to OMB for Review [ https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/news/press-releases/2026/01/ftc-submits-draft-anprm-related-rental-housing-fees-omb-review?utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nThe Federal Trade Commission announced today that it has submitted an Advance Notice of Proposed Rulemaking (ANPRM) related to fees in the rental housing market for review by the Office of Information and Regulatory Affairs (OIRA) within the Office of Management and Budget. Executive Orders 12866 and 14215 require all executive branch departments and agencies to submit their proposed and final \xe2\x80\x9csignificant regulatory actions\xe2\x80\x9d for review by OIRA. OIRA determined that the planned ANPRM is a \xe2\x80\x9csignificant regulatory action\xe2\x80\x9d and must undergo review before the FTC issues it.\r\n\r\nView Press Release [ https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/news/press-releases/2026/01/ftc-submits-draft-anprm-related-rental-housing-fees-omb-review?utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*More news from the FTC* [ https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/news/press-releases?utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\xc2\xa0 \r\nFacebook [ https://www.facebook.com/federaltradecommission?utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nTwitter [ https://twitter.com/FTC?utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nLinkedIn [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/163780?utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \xc2\xa0 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \xc2\xa0 \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nTo\xc2\xa0update or delete your subscription at any time, visit your\xc2\xa0subscriber preferences page [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFTC/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ]. If you have questions or problems with the subscription service, please contact subscriber support [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/s/?utm_source=govdelivery ].\xc2\xa0This is a free service provided by the\xc2\xa0Federal Trade Commission [ https://www.ftc.gov/?utm_source=govdelivery ].\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: Federal Trade Commission \xc2\xb7 600 Pennsylvania Ave., NW \xc2\xb7 Washington, DC 20580 \xc2\xb7 1-877-382-4357 \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
