[2026-04-27 11:07:08] Raw text/plain payload: b"2026 -4000 Ruble Penguins\r\nUkraine Update February 1\r\n\r\n2026 -4000 Ruble Penguins\r\n\r\nDylan Combellick (https://medium.com/@dylan_combellick?source=email-50207bf5a022-1769932660701-newsletter.subscribeToProfile-------------------------9021112b_9aec_4154_a60d_c2c927358b1e--------354e45830cd6)\r\n\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xe2\x88\x99\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\r\nFebruary 1, 2026\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xe2\x88\x99\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\r\n11 min read\r\n\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xe2\x88\x99\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\r\nView on Medium (https://medium.com/p/adab5ecc53ba?source=email-50207bf5a022-1769932660701-newsletter.subscribeToProfile-------------------------9021112b_9aec_4154_a60d_c2c927358b1e--------354e45830cd6)\r\n\r\nSo Goes the War\r\n\r\nThat was quick work. Russian Telegram channels are reporting that their Starlink devices stop working at speeds above either 90kph or 75kph, depending on the source. The Ukrainian Ministry of Defense contacted SpaceX, which set speed limits on the movement of Starlink devices. I assume that 75/90 kph is below the stall speed of the drones observed using them. Good work, Ministry and SpaceX.\r\n\r\n-\xe2\x80\x8a-\xe2\x80\x8a-\r\n\r\nUnder the cover of snow and fog, Russia attempted an armored assault near Hryshyne, in the Pokrovsk theater of operations. It was met with vigilance and skill by the Ukrainian defenders.\xc2\xa0\xe2\x80\xa6\r\n\r\nContinue reading (https://medium.com/p/adab5ecc53ba?source=email-50207bf5a022-1769932660701-newsletter.subscribeToProfile-------------------------9021112b_9aec_4154_a60d_c2c927358b1e--------354e45830cd6)\r\nThis is a member-only story and can only be read on Medium.\r\n\r\nSent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com by Dylan Combellick on Medium\r\nUnsubscribe (https://medium.com/me/email-settings/50207bf5a022/c1698d269dbe?type=noSetting&newsletterV3Id=354e45830cd6&source=email-50207bf5a022-1769932660701-newsletter.subscribeToProfile-------------------------9021112b_9aec_4154_a60d_c2c927358b1