[2026-04-27 11:07:33] Raw text/plain payload: b'*Cheesequake State Park February 2026 Events!*\r\n\r\nNo pre-registration required\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*Guided Nature Walk*\r\n\r\nSnow Day\r\n\r\n*Saturday, February 7th, 2026 11:00AM-12:30PM*\r\n\r\nDiscover the various ecosystems and winter wildlife of Cheesequake State Park on this 2-mile guided walk. This walk will go over easy, flat terrain. Dogs allowed on a leash!\xc2\xa0 Meet us at the Hooks Creek Lake Day Use Area by the front of the pavilion. Directions: https://maps.app.goo.gl/VFzhjbc6dRKxCVnB6.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Guided Nature Walk*\r\n\r\nSnow in the Park\r\n\r\n*Saturday, February 21st, 2026 11:00AM-12:30PM*\r\n\r\nDiscover the various ecosystems and winter wildlife of Cheesequake State Park on this 2-mile guided walk. This walk will go over easy, flat terrain. Dogs allowed on a leash!\xc2\xa0 Meet us at the Hooks Creek Lake Day Use Area by the front of the pavilion. Directions: https://maps.app.goo.gl/VFzhjbc6dRKxCVnB6.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Please dress for the weather. We recommend bringing water and binoculars! If you have any questions, please call our Nature Center at (732) 566-3208.\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*Visit Our Nature Center!*\r\n\r\nNature Center\r\n\r\nCome visit us at the Nature Center! We have educational displays and activities for visitors of all ages to enjoy. The Nature Center is open Wednesday-Sunday, 9:00AM-4:00PM (as staffing permits). It is accessible by a half mile walk from the trail head parking lot. ADA parking is available directly at the Nature Center.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*About Cheesequake State Park*\r\n\r\nCheesequake State Park \r\n\r\nLocated off of exit 120 form the Garden State Parkway, Cheesequake start park encompasses 1,610 acres. The park offers a large variety of recreational activities from camping, swimming, picnicking, crabbing, biking and over 10 miles of hiking trails. Cheesequake State Park\xe2\x80\x99s uniqueness lies in its geographical location. Not only is it situated in the middle of the urban north and the suburban south, but it also lies in a transitional zone between two different ecosystems. Open fields, saltwater and freshwater marshes, an Atlantic white cedar swamp, pine barrens habitats and a northeastern hardwood forest await you!\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nCheesequake State Park\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n300 Gordon Rd, Matawan NJ 07747\r\n\r\nNature Center: (732) 566-3208\r\n\r\nPark Office: (732) 566-2161\r\n\r\nLike us on Facebook! https://www.facebook.com/cheesequakestatepark [ https://www.facebook.com/cheesequakestatepark?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nhttps://www.state.nj.us/dep/parksandforests/parks/cheesequake.html [ https://www.state.nj.us/dep/parksandforests/parks/cheesequake.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nNew Jersey State Parks Service [ http://www.nj.gov/dep/parksandforests/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nQuestions?\xc2\xa0Contact Us [ http://www.nj.gov/dep/parksandforests/parks/contact_us.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \r\nSign up for email updates [ https://www.facebook.com/NewJerseyStateParks?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  [ https://twitter.com/newjerseydep?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] Follow us on Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/newjerseystateparks/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] Sign up for email updates [ http://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscriber/new ] \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nManage Preferences [ http://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection \xc2\xb7 401 E. State St. \xc2\xb7 Trenton, NJ 08625 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
