[2026-04-27 11:09:03] Raw text/plain payload: b'View this email as a web page [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/bulletins/40746c8 ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNJDEP Logo \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*NJDEP\xc2\xa0*\r\n*Rule Proposal Notice\r\n* \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*NJ DEPARTMENT OF ENVIRONMENTAL PROTECTION*\r\nWATER RESOURCE MANAGEMENT\r\nDIVISION OF WATER SUPPLY & GEOSCIENCE\r\n\r\n*Notice of Rule Proposal*\r\nSAFE DRINKING WATER ACT RULES (N.J.A.C. 7:10)\r\n\r\n*Public Notice*\r\n\r\nTake notice that the New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection (Department) is proposing a new rule and amendments to the Safe Drinking Water Act (SDWA) Rules. This rule proposal is intended to amend the Safe Drinking Water Act (SDWA) rules at N.J.A.C. 7:10, which incorporate by reference the Federal Lead and Copper Rule (Federal Rule), 40 C.F.R. 141, Subpart I, to establish New Jersey-specific requirements for implementation of the Federal Rule. The Department\xe2\x80\x99s proposed rule incorporates recent amendments to the State Safe Drinking Water Act (State Act) concerning lead service lines, notification of lead in drinking water, and drinking water testing for lead and copper (N.J.S.A. 58:12A-40 et seq.; N.J.S.A. 58:12A-12.4 et seq.; and N.J.S.A. 58:12A-12.7 et seq.). In addition, the Department is proposing to amend other provisions throughout N.J.A.C. 7:10 as a result of these new requirements to incorporate recent amendments to the State Act and ensure consistency with changes to the Federal Rule.\r\n\r\nThe Department is proposing new rules at N.J.A.C. 7:10-5.9 in accordance with such amendments to the State Act and the Federal Rule, including but not limited to: service line inventories; lead service line replacement; lead and copper sampling; sampling at schools and child care facilities; sampling and lead service line replacement plans; optimal corrosion control; testing protocols such as sequential monitoring and pipe scale analysis; monitoring for water quality parameters; lead and copper public education; and associated notice requirements.\r\n\r\nThe proposal is scheduled to be published in the New Jersey Register dated February 2, 2026. A copy of the proposal is available from: the Department\xe2\x80\x99s rule website at: https://dep.nj.gov/wp-content/uploads/rules/proposals/proposal-20260202a.pdf [ https://dep.nj.gov/wp-content/uploads/rules/proposals/proposal-20260202a.pdf?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], or in the New Jersey Register at: https://www.nj.gov/oal/rules/accessp/ [ https://www.nj.gov/oal/rules/accessp/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\r\n\r\nA public hearing concerning the proposal is scheduled as follows:\r\n\r\nTuesday, March 10, 2026, at 10:00 AM.\r\nVirtual meeting through the Department\xe2\x80\x99s video conferencing software, Microsoft Teams.\r\n\r\nAttendees should email LeadinDW@dep.nj.gov with their contact information (name, organization, telephone number, and email address) to obtain a meeting link & call-in number.\r\n\r\nWritten comments may be submitted electronically by Friday, April 3, 2026 at https://dep.nj.gov/rules/rule-comment-form/ [ https://dep.nj.gov/rules/rule-comment-form/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], or in hard copy to:\r\n\r\nStephanie J. Press, Esq.\r\nATTN: DEP Docket No. 11-25-12\r\nNJ Department of Environmental Protection\r\nOffice of Legal Affairs\r\nMail Code 401-04L; PO Box 402\r\n401 East State Street, 7th Floor\r\nTrenton, NJ 08625-0402\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nQuestions?\xc2\xa0Contact Us [ https://www.nj.gov/cgi-bin/dep/contactdep.pl?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \r\nFacebook [ https://www.nj.gov/dep/facebook.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] Twitter-X LinkedIn Instagram [ https://www.nj.gov/dep/instagram.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nManage Preferences [ http://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection \xc2\xb7 401 E. State St. \xc2\xb7 Trenton, NJ 08625 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
