[2026-04-27 11:09:58] Raw text/plain payload: b'February 10, 2026 | 1-2:30pm ET  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nNIST FISSEA logo \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nThe Human Firewall \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nFISSEA Winter Forum\r\n\r\nFebruary 10, 2026 | 1:00 pm - 2:30 pm ET\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*Annual Theme: Increasing Cybersecurity Awareness: The Human Firewall *Human behavior is key to developing cybersecurity awareness and training programs. This year\'s FISSEA theme focuses on humans at the center of education and training, including how humans can leverage emerging technologies to strengthen their efforts.\r\n\r\n*Agenda Announced!*\r\n\r\nThe 2026 FISSEA Winter Forum will feature an exciting lineup of speakers who will help us dive deep into the "Human Firewall." From the psychology of language to the power of AI, the Winter Forum will be packed with actionable insights to inform awareness and training programs.\r\n\r\nAgenda topics include:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * *Collaborative Discussion on Awareness Activities:* share and discover what\xe2\x80\x99s actually working in the field today! \r\n  * *Research on Common Cybersecurity Terms*: insights to help inform security professionals on how to better communicate security concepts. \r\n  * *Teaching Cyber Risk to Build Confidence*: how to transform "check-the-box" training into true "data trust." \r\n  * *Field-Tested Tactics:* practical methods for using generative tools to build more effective cybersecurity assessments. \r\n\r\nView the full agenda and register here [ https://www.nist.gov/news-events/events/2026/02/fissea-winter-forum-february-10-2026 ].\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Stay involved year-round:*\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Find us on social media by searching for #FISSEA \r\n  * Submit a proposal for an opportunity to speak at an upcoming FISSEA event. Learn more here [ https://survey.nist.gov/jfe/form/SV_dmy6dxR2mPY4udU ].\xc2\xa0 \r\n\r\nOn behalf of the FISSEA Planning Committee, we\xc2\xa0truly thank you for your continued support with FISSEA and look forward to having you join us at the\xc2\xa0FISSEA Winter Forum\xc2\xa0on\xc2\xa0February 10,\xc2\xa02026.\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nConnect with us\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/NIST ]X [ https://twitter.com/NIST ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/NIST ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/nist ]flickr [ https://www.instagram.com/nist/ ]  \r\n\r\nReceived this email from a friend? Subscribe here [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/new?topic_id=USNIST_1 ].\r\n\r\n NIST [ https://www.nist.gov ] \r\n\r\nSubscriber services:\r\n\r\nManage Preferences [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIf you have questions or problems with the subscription service, please contact subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ].\r\nTechnical questions? Contact inquiries@nist.gov. (301) 975-NIST (6478).\r\n\r\nThis service is provided to you at no charge by National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST).\xc2\xa0100 Bureau Drive, Stop 1070\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7 Gaithersburg, MD 20899\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0301-975-6478\r\n\r\n GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
