[2026-04-27 11:10:00] Raw text/plain payload: b"Census Bureau Upcoming and Recently Released Products  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/en.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*?? In Case You Missed It*\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n2020-2024 Embargo ACS [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-gains-educational-attainment.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n2020-2024 American Community Survey\r\n\r\nOn Jan. 29, the U.S. Census Bureau released the remaining 2024 American Community Survey (ACS) 5-year estimates\xc2\xa0and 5-year Variance Replicate Estimates. The last release of 2020-2024 ACS 5-year PUMS files is set for March 5. The updated release schedule [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/news/data-releases/2024/release-schedule.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0is available online.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-gains-educational-attainment.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n2024 Community Resilience Estimates\r\n\r\nOn Jan. 29, the U.S. Census Bureau released new community resilience estimates by social vulnerability to natural disasters. This product helps local governments and community stakeholders plan mitigation and recovery strategies in the event of a disaster. Estimates will be released for the nation, states, counties, core-based statistical areas and tracts.\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2024-cre-natural-hazard-risk-tables.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSocial and Economic Characteristics of Currently Unmarried Women With a Recent Birth: 2023\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nOn Jan. 28, the U.S. Census Bureau released a new report that explores social and economic characteristics of unmarried women who gave birth in 2023. The report uses American Community Survey [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (ACS) data and makes comparisons, when possible, to an earlier report [ https://www2.census.gov/library/publications/2013/acs/acs-21.pdf?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] that used 2011 ACS 1-year estimates.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/births-to-unmarried-women-declined.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nCity Population Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/population-growth-slows.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nVintage 2025\xc2\xa0Population Estimates, Components of Change\xc2\xa0and Voting-Age Population for the Nation, States\xc2\xa0and Puerto Rico\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nOn Jan. 27, the U.S. Census Bureau released July 1, 2025, estimates of total population and voting-age population for the nation, states and Puerto Rico, as well as corresponding annual estimates and components of change since the 2020 Census.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/population-growth-slows.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSAIPE [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2024-saipe.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nOn Jan. 27, the U.S. Census Bureau released new data on small area income and poverty estimates for states, counties and school districts. The new data come from the 2024 Small Area Income and Poverty Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/saipe.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (SAIPE), which provides the only up-to-date, single-year income and poverty statistics for the nation\xe2\x80\x99s 3,143\xc2\xa0counties and 13,126\xc2\xa0school districts.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2024-saipe.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nPublic Information Office\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nUpcoming Events and News Releases:\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*_Tuesday, Feb. 3_*\r\n\r\n***********************\xe2\x80\xa2 **********************Economic Indicator*: (10 a.m.) Housing Vacancies and Homeownership [ http://www.census.gov/housing/hvs/?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x93 4th Quarter 2025__\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*_Wednesday, Feb. 4_*\r\n\r\n************************\xe2\x80\xa2 ***********************Profile America Facts for Features:* National Black History Month: February (tentative)\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*_Friday, Feb. 6_*\r\n\r\n***********************\xe2\x80\xa2 **********************Tip Sheet: *Biweekly Tip Sheet__\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Newsroom* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nNews media: 301-763-3030 or 877-861-2010 or\xc2\xa0pio@census.gov\r\n\r\nNon-media: 1-800-923-8282 or\xc2\xa0ask.census.gov [ https://ask.census.gov/?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nSubscribe now [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/new? ]\xc2\xa0to receive Census Bureau releases and information via e-mail or SMS.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nWe serve as the nation\xe2\x80\x99s leading provider of quality data about its people and economy.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau is the federal government's largest statistical agency. As the world\xe2\x80\x99s premier statistical agency, we are dedicated to making our nation a better place. Policy-makers, businesses, and the public use our data to make informed decisions.\r\n\r\n*Resources for Media*\r\n\r\nFor media interviews, please contact the\xc2\xa0Public Information Office [ https://lnks.gd/l/eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..p-5wpj2DTx0_qgyLiv6JuMTDOF_vZlHcwFpt971jIDs/s/866068797/br/124287751808-l?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Toll Free at 877-861-2010, 301-763-3030, or\xc2\xa0pio@census.gov.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n*Stay connected with us!*\r\n\r\nJoin the conversation on social media.\r\n\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nSubscriber Settings [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Remove me from All Subscriptions  [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n&lt;!-- /* template top padding on mobile */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { table#flexible-abe-main-table { padding:0 !important; } } --&gt; ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260202mspios1ccpupnl&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n"
