[2026-04-27 11:10:02] Raw text/plain payload: b"View email in browser  <[[https://click.explore.redhat.com/v/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX98J_hiyNzHql8x8jNjlcauD0SakF6JVzvbQ9OX4sNCLkCi1LZcbou9p6qUFxZNkfZBg=]]>\r\nBuild here\r\nDeploy an Oracle SQLcl MCP server on OpenShift  <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX-MaNkRyvcJVazis_Q-0NxU8hwoOV7JaH_KzppYWWW68jnZHMHs2mkGKfCMlRXk-Qkok=>\r\nDeploy an Oracle SQLcl MCP server on an OpenShift cluster and use it with the OpenShift AI platform in this AI quickstart.\r\n\r\n Simplify transit router deployment in Open Virtual Network  <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX-DyOWCdEx7_w1M2Vvyay494cvLSvZANiVsmRaRNLPk59XkvnRK6zhu7vo3lZl6szM6g=>\r\nLearn how the new transit router (TR) component in OVN Interconnect simplifies multi-AZ routing by automating tasks.\r\n\r\nHow to build an AI-driven product recommender with OpenShift AI <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX95QwslNaVUuneli451v3sS9jmVxzf8yHsdYiYnwbahZu_IHTLAe_DgMkyP76Uv1bQF8=>\r\nLearn how to build AI-enabled applications for product recommendations, semantic product search, and automated product review summarization with OpenShift AI.\r\n\r\nMulti-homed inventory management with Ansible Automation Platform <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX-edckVR2Dwf_EFu2NZi7q-bcVtNLr4QKGQcyk20rlseDRjLSWhHz5mWxCqdGAOtR8ME=>\r\nA guide to structuring your inventory to manage complex networking while maintaining a single host count in Ansible Automation Platform.\r\n\r\n Transform complex metrics into actionable insights with this AI quickstart  <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX-CgqGaqztaPYCFLtWLVRYB1fOFImATK_M8FmbaVlwTYmBsL6nqYBD4Dyf25Sah_tlpA=>\r\nExplore the AI Observability Metric Summarizer, an intelligent, conversational tool built for Red Hat OpenShift AI environments.\r\n\r\n E-book: The Grumpy Developer's Guide to OpenShift  <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX-O-4cC3Fo6e_YRoVOmLrCaEasFUzYEXCsl28IQhC7GX0hOCmz6RCKxt5ft9WxULKjYk=>\r\nThis hands-on manual guides you through the core principles of application development, providing the practical recipes you need to build and deploy with confidence.\r\n\r\n Learning path: Install Red Hat Trusted Artifact Signer using Google identity provider and Cosign  <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX927VzQiUcjucday2L_IJpVkHOf90E8djyvUb6oQ9TZXZTSOQur1LINih7htB1RcJHXM=>\r\nMaster the setup of Red Hat Trusted Artifact Signer by integrating Google as your identity provider, then transition into a practical walkthrough on securing your container images through Cosign-based signing and verification.\r\nBits\r\nRed Hat OpenShift AI <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX-Gym-ZYoYzvIbKNp1lMZFEy0Ci3igMcFl5npMJ9innjl8V5R7-N-xxsoutITbrhtJ7A=>Red Hat OpenShift AI is an artificial intelligence platform that runs on top of Red Hat OpenShift and provides tools across \r\nthe AI/ML lifecycle.\xc2\xa0\r\nTry it in the Developer Sandbox <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX95J3n-q0OP-6-tUhmJzP81hdWnF2laMejlujyESgb0uBxFf39yjG_kFq38VZ-sLKuI0=>\r\nUpcoming events\r\nRed Hat at DeveloperWeek 2026 <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX-BSD-2KdiV4Iq4qPCtGjONdtK9_8tSZNeyTPv6c0wedVONrorOvyB18YvuXBsG13iKg=>FEBRUARY 18-20, 2025\r\nJoin us in San Jose, California for DeveloperWeek 2026. Visit the Red Hat Developer booth at 126 to connect with our expert technologists, catch a demo, and grab some Red Hat swag (while supplies last).\r\nGo anywhere\r\nEnd-to-end security for AI: Integrating AltaStata Storage with Red Hat OpenShift \r\nconfidential containers <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX-UjFa2dvrV6oUlVjvvxNPWTZlcsFF4mpl0wtqL7MnPWdgE8kfxixmmhaewEjxMnWWH0=>\r\n\r\nHow to set up \r\nAmazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP to use with Red Hat OpenShift Service on AWS <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX-Bd9TDNhDaYuxNnp6rABNolp781aKwN6NugsQN4faT6pzEmvd6ZyXWKJevGHJ9wN0k8=>\r\nNew observability features in Red Hat OpenShift 4.20 and Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management 2.15 <https://click.explore.redhat.com/NDI3LVRCQy00NzQAAAGfvvSX-MtYwcyf0EJpcL0sUdTKRPiUP1OdoyHaLve0ARz40EhkdONv4KvIyveWhn-kDGNweKc=>\r\n\r\n\r\n.\r\n"
