[2026-04-27 11:10:53] Raw text/plain payload: b"Bookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/bulletins/3ff421f?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\na { color:#0073AF !important;} a:hover { color:#004673 !important;} &amp;amp;amp;amp;lt;!-- body { font-family: arial; } p { font-size: 12px; } li { font-size: 12px; } h2 { font-size: 24px; font-style: italic;} --&amp;amp;amp;amp;gt; \r\nIRS.gov Banner \r\nIRS Tax Stats Dispatch February 3, 2026 \r\n \r\nUseful Links:\r\n\r\nTax Statistics Home [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nStatistics\r\n\r\nBusiness Tax [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-business-tax-statistics ]\r\n\r\nCharitable [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-charitable-and-exempt-organizations-statistics ]\r\n\r\nCompliance [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/irs-taxpayer-compliance-research ]\r\n\r\nIndividual Tax [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-individual-tax-statistics ]\r\n\r\nBy Form [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-statistics-by-form ]\r\n\r\nProducts & Publications [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-products-publications-and-papers ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIRS Resources\r\n\r\nContact My Local Office [ https://www.irs.gov/help/contact-your-local-irs-office ]\r\n\r\nFiling Options [ https://www.irs.gov/filing ]\r\n\r\nForms & Pubs [ https://www.irs.gov/forms-instructions ]\r\n\r\nFrequently Asked Questions [ https://www.irs.gov/faqs ]\r\n\r\nNews [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom ]\r\n\r\nTaxpayer Advocate [ https://www.irs.gov/taxpayer-advocate ]\r\n\r\nWhere to File [ https://www.irs.gov/filing/where-to-file-paper-tax-returns-with-or-without-a-payment ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\nIssue Number: \xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa02026 - 02\r\n\r\nInside This Issue\r\n\r\n  * Fiscal Year Return Projections for the United States: 2025-2032, Publication 6292 (Fall 2025) [ #First ] \r\n  * Calendar Year Projections of Individual Returns by Major Processing Categories (Publication 6187)  [ #Second ] \r\n  * Calendar Year Projections for the United States and IRS Campuses (Publication 6186) [ #Third ] \r\n  * Calendar Year Return Projections by State: 2025-2032 (Publication 6149) [ #Fourth ] \r\n  * Heavy Highway Vehicles Use Tax Return [ #Fifth ] \r\n  * 2023 Partnership Returns Line-Item Estimates (Publication 5035) [ #Sixth ] \r\n  * Partnership Tables, Tax Year 2023 [ #Seventh ] \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n* \xc2\xa01.\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0Fiscal Year Return Projections for the United States: 2025-2032, Publication 6292 (Fall 2025) [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-projections-of-federal-tax-return-filings ]*________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe Fall 2025 issue of Fiscal Year Return Projections for the United States (Publication 6292) is now available on SOI's tax stats webpage. This semiannual publication contains United States-level projections of the number of tax returns for Fiscal Years (FYs) 2025\xe2\x80\x932032 of approximately 50 different individual, business, and tax-exempt return types (e.g., Forms 1040, 1120, 941, and 990) to be filed by major return categories and by IRS business operating divisions. There is also additional detail by medium of filing (paper versus electronic) and actual number of returns filed for FY 2024.\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n* \xc2\xa02.\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0Calendar Year Projections of Individual Returns by Major Processing Categories (Publication 6187) [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-calendar-year-projections-publication-6187 ]*________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe 2025 update of Calendar Year Projections of Individual Returns by Major Processing Categories (Publication 6187) is now available on SOI\xe2\x80\x99s Tax Stats webpage. This publication presents multi-year projections of the number of returns in the Form 1040, U.S. Individual Income Tax Return, series to be filed with the IRS by categories important to IRS planning operations, including filing medium (paper versus electronic), as well as other characteristics, such as refund returns. Forecasts are shown at the national level, and selected portions are shown by state and IRS Processing Campus locations. This publication is updated annually and incorporates the latest changes in legal and regulatory matters, administrative plans, and recent filing experiences.\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n* \xc2\xa03.\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0Calendar Year Projections for the United States and IRS Campuses (Publication 6186) [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-calendar-year-projections-publication-6186 ]*________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe 2025 update of Calendar Year Projections for the United States and IRS Campuses (Publication 6186) is now available on SOI's Tax Stats webpage. This annual publication provides multiyear projections of the number of returns expected to be filed nationwide and processed at seven IRS campuses in future calendar years. Projections are presented for different types of tax returns filed by individuals, businesses, and tax-exempt organizations, including widely used forms such as Forms 1040, 1120, 941, and 990. The publication also provides projections for selected IRS examination classes, offering insights into expected return volumes across different taxpayer categories.\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n* \xc2\xa04.\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0Calendar Year Return Projections by State: 2025-2032 (Publication 6149) [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-calendar-year-projections-publication-6149 ]*________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe 2025 update of Calendar Year Return Projections by State: 2025-2032 (Publication 6149) is now available on SOI's Tax Stats webpage. This annual publication contains multi-year calendar-year projections of the number of tax returns to be filed with the IRS by state. The publication includes detailed projections by about 50 different individual, business, and tax-exempt organization return types such as Form 1040, Form 1120, Form 941, and Form 990. There is also additional detail by medium of filing (paper versus electronic).\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n* \xc2\xa05.\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0Heavy Highway Vehicles Use Tax Return [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-projections-publications-supplemental-tables ]*________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nA table presenting national statistics on the number of Form 2290, Heavy Highway Vehicle Use Tax Returns filed electronically by month is now available on SOI's Tax Stats webpage. The updated table includes the number of filings through the third quarter of Calendar Year 2025.\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n* \xc2\xa06.\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa02023 Partnership Returns Line-Item Estimates (Publication 5035) [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-partnership-returns-line-item-estimates-publication-5035 ]*________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe 2023 Partnership Returns Line-Item Estimates (Publication 5035) is now available on SOI\xe2\x80\x99s Tax Stats webpage. This publication presents estimates of frequencies of filer entries recorded on the applicable lines of the forms and schedules filed with partnership returns for Tax Year 2023, and it contains corresponding population estimates of dollar amounts recorded on those lines (as applicable).\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n* \xc2\xa07.\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0Partnership Tables, Tax Year 2023 [ https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-partnership-statistics ]*________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nEighteen tables containing Tax Year 2023 statistics for partnerships from Form 1065, U.S. Return of Partnership Income are now available on SOI\xe2\x80\x99s Tax Stats webpage. The tables include statistics on the types of partnerships and specific industrial sectors. The statistics cover balance sheets, trade and business income and deductions, portfolio income, and rental income. Data are classified by industry and size of total assets. Two historical tables (SOI Bulletin, historical tables 11 and 12) for partnerships are also available, updated with Tax Year 2023 statistics. These tables provide balance sheet and income statement data as well as counts of partnership returns based on size of assets and receipts.\r\n\r\nBack to Top [ #Fifteenth ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nFor more information on Federal Taxes please visit\xc2\xa0IRS.gov [ https://www.irs.gov/ ].\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to Tax Stats Dispatch Mailing List, an IRS e-mail service.\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically from the mailing list Tax Stats. Please Do Not Reply To This Message. To subscribe to another list, please go to the e-News Subscriptions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ] page on the IRS Web site.\r\n\r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nUpdate your subscriptions, modify your password or email address, or stop subscriptions at any time on your Subscriber Preferences Page [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ]. You will need your email address to log in. If you have questions or problems with the subscription service, visit subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ].\r\n\r\nThis service is provided to you at no charge by the Internal Revenue Service (IRS) [ https://www.irs.gov/ ].\r\n\r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com by: Internal Revenue Service (IRS) \xc2\xb7 Internal Revenue Service \xc2\xb7 1111 Constitution Ave. N.W. \xc2\xb7 Washington, D.C. 20535 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n"
