[2026-04-27 11:11:08] Raw text/plain payload: b'View as a webpage\xc2\xa0 /\xc2\xa0 Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDAOC/bulletins/4078139 ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHeader-Hybrid \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nOffice of Communications\xc2\xa0 |\xc2\xa0 press@usda.gov\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nStatement by Secretary of State Marco Rubio and Secretary of Agriculture Brooke Rollins\r\n\r\n"Securing Critical Water Resources for South Texas Agriculture"\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*(Washington, D.C., February 3, 2026)* \xe2\x80\x93 On January 31st, the U.S. Department of Agriculture and the U.S. Department of State welcomed a new commitment between the United States and Mexico that strengthens implementation of the 1944 Water Treaty, providing greater certainty for farmers, ranchers, and producers in South Texas who rely on consistent water deliveries from the Rio Grande.\r\n\r\nThis announcement follows a call last week between President Trump and President Sheinbaum, during which both leaders reaffirmed their commitment to resolving longstanding water management challenges and supporting communities and producers on both sides of the border.\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cWater is the lifeblood of the farmers and ranchers who power South Texas\xe2\x80\x99s agricultural economy,\xe2\x80\x9d *said U.S. Secretary of Agriculture Brooke L. Rollins.*\xc2\xa0 \xe2\x80\x9cThis understanding between our countries is a direct result of President Trump\xe2\x80\x99s determination to secure fair, practical deals that deliver for American agriculture, and we\xe2\x80\x99re grateful to President Sheinbaum and the Government of Mexico for their partnership in this effort.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cUnder President Trump\xe2\x80\x99s leadership and direction,\xe2\x80\x9d *said U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio,* \xe2\x80\x9cthe Department of State, Department of Agriculture, and the U.S. International Boundary and Water Commission have worked to secure Mexico\xe2\x80\x99s commitment to meet its obligations under the 1944 Water Treaty, while also providing a plan to eliminate the deficit from the prior cycle, strengthening water security for Texas communities and U.S. agriculture.\xc2\xa0 This is another example of how the Trump Administration continues to produce benefits for the American people on issues ranging from illegal immigration, countering cartels, and modernizing trade, as well as securing water for our farmers.\xe2\x80\x9d\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nUnder the negotiated outcome, Mexico committed to deliver a minimum of 350,000 acre\xe2\x80\x91feet of water per year to the United States during the current five\xe2\x80\x91year cycle, providing stability for agricultural producers and rural communities in the Lower Rio Grande Valley. \xc2\xa0Mexico has also committed to a detailed plan to fully repay all outstanding water debt accrued during the previous cycle.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, both parties will hold monthly meetings to ensure timely, consistent deliveries and prevent future deficits. USDA,\xc2\xa0the Department of State, and\xc2\xa0other federal partners\xc2\xa0will continue to work closely\xc2\xa0as implementation moves forward.\r\n\r\n###\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0 \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*\r\nU.S. Department of Agriculture*\r\n\r\nwww.usda.gov [ https://www.usda.gov/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Contact us [ https://ask.usda.gov/s/contactsupport?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\ntwitter [ https://www.twitter.com/usda/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/usda/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/usdagov/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]flickr [ https://flickr.com/usdagov?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/usda/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nBookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDAOC/bulletins/0?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nManage Subscriptions [ http://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDAOC/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe All [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDAOC/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.b0b9ffc01626a62fade26e4ffc0836cd&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \xc2\xa0 \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using govDelivery on behalf of: USDA Office of Communications \xc2\xb7 1400 Independence Ave., S.W. \xc2\xb7 Washington, DC 20250  GovDelivery logo  [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
