[2026-04-27 11:11:10] Raw text/plain payload: b"Share / View as a webpage [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/PALANCASTER/bulletins/407875e ]\r\n\r\nLancaster County, Pennsylvania \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*Lancaster DPS Emergency Management Division*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nFebruary Preparedness Newsletter\r\n\r\nFebruary's Preparedness Newsletter will highlight January's 9-1-1 call numbers, staff accomplishments, training opportunities and winter weather safety! \xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nThank You  \r\n9-1-1 Communications for January 2026\r\n\r\nWell done to our 9-1-1 communications team! In the month of January, they answered\xc2\xa0*32,398**\xc2\xa0calls*!\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\r\n  * 911 calls- 12,876 \r\n  * Non-emergency calls- 19,438 \r\n  * Outgoing calls- 6,862 \r\n\r\nIn total there were 39,260 calls coming in and out of communication center!\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nStaff Accomplishments\r\n\r\nCongratulations Jessica and Joyce on earning their County Associate Certificates. Joyce also received her Radiological Response Technician Certificate. Great work! \xc2\xa0\r\n\r\njessica and Joyce\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nCERT March Schedule \r\nUpcoming Training Opportunity - Community Emergency Response Team\r\n\r\nCERT is a nationwide program of the Department of Homeland Security and can be described neighbors helping neighbors. The program helps educate community members about disaster preparedness for local hazards including fire safety, disaster medical operations, and light search and rescue. CERT is a volunteer training and volunteer organization designed to have the community respond when first responders are overloaded and work alongside them.\r\n\r\nWe are excited to announce our Spring CERT is open for registration.\xc2\xa0Sign up today! [ https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Flinks-2.govdelivery.com%2FCL0%2Fhttps%3A%252F%252Fwww.cognitoforms.com%252FLancasterCountyDepartmentOfPublicSafety%252FCERTMarchClassRegistration%2F1%2F0101019bc26e2032-424aeab1-7905-4bc0-8d48-d0eb698aab17-000000%2F32sGE_ndYGjslBJFNshs2C0SaHwJZWiDDwbIFYRKquU%3D440&data=05%7C02%7CBGoodling%40lancastercountypa.gov%7C3a772fbab227447909bd08de5450e704%7C1b7b599652dc45fab6a1af44d53ea7c8%7C0%7C0%7C639040903619658221%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=gFw1uXGGICBeGCgkbMQ35RgDky6WEypxTQ35cpIcmHw%3D&reserved=0 ]\r\n\r\nCERT training consists of 9 units including:\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n  * Disaster Preparedness \r\n  * CERT Organization \r\n  * Disaster Medical Operations 1 and 2 \r\n  * Disaster Psychology \r\n  * Fire Safety and Utility Control \r\n  * Light Search and Rescue Operations \r\n  * CERT and Terrorism \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nWinter Ready\r\n\r\nPreventing House Heating Fires\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nAlthough trending downward since the early 1980s, heating fires remained the second leading cause of home fires in 2021. An estimated 32,200 home heating fires were reported to fire departments within the United States. These fires caused an estimated 190 deaths, 625 injuries and $442 million in property loss.\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Keep anything that can burn at least three feet from all heat sources including fireplaces, wood stoves, radiators, portable heaters or candles. \r\n  * Always plug space heaters directly into an outlet, and make sure its cord isn\xe2\x80\x99t damaged or frayed. \r\n  * Never use an oven to heat your home. \r\n  * Maintain heating equipment and chimneys by having them cleaned and inspected each year by a professional. \r\n  * Visit the U.S. Fire Administration\xc2\xa0Home Fires page [ https://www.usfa.fema.gov/prevention/home-fires/ ]\xc2\xa0to learn about how to prepare for and prevent home fires including tips for\xc2\xa0individuals with disabilities [ https://www.usfa.fema.gov/prevention/home-fires/at-risk-audiences/people-with-disabilities/ ]\xc2\xa0and\xc2\xa0older adults [ https://www.usfa.fema.gov/prevention/home-fires/at-risk-audiences/older-adults/ ]. \r\n\r\nPreventing Home Heating Fires \r\n\r\nLow Cost Keeping House Warm \r\nLow-Cost Tips for Keeping your Home Warm \xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n  * To save on heating bills, close the doors of rooms you are not using. Close the vents and shut the doors in these rooms and keep the basement door closed. Place a rolled towel at the bottom of all doors to keep drafts out. \r\n  * About 30% of a home\xe2\x80\x99s heating energy is lost through its windows. Keep window coverings like blinds or curtains open during the day to take advantage of the sun\xe2\x80\x99s heat in the winter \xe2\x80\x93 especially windows that get direct sunlight. Close them at night to keep heat from escaping. If you have gaps around the windows, try using weather stripping or caulk to keep the cold air out. You can also apply inexpensive window insulation kits that create an airtight seal around windows. \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nFall and Winter Energy-Saving Tips | Department of Energy [ https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/fall-and-winter-energy-saving-tips ]\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nCarbon Monoxide (CO) Poisoning \xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nCarbon monoxide (CO) is an odorless, colorless gas that kills without warning. It claims the lives of hundreds of people every year and makes thousands more ill. Many household items including gas- and oil-burning furnaces, portable generators, and charcoal grills produce this poison gas. Following these important steps can keep your family safe.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nCO DETECTORS\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Install battery-operated or battery back-up CO detectors near every sleeping area in your home. \r\n  * Check CO detectors regularly to be sure they are functioning properly. \r\n\r\nOIL & GAS FURNACES \xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Have your furnace inspected every year. \r\n\r\nPORTABLE GENERATORS \xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Never use a generator inside your home or garage, even if doors and windows are open. \r\n  * Only use generators outside, more than 20 feet away from your home, doors, and windows. \r\n\r\nCO Poisoning \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nWelcome Spring Interns!\r\n\r\nSkye is a Junior Criminal Justice Major at Elizabethtown College. She was drawn to emergency management because they value the role it plays in preparing communities for emergencies, building trust and confidence, and strengthening the community as a whole.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n  Skye \r\n\r\nDelaney  \r\n\r\nDelaney is a senior at Millersville University pursing a dual BS-MS degree in Emergency Management. She was drawn to emergency management by the people in the field. Their passion for helping others inspires her to be a part of it.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nStay Connected with Lancaster County, PA: Facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/LanCoPennsylvania/ ] \xc2\xa0 X [ https://www.co.lancaster.pa.us/twitter ] \xc2\xa0 Govdelivery [ http://www.granicus.com ] SUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\nManage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/PALANCASTER/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe All [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/PALANCASTER/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.6d3846f1b7cea9478076b7229739f574&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]  \r\n \r\n \r\nbody .abe-section-table {max-width:601px !important;} body .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} #footer-container td {padding:0px;} \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using govDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: Lancaster County, PA \xc2\xb7 150 N Queen Street\r\nLancaster, PA 17603 GovDelivery logo  [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n"
