[2026-04-27 11:11:24] Raw text/plain payload: b'View as a webpage / Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOEOS/bulletins/4079eb7 ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n2025 Office of Science/DOE logo \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nEnergy Department Announces Members of the Office of Science Advisory Committee, Strengthening Gold Standard Science in America\r\n\r\n"The U.S. Department of Energy today announced the chair and members of the newly established Office of Science Advisory Committee, a unified advisory body that will provide independent advice on complex scientific and technical challenges across the Department\xe2\x80\x99s Office of Science."\r\n\r\nThe U.S. Department of Energy (DOE) today announced the chair and members of the\xc2\xa0newly established [ https://www.energy.gov/science/articles/doe-establishes-office-science-advisory-committee?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Office of Science Advisory Committee (SCAC), a unified advisory body that will provide independent advice on complex scientific and technical challenges across the Department\xe2\x80\x99s Office of Science.\r\n\r\nToday\xe2\x80\x99s announcement advances the Department\xe2\x80\x99s implementation of President Trump\xe2\x80\x99s Executive Order\xc2\xa0"Restoring Gold Standard Science" [ https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/05/restoring-gold-standard-science/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0as the cornerstone of federal research\xe2\x80\x94ensuring that the Department and its National Laboratory systems\' science is collaborative, transparent, and guided by evidence to rebuild public trust in science. As DOE modernizes and strengthens its scientific enterprise, SCAC will provide expert input to help inform priorities, improve coordination, and address cross-cutting research challenges across the Office of Science.\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cThe establishment of SCAC underscores the Department\'s commitment to scientific integrity and the power of partnership,\xe2\x80\x9d said\xc2\xa0*DOE Under Secretary for Science Dar\xc3\xado Gil*. \xe2\x80\x9cBy bringing together leading minds from diverse institutions, we\xe2\x80\x99re forging a collaborative framework that will not only enhance our scientific endeavors but also accelerate the translation of fundamental research into tangible benefits for the American people. This committee exemplifies how shared vision and collective expertise are essential for navigating the complex scientific landscape of today and tomorrow.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\nMembers of SCAC, appointed by Under Secretary Gil, represent the full breadth of Office of Science research, drawing expertise from leaders across academia, industry, science philanthropy, and the Department\'s National Laboratories. The Committee will help the Office of Science adapt to a rapidly evolving research landscape and address interdisciplinary challenges in a streamlined and flexible manner. It will also provide advice on initiatives that are priorities for the entire Office, including the Genesis Mission, scientific discovery, fusion energy, and quantum science.\r\n\r\nSCAC will be chaired by Persis Drell, professor of materials science and engineering and physics at Stanford University, provost emerita of Stanford, and director emerita of SLAC National Accelerator Laboratory.\r\n\r\nThe Committee will adopt the core functions of the Office of Science\xe2\x80\x99s six former discretionary advisory committees. Any current charged responsibilities of these former committees will transfer to SCAC, providing a single, coordinated source of independent expert advice. A full list of the 21 SCAC members is available\xc2\xa0here [ https://science.osti.gov/About/Federal-Advisory-Committee/SCAC/Membership?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nStay Connected with US Department of Energy Office of Science: Office of Science Website [ https://www.energy.gov/science/office-science?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0Twitter [ https://twitter.com/doescience?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0LinkedIn Icon [ https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/office-of-science?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0Youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/doescience?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  SUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\nManage Subscriptions [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOEOS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe All [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDOEOS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.f79aa68a3024cd2fce56df538b9b073f&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]  \r\nbody .abe-section-table {max-width:601px !important;} body .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: US Department of Energy Office of Science \xc2\xb7 1000 Independence Ave., SW\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0Washington, DC\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7 20585\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0(202) 586-5430  GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
