k1SklhtrAfdq9ykvMrsjkm9Bt-2FiA2GYdCHNyMx4Vf4SfYZpphrxsTdpNAB6c1zP8gfliVo3ncEUZbRsGGTCGWTLUUZyuGuaWEA2sMsBirMWP-2F-2BMhD1TQgghj3Jr8ivL8oNc2dLeZEeL3rrCBB09uEISFq-2FduhRehOmdsoPGEtqx-2BeGL1dakDY1kjOb-2BM1EipSHxDL43Edt1YiJQ8g5A7gGOAYtHCA5ogdGtPzEuuTN6crY8Qx\r\n)By Debra Cope\r\n\r\nIf your New Year\xe2\x80\x99s goals have already lost their steam, take\r\nheart \xe2\x80\x94 now is actually an ideal time to make certain high-impact\r\nfinancial moves.\r\n\r\nEven though the 2025 tax year has ended, the IRS lets us\r\nretroactively contribute to certain tax-advantaged accounts until\r\nApril 15, giving us a second chance to maximize our retirement\r\nand health savings and potentially lower our taxable income.\r\nBetter still, it\xe2\x80\x99s an opportunity to look at our finances after\r\nthe year is over, when we know exactly how much we\xe2\x80\x99ve earned and\r\nwhat else we might do to lower our tax bill.Keep&nbsp;reading (\r\nhttps://ablink.newsletter.sofi.com/ls/click?upn=u001.k-2FImUMyJvquSjfrastfytIPj6h1-2BVfWjnUDDp-2FeYQFLpjhu-2F6ot-2F5dL1x7ZEqHyiH0ER2K1JLQQIKz76eM6rBVe8J2TQBIdkgnY4cpwrcf3QrUWMGYrJJb8QQFsWo4ALk8XICsaol9Jv0HMHahDKiCnJEfqGjWJeIFy9ea0RZK5T8gfz3dADvi-2FRcSMbZ0iwJZi4cnWuM15zo2SsTl0n0kA-2F6tTxpXdu4WYmGvcx82KxUy1a1H6Q0vZkZ5OEQgkccT2ICrckq59HChyccyu6idiwwF9Qb0m4fS31kmpvQCI-3Di6PS_Hvirw9jLOYnqUg7ucIAtvDa4JCWhfjePQT8cfdKWfeKaKK6WyzUu0MT5hcL83ezarLAJeFzEeRP-2BR0XWfLa6c9zJW9jObGwn6mBHS1-2Fc1QxpZyp3v45YUjkQGTWoOdFBB3HDhYXUXnxpygjSHMuXCHCahG-2BOxOBEuvjkFO0IlCSoLE6xKfWjID-2F6NMNZLEx-2FfHpQpqkpLHLKzupfyvAb-2F36yxL2teGmR9RXVMyrG6FN9lCIYFB2irP8oX5XnhjtpAyl3-2BgbSY5Vj56jBNaUDNQ4o1U6ZJhuMYjeo-2FY1WD5JFPjj7Jd2zhKEqdGGtMLzSFzZqn9u3ePygcXVxAbdXilEthYZmHcrPN6pxtdS6BRngTXcqkyMLUUNvgMg6smTd7fU6eLkg86zRL3K-2FWs9MUDPglkO0PmvkgVBVvTwlh3t3h9Gguc2W1C-2BElPcxhwFWbsgoMdMWsfKmHpwp2SQEsJkaneboXJ2ELlDBug6Msv7v7YwK9p-2F-2BuqyOurVvHlNOyElgwE8nkLo041Qk1SklhtrAfdq9ykvMrsjkm9Bt-2FiA2GYdCHNyMx4Vf4SfYZpphrxsTdpNAB6c1zP8gfliVo3ncEUZbRsGGTCGWTLUUZyvIiNXtbs-2BlpJpvycMhX8HfQ14Zv8Tm14Ge5cXlG