[2026-04-27 11:12:04] Raw text/plain payload: b'New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection News Release \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE*\r\nFebruary 4, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*Contact: *Caryn Shinske (609) 984-1795\r\nLawrence Hajna (609) 984-1795*\r\n*Vincent Grassi (609) 984-1795*\r\n*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*ACTING DEP COMMISSIONER POTOSNAK ANNOUNCES JOSEPH SEEBODE AS DEPUTY COMMISSIONER*\r\n\r\n*(26/P08) TRENTON \xe2\x80\x93 *Acting Department of Environmental Protection Commissioner Ed Potosnak today announced the appointment of Joseph J. Seebode to the role of Deputy Commissioner to advance the Sherrill Administration\xe2\x80\x99s environmental goals.\r\n\r\nPhoto of DEP Deputy Commissioner Joseph J. Seebode \r\n\r\nAs Deputy Commissioner, Seebode will serve as second in command for the DEP and will be responsible for continuing the agency\xe2\x80\x99s successes in developing and implementing policies that protect air and water quality, advance climate resilience, preserve natural resources, provide quality open space for the public, and ensure environmental justice, among many other roles.\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cJoe\xe2\x80\x99s on-the-ground experience advancing projects with the Army Corps will be a major asset in accomplishing the Sherill Administration\xe2\x80\x99s mission to deliver for the people of New Jersey by reducing permitting times while protecting health, safety and environment,\xe2\x80\x9d *Acting Commissioner Potosnak said*. \xe2\x80\x9cIn particular, his wealth of knowledge in building and growing partnerships will be critical to ensuring the protection of our air, land, water and natural resources.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\nSeebode, an environmental engineer with more than 40 years of experience, including a stint as a DEP Assistant Commissioner in the early 2000s, returns to the DEP after an exciting and fulfilling public service career with the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers, where he most recently served as the Deputy District Engineer and Chief of Programs and Project Management for the New York District.\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x9cI am excited to return to DEP and work with its deeply talented team of scientists, engineers and professionals to continue raising the bar on environmental protection, stewardship and permitting turnaround times,\xe2\x80\x9d *Deputy Commissioner Seebode said*. \xe2\x80\x9cFrom coastal resilience to brownfields redevelopment, the projects and policies we undertake today will protect and strengthen our environment for future generations.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\nIn his most recent role at the Army Corps, Seebode oversaw an interdisciplinary team of engineers and scientists delivering major military and civil works construction and regional infrastructure improvements in New York, New Jersey and Greenland.\r\n\r\nWhile at the Army Corps, Seebode\xe2\x80\x99s leadership helped guide post-Hurricane Sandy recovery efforts such as the removal of water from flooded tunnels, emergency dredging, coastline repair work and debris removal. He also oversaw other major initiatives for the New York District, including a $2.1 billion deepening project for the Port of New York and New Jersey and a comprehensive environmental restoration strategy for the New York/New Jersey Harbor Estuary.\r\n\r\nSeebode\xe2\x80\x99s post-Sandy efforts and the port-deepening project earned him the prestigious Richard J. Sullivan Award in December 2025 for his dedication to advancing coastal resilience, environmental restoration and sustainable water management. The award is part of the DEP\xe2\x80\x99s annual Governor\xe2\x80\x99s Environmental Excellence Awards program\r\n\r\nFrom 2003 to 2006, Seebode served as a DEP Assistant Commissioner on an intergovernmental detail, overseeing a team engaged in a wide array of environmental engineering and remediation activities.\r\n\r\nSeebode earned bachelor\'s and master\'s degrees from Manhattan College after graduating from Seton Hall Prep and is a proud member of the Seton Hall Prep Athletic Hall of Fame.\r\n\r\n###\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n"The New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection is dedicated to protecting New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s environment and public health. The agency prioritizes addressing climate change, protecting New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s water, revitalizing its communities and managing and promoting its natural and historic resources."\r\n\r\n"For the most recent information, follow the DEP on X @NewJerseyDEP [ https://twitter.com/newjerseydep?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Facebook @newjerseydep [ https://www.facebook.com/newjerseydep/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Instagram @nj.dep [ https://www.instagram.com/nj.dep/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], and LinkedIn @newjerseydep [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/newjerseydep?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ],\xc2\xa0or visit\xc2\xa0""www.nj.gov/dep" [ http://www.nj.gov/dep?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]"."\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nQuestions?\xc2\xa0Contact Us [ https://www.nj.gov/cgi-bin/dep/contactdep.pl?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \r\nFacebook [ https://www.nj.gov/dep/facebook.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] Twitter-X LinkedIn Instagram [ https://www.nj.gov/dep/instagram.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nManage Preferences [ http://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection \xc2\xb7 401 E. State St. \xc2\xb7 Trenton, NJ 08625 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
