[2026-04-27 11:12:25] Raw text/plain payload: b'n i s t  \r\n \r\n\r\nView as a Web Page [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/bulletins/407c764 ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\nevents  \r\nRegistration is now open!\r\n\r\nCybersecurity IoT \r\n\r\nThe NIST Cybersecurity for IoT Program [ https://www.nist.gov/itl/applied-cybersecurity/nist-cybersecurity-iot-program ] is hosting a workshop to collect inputs from the community on future proposed directions that would be most useful in today\xe2\x80\x99s IoT cybersecurity landscape as well as next steps for the revision of NIST SP 800-213:" IoT Device Cybersecurity Guidance for the Federal Government: Establishing IoT Device Cybersecurity Requirements".\r\n\r\nJoin us on March 31 and April 1, 2026 at the NIST Gaithersburg campus for two days of presentations and discussion \xe2\x80\x93 for in-person attendance, please register by March 18th.\r\n\r\nSP 800-213 inputs will be used to help further guidance for manufacturers on device security. Additionally, we are seeking inputs on what guidance would be most useful for federal agencies looking to use, acquire, and secure connected devices (including operational technologies (OT) for critical infrastructure applications). Your feedback is critical to shaping the direction and development of cybersecurity guidance for emerging technologies!\r\n\r\nRegister Now [ https://www.nist.gov/news-events/events/2026/03/cybersecurity-iot-workshop-future-directions ]\r\n   \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nConnect with us\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/NIST ]X [ https://twitter.com/NIST ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/NIST ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/nist ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/nist/ ]  \r\n\r\nReceived this email from a friend? Subscribe here [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/new ].\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nPrivacy Policy [ https://www.nist.gov/privacy-policy#privpolicy ]\r\n\r\n NIST [ http://www.nist.gov/ ] \r\n\r\n*You are subscribed to receive updates from the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST).*\r\n\r\n*Subscriber services:*\r\n\r\n*Manage Preferences [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USNIST/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]*\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIf you have questions or problems with the subscription service, please contact subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ].\r\nTechnical questions? Contact inquiries@nist.gov. (301) 975-NIST (6478).\r\n\r\nThis service is provided to you at no charge by National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST).\xc2\xa0100 Bureau Drive, Stop 1070\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7 Gaithersburg, MD 20899\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0301-975-6478\r\n\r\n GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
