[2026-04-27 11:13:08] Raw text/plain payload: b"Bookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/bulletins/407eb99?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\na { color:#0073AF !important;} a:hover { color:#004673 !important;} &amp;amp;lt;!-- body { font-family: arial; } p { font-size: 12px; } li { font-size: 12px; } h2 { font-size: 24px; font-style: italic;} --&amp;amp;gt; \r\nIRS.gov Banner \r\nIRS Tax Tips Feb. 5, 2026 \r\n \r\nUseful Links:\r\n\r\nIRS.gov [ https://www.irs.gov/ ]\r\n\r\nHelp For Hurricane Victims [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/disaster-assistance-and-emergency-relief-for-individuals-and-businesses-1 ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nNews Essentials\r\n\r\nWhat's Hot [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/whats-hot ]\r\n\r\nNews Releases [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\nIRS - The Basics [ https://www.irs.gov/about-irs/irs-the-basics ]\r\n\r\nIRS Guidance [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/understanding-irs-guidance-a-brief-primer ]\r\n\r\nMedia Contacts [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-media-relations-office-contact-number ]\r\n\r\nFacts & Figures [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nAround The Nation [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/around-the-nation ]\r\n\r\ne-News Subscriptions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/e-news-subscriptions ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe Newsroom Topics\r\n\r\nMultimedia\xc2\xa0Center [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/multimedia-center ]\r\n\r\nNoticias en Espa\xc3\xb1ol [ https://www.irs.gov/es/spanish/noticias-en-espanol ]\r\n\r\nRadio PSAs [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-radio-psas ]\r\n\r\nTax Scams/Consumer Alerts [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-scams-consumer-alerts ]\r\n\r\nThe Tax Gap [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/the-tax-gap ]\r\n\r\nFact\xc2\xa0Sheets [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets ]\r\n\r\nIRS Tax Tips [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-tax-tips ]\r\n\r\nArmed Forces [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-information-for-members-of-the-us-armed-forces ]\r\n\r\nLatest News [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/news-releases-for-current-month ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nIRS Resources\r\n\r\nContact\xc2\xa0Your Local IRS\xc2\xa0Office [ https://www.irs.gov/help/contact-your-local-irs-office ]\r\n\r\nFiling Your Taxes [ https://www.irs.gov/filing ]\r\n\r\nForms & Instructions [ https://www.irs.gov/forms-instructions ]\r\n\r\nFrequently Asked Questions [ https://www.irs.gov/help/telephone-assistance ]\r\n\r\nTaxpayer Advocate Service [ https://www.irs.gov/taxpayer-advocate ]\r\n\r\nWhere to File [ https://www.irs.gov/filing/where-to-file-paper-tax-returns-with-or-without-a-payment ]\r\n\r\nIRS Social Media [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-new-media-1 ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\nIssue Number: Tax Tip 2026-10\r\n\r\n*Tax credits for individuals*\r\n\r\nA tax credit reduces the amount a person owes in income taxes dollar-for-dollar. Some tax credits are even refundable, meaning if a person's tax bill is less than the amount of a refundable credit, they can get the difference back in their refund. The One, Big, Beautiful Bill [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/one-big-beautiful-bill-provisions#individuals ] has brought enhancements to some of these credits.\r\n\r\nHere\xe2\x80\x99s a quick overview of some of the more common credits:\r\n\r\n*Tax credits*\r\n\r\n\r\n  * *Child Tax Credit [ https://www.irs.gov/credits-deductions/individuals/child-tax-credit ]* helps families with qualifying children. For 2025, the amount is up to $2,200 per qualifying child. \r\n  * *Child and Dependent Care Credit [ https://www.irs.gov/credits-deductions/individuals/child-and-dependent-care-credit-information ] *can reduce federal income tax by claiming the credit for child and or dependent care expenses while the person worked or was looking for work. \r\n  * *Saver\xe2\x80\x99s Credit [ https://www.irs.gov/retirement-plans/plan-participant-employee/retirement-savings-contributions-credit-savers-credit ]* may be available if a taxpayer made eligible contributions to their IRA or employer-sponsored retirement plan. The maximum credit is $1,000 ($2,000 if married filing jointly). \r\n\r\n*Refundable tax credits*\r\n\r\n\r\n  * *Earned Income Tax Credit [ https://www.irs.gov/credits-deductions/individuals/earned-income-tax-credit-eitc ]* helps low to moderate-income workers and families get a tax break. The amount of the credit may vary based on income, family size and filing status. \r\n  * *Premium Tax Credit [ https://www.irs.gov/credits-deductions/premium-tax-credit-ptc-overview ]* is available to taxpayers who buy their health insurance through the Health Insurance Marketplace and meet other criteria. It\xe2\x80\x99s a refundable credit based on the taxpayer\xe2\x80\x99s income and the cost of their healthcare plan. \r\n  * *Fuel Tax Credit [ https://www.irs.gov/credits-deductions/businesses/fuel-tax-credit ]* may be claimed if fuel was purchased for use for off-highway business and farming purposes. \r\n\r\n*Partially refundable tax credits*\r\n\r\n\r\n  * *Additional Child Tax Credit* is a refundable portion of the CTC. For 2025, up to $1,700 per qualifying child may be refundable. \r\n  * *Adoption Tax Credit* [ https://www.irs.gov/credits-deductions/individuals/adoption-credit ] is available to taxpayers who finalized an adoption in 2025 or started the adoption process before 2025. The maximum amount, for 2025, is $17,280 per eligible child. The refundable amount is up to $5,000 per qualifying child. However, any nonrefundable amount carried forward can\xe2\x80\x99t be used to calculate a refundable portion for future tax years. \r\n  * *American Opportunity Tax Credit [ https://www.irs.gov/credits-deductions/individuals/education-credits-aotc-and-llc ]* helps offset qualifying education expenses for an eligible college student. The amount is up to $2,500 per year and up to $1,000 is refundable. \r\n\r\nIt\xe2\x80\x99s important for people to keep records to show their eligibility for the tax credits they claim. Unfortunately, scam promoters [ https://www.irs.gov/help/tax-scams ] can share misleading information about credits while trying to promote large refunds. The IRS Interactive Tax Assistant [ https://www.irs.gov/help/ita ] can help a person decide if they're eligible for many popular tax credits and deductions.\r\n\r\n*More information*\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Tax credits for individuals: What they mean and how they can help refunds [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-credits-for-individuals-what-they-mean-and-how-they-can-help-refunds ] \r\n\r\nSubscribe to IRS Tax Tips [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/subscribe-to-irs-tax-tips/ ]\r\n\r\nBack to top [ #top ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ] \xc2\xa0Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ] \xc2\xa0LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to IRS Tax Tips, an IRS e-mail service. For more information on federal taxes please visit IRS.gov [ https://www.irs.gov/ ].\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically from the IRS Tax Tips mailing list. *Please Do Not Reply To This Message.*\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nUpdate your subscriptions, modify your password or email address, or stop subscriptions at any time on your Subscriber Preferences Page [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ]. You will need your email address to log in. If you have questions or problems with the subscription service, visit subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ].\r\n\r\nThis service is provided to you at no charge by the Internal Revenue Service (IRS) [ https://www.irs.gov/ ].\r\n\r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com by: Internal Revenue Service (IRS) \xc2\xb7 Internal Revenue Service \xc2\xb7 1111 Constitution Ave. N.W. \xc2\xb7 Washington, D.C. 20535 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n"
