[2026-04-27 11:13:45] Raw text/plain payload: b'FDA has updated the list of breakthrough devices and marketing authorizations for 2025  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nIf your email program has trouble displaying this email, view as a webpage [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/bulletins/407fa5b ].\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nU.S. Food and Drug Administration, Center for Devices and Radiological Health\r\n\r\nBookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/bulletins/407fa5b?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nFDA Updates Breakthrough Devices Program Metrics and Marketing Authorizations List\r\n\r\nToday, the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has updated the Breakthrough Device designations data, which includes the number of breakthrough devices that have received marketing authorizations.\r\n\r\nFrom the launch of the Breakthrough Devices Program through December 31, 2025, the FDA has granted a total of *1,246* Breakthrough Device designations. Of those, the Center for Devices and Radiological Health granted 1,226 designations and the Center for Biologics Evaluation and Research granted 20 designations.\r\n\r\nThe agency has also granted *185* marketing authorizations for breakthrough devices since the launch of the Breakthrough Devices Program.\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.fda.gov/medical-devices/how-study-and-market-your-device/breakthrough-devices-program?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nThe Breakthrough Devices Program is intended to provide patients and health care providers with timely access to certain medical devices by speeding up development, assessment, and review for premarket approval, 510(k) clearance, and De Novo marketing authorization. Through the program, manufacturers can interact with the FDA\xe2\x80\x99s experts to receive feedback on device development, receive help navigating the path to FDA marketing authorization, and obtain prioritized review on regulatory submissions.\r\n\r\n*Questions?*\r\n\r\nIf you have questions about the Breakthrough Devices Program, contact BreakthroughDevicesProgram@fda.hhs.gov.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nFollow us on X at @FDADeviceInfo [ https://x.com/FDADeviceInfo?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n \r\ntwitter [ https://x.com/FDADeviceInfo?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/FDA?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC_giJ3xlEL9jUF1YfJdzzuQ?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]LinkedIn [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/fda?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\n*Manage Subscriptions* [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 *Unsubscribe All* [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.ee0243ee8741fe358146537aecf40e1e&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 *Help* [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} td {line-height:1;} \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: U.S. Food and Drug Administration \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\r\n10903 New Hampshire Ave\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0Silver Spring, MD \xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0 20993-0002\xc2\xa0\xc2\xb7\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa01-888-INFO-FDA GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
