[2026-04-27 11:13:50] Raw text/plain payload: b'"No tax on tips"; One, Big, Beautiful Bill; Filing season; Free File; taxes  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n2020_04_14_Patriotic_Image \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nr\r\n\r\nOutreach Connection\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nFebruary 06, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nOutreach Connection FY26-03\r\nThe One Big Beautiful Bill Act word Flag of the United States of America background\r\n"No Tax on Tips"\r\n\r\nWhat eligible workers that customarily receive tips should know about the \xe2\x80\x9cNo Tax on Tips\xe2\x80\x9d provision under the One, Big, Beautiful Bill.\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Qualified tips [ #link_2 ] \r\n  * Guidance [ #link_1 ] \r\n  * Claiming the deduction [ #link_3 ] \r\n  * More information [ #link_4 ] \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nQualified tips\r\nSmiling male barber with clippers in hand in a barber shop\r\n\r\nThe One, Big, Beautiful Bill proposed regulations identify occupations customarily and regularly receive tips and define \xe2\x80\x9cqualified tips\xe2\x80\x9d eligible taxpayers may claim as a deduction.\r\n\r\n*Related resources*\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Occupations where workers customarily and regularly receive tips [ https://www.irs.gov/forms-pubs/occupations-that-customarily-and-regularly-received-tips-on-or-before-december-31-2024 ] \r\n  * IRS YouTube video:\xc2\xa0Tax-free tip for service workers [ https://www.youtube.com/shorts/Bc_XpBVodpY?feature=share ] \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nGuidance\r\nYoung female barista with tip jar at table in cafe\r\n\r\nEmployees and self-employed individuals in certain qualified occupations who customarily and regularly receive tips might be eligible to deduct qualified tips.\r\n\r\n*Related resources*\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Guidance for individuals who received tips during tax year 2025 [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/treasury-irs-provide-guidance-for-individuals-who-received-tips-or-overtime-during-tax-year-2025 ] \r\n  * Penalty relief for tax year 2025 for information reporting on tips [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/treasury-irs-provide-penalty-relief-for-tax-year-2025-for-information-reporting-on-tips-and-overtime-under-the-one-big-beautiful-bill ] \r\n  * How to take advantage of no tax on tips [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/one-big-beautiful-bill-how-to-take-advantage-of-no-tax-on-tips-and-overtime ] \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nClaiming the deduction\r\nSmiling waiter talking to couple, recommending drinks and dishes of the day\r\n\r\nFor tipped workers, the maximum annual deduction is $25,000, which phases out for taxpayers with modified adjusted gross income over $150,000 ($300,000 for joint filers).\r\n\r\n*Related resources*\r\n\r\n\r\n  * IRS YouTube video: Deducting tips from taxes [ https://www.youtube.com/shorts/T4Irx8UIOfo?feature=share ] \r\n  * IRS opens 2026 filing season [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-opens-2026-filing-season ] \r\n  * Use IRS Free File to conveniently file your return at no cost [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/use-irs-free-file-to-conveniently-file-your-return-at-no-cost ] \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nMore information\r\n\r\n  * One, Big, Beautiful Bill provisions \xe2\x80\x93 Individuals and workers [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/one-big-beautiful-bill-provisions-individuals-and-workers ] \r\n  * E-file: Do your taxes for free [ https://www.irs.gov/e-file-do-your-taxes-for-free ] \r\n  * IRS YouTube video: Cheers to No Tax on Tips [ https://www.youtube.com/shorts/4WqqLuDCgPc ] \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ]Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ]LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ] [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]  \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nUpdate your subscriptions, modify your password or email address, or stop subscriptions at any time on your Subscriber Preferences Page [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/subscriber/new?preferences=true ]. You will need to use your email address to log in. If you have questions or problems with the subscription service, please contact subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ].\r\n\r\n This service is provided to you at no charge by the Internal Revenue Service (IRS) [ https://www.irs.gov/ ]. \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com by: Internal Revenue Service (IRS) \xc2\xb7 Internal Revenue Service \xc2\xb7 1111 Constitution Ave. N.W. \xc2\xb7 Washington, D.C. 20535 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/ ] \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
