[2026-04-27 11:13:53] Raw text/plain payload: b'Census Bureau Upcoming and Recently Released Products.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnited States Census Bureau [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/tip-sheets/2026/tp26-03.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nTip Sheet (TP26-03)\r\n\r\n*Upcoming\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0 *\r\n\r\n*Online Product Calendar* \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau provides anticipated release dates for its regular and recurring statistical products through its online product calendar [ https://www.census.gov/about/event-calendar.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]. This calendar is regularly updated to reflect the most current information.\r\n\r\n*Demographic*\r\n\r\n*2024 Rental Housing Finance Survey *\xe2\x80\x94 The U. S. Census Bureau and the Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) will release the 2024 Rental Housing Finance Survey (RHFS) summary tables in the RHFS Table Creator, public use files and codebook on census.gov. The RHFS Table Creator is an interactive data tool that allows users to create custom tables of financial, mortgage, and property characteristics of single-family and multifamily residential properties for rent in the United States. Data available include property, residential structure(s), mortgage characteristics, ownership status, commercial use of space, benefits received and more. Visit Data [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/rhfs/data.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/rhfs/data/puf.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]for the latest RHFS data and Rental Housing Finance Survey (RHFS) [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/rhfs.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] for more information about the survey. (Tentatively scheduled for release Feb. 19.)\r\n\r\n*Economic*\r\n\r\n*New Post-Secondary Employment Outcomes Data *\xe2\x80\x94\xc2\xa0The U.S. Census Bureau is scheduled to announce new education partners for its\xc2\xa0Post-Secondary Employment Outcomes (PSEO) [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/data/pseo_experimental.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xe2\x80\xafexperimental data product.\xc2\xa0The\xc2\xa0PSEO\xc2\xa0provides\xc2\xa0earnings and employment outcomes for\xc2\xa0college and university graduates\xc2\xa0by degree level, degree major, post-secondary institution, and state of institution,\xc2\xa0and\xc2\xa0is\xc2\xa0used by parents, students, institutions, and workforce agencies to learn about\xc2\xa0the\xc2\xa0labor force\xc2\xa0outcomes of graduates.\xe2\x80\xaf(Scheduled for release Feb. 12.)\r\n\r\n*Call for Presentations for the 2026 Local Employment Dynamics (LED) Partnership Virtual Workshop* \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau invites you to submit a proposal to*\xc2\xa0*present virtually at the 2026 LED Partnership Hybrid Workshop May 12-13, 2026. This year\xe2\x80\x99s theme is"\xc2\xa0\xe2\x80\x9cNumbers to Narratives: Data for Better Decisions.\xe2\x80\x9d"\xc2\xa0The event will highlight the useful applications of data made possible through the LED State/Federal partnership including\xc2\xa0the Quarterly Workforce Indicators (QWI), the Longitudinal Employer-Household Dynamics (LEHD) Origin-Destination Employee Statistics (LODES), OnTheMap or OnTheMap for Emergency Management, Job-to-Job Flows (J2J), Post-Secondary Employment Outcomes (PSEO) and Veteran Employment Outcomes (VEO). Please visit\xc2\xa0LEHD [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0for proposal guidance. Additional details will be posted when available. Information on previous workshops can be found at\xc2\xa0Workshops and Webinars - Longitudinal Employer-Household Dynamics [ https://lehd.ces.census.gov/workshops_webinars/?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\xc2\xa0Please email CES.Local.Employment.Dynamics@census.gov for questions about the workshop. (Deadline to submit proposal: Feb. 18.)\r\n\r\n*Read More* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/tip-sheets/2026/tp26-03.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n*\xe2\x80\x9c**Unlocking NAICS 5- and 6-Digit Details in the Quarterly Workforce Indicators (QWI) Data Set* [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/2026/unlocking-naics-5-6-digit-details.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\xe2\x80\x9d*\xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau and the Local Employment Dynamics (LED) Partnership, in collaboration with the Council for Community and Economic Research (C2ER) and the Labor Market Information (LMI) Institute, welcome Andrew Foote as he presents, \xe2\x80\x9cUnlocking NAICS 5- and 6- Digit Details in the Quarterly Workforce Indicators (QWI).\xe2\x80\x9d This presentation will introduce the newly released North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) 5- and 6- digit QWI tabulations and the available demographic and firm level crossings, including sex, age, race and ethnicity, education, and firm age and size at the state level. (Feb. 18.)\r\n\r\n*Census Business Builder Version 5.11*\xc2\xa0\xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau will release version 5.11 of the Census Business Builder (CBB) tool. This release will include new data for the 2024 American Community Survey (ACS) 5-year estimates, metadata updates, the unemployment rate and bug fixes for previously known issues.\xc2\xa0More information on Census Business Builder is available\xc2\xa0online [ https://www.census.gov/data/data-tools/cbb.Help_&_FAQs.html.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]. (Scheduled for release Feb. 25.)\r\n\r\n*Business Trends and Outlook Survey* [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/btos.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x94 The Business Trends and Outlook Survey (BTOS) measures business conditions on an ongoing basis. BTOS experimental data products are representative of all employer businesses other than farms in the U.S. economy. The data allow greater insight into the state of the economy by providing continuous, timely information for key economic measures. Data are released biweekly and are available by sector, state, employment size and the 25 most populous metropolitan statistical areas. New questions on artificial intelligence were added Nov. 17 and will be released in 2026.\r\n\r\n*Federal Register Notices*\r\n\r\nThe U.S. Census Bureau publishes updates in the Federal Register to keep the public informed about surveys, censuses and related activities. Some notices include a comment period during which the public can provide feedback. For more information on Census Bureau Federal Register notices (FRNs), check out Collections of Information and Federal Register Notices [ https://www.census.gov/about/policies/collections.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\r\n\r\nCurrent FRNs include:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * American Community Survey and Puerto Rico Community Survey [ https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/12/19/2025-23329/agency-information-collection-activities-submission-to-the-office-of-management-and-budget-omb-for?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0(Comment period ends Feb. 17) \r\n  * Annual Integrated Economic Survey [ https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/01/20/2026-00924/agency-information-collection-activities-submission-to-the-office-of-management-and-budget-omb-for?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0(Comment period ends Feb. 19) \r\n  * Automated Export System [ https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/01/26/2026-01432/agency-information-collection-activities-submission-to-the-office-of-management-and-budget-omb-for?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0(Comment period ends Feb. 25) \r\n  * 2026 Operational Test in Support of the 2030 Census [ https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/02/03/2026-02206/agency-information-collection-activities-submission-to-the-office-of-management-and-budget-omb-for?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0(Comment period ends March 5) \r\n\r\n*Recently Released*\r\n\r\n*(Released since Jan. 23, 2026)**\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*2024 Community Resilience Estimates* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2024-cre-natural-hazard-risk-tables.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 29 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released new community resilience estimates by social vulnerability to natural disasters. This product helps local governments and community stakeholders plan mitigation and recovery strategies in the event of a disaster. Estimates were released for the nation, states, counties, core-based statistical areas and tracts.*\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*American Community Survey**\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-Year Citizen Voting Age by Race and Ethnicity Special Tabulation\xc2\xa0 [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/decennial-census/about/voting-rights/cvap.2024.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#list-tab-1518558936 ]*\xe2\x80\x94 Jan.\xc2\xa030 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released the 2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-Year Citizen Voting Age by Race and Ethnicity (CVAP) special tabulation. This special tabulation is created for use in voting rights analysis and is published for a series of geographies, down to block-group level. Publication of this special tabulation is only available for download from the Census Bureau\xc2\xa0Citizen Voting Age by Race and Ethnicity\xc2\xa0webpage [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/decennial-census/about/voting-rights/cvap.2024.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#list-tab-1518558936 ].\r\n\r\n*2020-2024 American Community Survey\xc2\xa0* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-gains-educational-attainment.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 29 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released the remaining 2024 American Community Survey (ACS) estimates. The data was released Jan. 29 and included the 2020-2024 ACS 5-year estimates and 5-year Variance Replicate Estimates. The 5-year estimates were available to embargo subscribers on Jan. 27. The last release of 2020-2024 ACS 5-year PUMS (Public Use Microdata Sample) files is set for March 5. The updated\xc2\xa0release schedule [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/news/data-releases/2024/release-schedule.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0is available online.\xc2\xa0Spanish [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/acs-5-year-gains-educational-attainment/acs-5-year-gains-educational-attainment-spanish.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*Demographic*\r\n\r\n*Social and Economic Characteristics of Currently Unmarried Women With a Recent Birth: 2023* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/births-to-unmarried-women-declined.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 28 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released a new report that explores social and economic characteristics of unmarried women who gave birth in 2023. The report uses American Community Survey [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (ACS) data and makes comparisons, when possible, to an earlier report [ https://www2.census.gov/library/publications/2013/acs/acs-21.pdf?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] that used 2011 ACS 1-year estimates.\r\n\r\n*Small Area Income and Poverty Estimates for States, Counties and School Districts* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2024-saipe.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 27 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released new data on small area income and poverty estimates for states, counties and school districts. The new data come from the 2024\xc2\xa0Small Area Income and Poverty Estimates [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/saipe.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0(SAIPE), which provides the only up-to-date, single-year income and poverty statistics for the nation\xe2\x80\x99s 3,143\xc2\xa0counties and 13,126\xc2\xa0school districts.\r\n\r\n*Vintage 2025\xc2\xa0Population Estimates, Components of Change\xc2\xa0and Voting-Age Population for the Nation, States\xc2\xa0and Puerto Rico\xc2\xa0* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/population-growth-slows.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 27 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released July 1, 2025, estimates of total population and voting-age population for the nation, states and Puerto Rico, as well as corresponding annual estimates and components of change since the 2020 Census.\xc2\xa0Spanish [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/population-growth-slows/population-growth-slows-spanish.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*New Data Tables on Characteristics of Same-Sex Couple Households* [ https://www.census.gov/data/tables/time-series/demo/same-sex-couples/ssc-house-characteristics.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 26 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released new data tables from the 2024 American Community Survey 1-year estimates on Characteristics of Same-Sex Couple Households: 2005 to Present. The annual release explores demographic and economic characteristics of same-sex couple households by age, race, ethnicity, educational attainment, employment status, income and home tenure.*\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*Energy and Rental Assistance Fact Sheet* [ https://www.census.gov/library/fact-sheets/2026/demo/p70fs-213.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 26 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released a new fact sheet on energy and rental assistance based on data from the Survey of Income and Program Participation (SIPP). SIPP is a nationally representative longitudinal survey that provides comprehensive information on the dynamics of income, employment, household composition and government program participation. The fact sheet provides a quick and easy way to get statistics on recipients of energy and rental assistance for calendar year 2023.\r\n\r\n*Child Support Received Fact Sheet\xc2\xa0* [ https://www.census.gov/library/fact-sheets/2026/demo/p70fs-214.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 26 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released a new fact sheet on child support received based on data from the Survey of Income and Program Participation (SIPP). SIPP is a nationally representative longitudinal survey that provides comprehensive information on the dynamics of income, employment, household composition and government program participation. The fact sheet provides a quick and easy way to get statistics on parents who received child support in calendar year 2023.\r\n\r\n*Demographic Analysis and Population Projection System (DAPPS)\xc2\xa0* [ https://www.census.gov/data/software/dapps.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xe2\x80\x94 Dec. 3 \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released Demographic Analysis and Population Projection System (DAPPS 4.1 [ https://www.census.gov/data/software/dapps.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]). DAPPS is a comprehensive freely available software that offers advanced methods to analyze and project populations. It contains access to over 25 different techniques for analyzing population dynamics, such as age and sex distributions, fertility, mortality and migration.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*America Counts: Stories Behind the Numbers**\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*America Counts* [ https://www.census.gov/AmericaCounts?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] tells the stories behind the numbers in a new and inviting way. We feature stories on various topics such as families, housing, employment, business, education, the economy, emergency preparedness and the population.\r\n\r\n\r\n  * How Income Varies by Race and Geography [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/household-income-by-race-and-state.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (Jan. 29) \r\n  * Rental Costs Up, Mortgages Stayed Flat [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/housing-costs.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (Jan. 29) \r\n  * Share of Owner-Occupied, Mortgage-Free Homes Up in 2024 [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/mortgage-free-homes.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (Jan. 29) \r\n  * U.S. Population Growth Slowest Since COVID-19 Pandemic [ https://www.census.gov/library/stories/2026/01/pop-estimates-state-change.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (Jan. 27) \r\n\r\n*Stats for Stories**\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*Stats for Stories* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/stories.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] provides links to timely story ideas highlighting the U.S. Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s newsworthy statistics that relate to current events, observances, holidays and anniversaries. The story ideas are intended to assist the media in story mining and producing content for their respective audiences.\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Small Business Saturday: Nov. 29, 2025 [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/stories/small-business-saturday.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Blogs*\r\n\r\n*New Population Estimates Show Decline in Net International Migration* [ https://www.census.gov/newsroom/blogs/random-samplings/2026/01/historic-decline-in-net-international-migration.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \xe2\x80\x94 Jan. 27 \xe2\x80\x94 Written by: Population Estimates Program Staff, U.S. Census Bureau \xe2\x80\x94 The U.S. Census Bureau released a new series of population estimates that reflect demographic change since the 2020 Census. International migration is one of the most dynamic sources of demographic change and that has certainly been the case this decade.\r\n\r\n*Resources**\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*Emergency Management/Disaster Resources* \xe2\x80\x94 When major disasters strike, visit our Emergency Management webpage [ https://www.census.gov/topics/preparedness.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] for demographic and economic data on impacted areas. Each disaster will include data from our key emergency management tools: OnTheMap for Emergency Management, Community Resilience Estimates, Census Business Builder: Regional Analyst Edition and other useful resources.\r\n\r\n*Learn What Surveys Are Being Conducted in Your Community* \xe2\x80\x94 Discover which of the U.S. Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s annual surveys [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/surveyhelp.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] are being conducted in your community [ http://www.census.gov/regions/?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]. In a variety of surveys and censuses, evolving from the first census in 1790 [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/decennial-census/decade/1790/about-1790.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], the Census Bureau provides official information about America\xe2\x80\x99s people, businesses, industries and institutions. Learn more about surveys currently being conducted in each Census Bureau region:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Atlanta [ https://www.census.gov/about/regions/atlanta/surveys-programs.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * Chicago [ https://www.census.gov/about/regions/chicago/surveys-programs.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * Denver [ https://www.census.gov/about/regions/denver/surveys-programs.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * Los Angeles [ https://www.census.gov/about/regions/los-angeles/surveys-programs.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * New York [ https://www.census.gov/about/regions/new-york/surveys-programs.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * Philadelphia [ https://www.census.gov/about/regions/philadelphia/surveys-programs.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n  * All Surveys [ https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/surveyhelp/list-of-surveys.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\n*Data Tools*\r\n\r\nThe U.S. Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s interactive applications used to access statistics from our 130-plus annual surveys and programs. A complete list can be accessed on the Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s Data Tools and Apps [ https://www.census.gov/data/data-tools.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] webpage.\r\n\r\n*Training Opportunities*\r\n\r\n*U.S. Census Bureau Training Opportunities* \xe2\x80\x94 Webinars are available on a regular basis to help the public access and use Census Bureau statistics. These free sessions, which are 60 to 90 minutes each, show users how to navigate Census Bureau databases and mapping tools and find demographic and economic statistics at the local or national level. Descriptions of upcoming sessions are available on our Census Academy [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/upcoming.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] webpage. Login details are provided at least one week before a webinar.\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Unlocking NAICS 5- and 6-Digit Details in the QWI Data Set [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/upcoming.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (Wednesday, Feb. 18, 1:30-2:45 p.m. ET) \r\n  * Introduction to the ACS Public Use Microdata Sample (PUMS) Files [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars/upcoming.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] (Wednesday, Feb. 25, 2-3 p.m. ET) \r\n\r\n*Archived Training Resources* \xe2\x80\x94 Visit the U.S. Census Bureau\xe2\x80\x99s Educational Resource Library [ https://www.census.gov/data/academy/webinars.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] for previously recorded, free training available at your convenience. The library includes presentations, recorded webinars, tutorials and other helpful materials.\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nHelp us spread the word about Census Bureau data!\r\n\r\nShare this on social media or forward it to a friend.\r\n\r\n*Share This* [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/bulletins/4081dee ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nAbout the Census Bureau\r\n\r\nWe serve as the nation\xe2\x80\x99s leading provider of quality data about its people and economy.\xc2\xa0The Census Bureau is the federal government\'s largest statistical agency. As the world\xe2\x80\x99s premier statistical agency, we are dedicated to making our nation a better place. Policy-makers, businesses, and the public use our data to make informed decisions.\r\n\r\nResources for Media\r\n\r\nFor media interviews, please contact the\xc2\xa0Public Information Office [ https://lnks.gd/l/eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..p-5wpj2DTx0_qgyLiv6JuMTDOF_vZlHcwFpt971jIDs/s/866068797/br/124287751808-l?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Toll Free at 877-861-2010, 301-763-3030, or\xc2\xa0pio@census.gov.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\n*Stay connected with us!*\r\n\r\nJoin the conversation on social media.\r\n\r\n facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]linkedin [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ https://twitter.com/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/us-census-bureau/?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]youtube [ https://www.youtube.com/user/uscensusbureau/?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nSubscriber Settings [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/edit?preferences=true#tab1 ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Remove me from All Subscriptions  [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USCENSUS/subscriber/one_click_unsubscribe?verification=5.76359f46a06559a62e8e0404a80cc7e5&destination=jasonnorman66994%40gmail.com ]\xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\r\n\r\n \r\n&lt;!-- /* template top padding on mobile */ @media only screen and (max-width: 480px) { table#flexible-abe-main-table { padding:0 !important; } } --&gt; ________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThis is an official email from the U.S. Census Bureau. If you have any questions or comments, please contact us (http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html [ http://www.census.gov/about/contact-us.html?utm_campaign=20260206pios&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]).  \xc2\xa0 \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;} table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:7px; margin-right:7px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;}\r\n'
