[2026-04-27 11:14:00] Raw text/plain payload: b'If your email program has trouble displaying this email, view as a webpage [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USFDA/bulletins/4082a53 ].\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nUS Food and Drug Administration \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nFY26 Funding Opportunities for Antimicrobial Regulatory Science Research\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nDear Colleagues,\r\n\r\nI would like to inform you that the FDA will be accepting proposals focused on updating susceptibility test interpretive criteria (breakpoints).\r\n\r\nSpecifically, research proposals focused on evaluating microbiologic, pharmacokinetic/ pharmacodynamic, and clinical data that could be utilized by standards development organizations and the FDA to update breakpoints for "Candida auris "will be prioritized.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Request for Proposals to Facilitate Development of Susceptibility Test Interpretive Criteria (STIC or Breakpoints) for Candida auris [ https://www.fda.gov/media/190984/download?attachment=&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nProposals should be submitted to the FDA Broad Agency Announcement. *\xc2\xa0Please note that the BAA submission due date is February 24, 2026*.\r\n\r\nDetailed information to apply to this open announcement can be on: Office of Infectious Diseases Research Activities | FDA [ https://www.fda.gov/about-fda/center-drug-evaluation-and-research-cder/office-infectious-diseases-research-activities?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nPlease feel free to share this information with others who may be interested in applying.\r\n\r\n** If you did not subscribe to the FDA Recognized Antimicrobial STIC Breakpoints subscription you may unsubscribe from this list by clicking on the "Manage Preferences or Unsubscribe from this List" link below.\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n\r\nfeed [ https://www.fda.gov/about-fda/contact-fda/subscribe-podcasts-and-news-feeds?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]twitter [ 