[2026-04-27 11:14:08] Raw text/plain payload: b'Township of Radnor Pennsylvania \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*Radnor Township News & Events*\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nFebruary 6 - February 13, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nBishop Richard Allen 26 [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/4000/14?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/3984/14?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]Friday, February 13: 8th Annual Bishop Richard Allen Wreath Laying Ceremony [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/4000/14?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nOn Friday, February 13,\xc2\xa0join Radnor Township, members of the AME Community, and Friends as we celebrate the life and legacy of Bishop Richard Allen, and commemorate Bishop Richard Allen Park\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/4000/14?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nA Vision for Wayne [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/3969/14?loadingmode=PreviewContent&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nA Vision for Wayne Update 2026 [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/3969/14?loadingmode=PreviewContent&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/3969/14?loadingmode=PreviewContent&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\nRadnor Day Camp Registration 26 [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/4004/14?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nRadnor Day Camp Registration is NOW OPEN! [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/4004/14?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/4004/14?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nTownship News\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nRadnor Seal \r\nMonday, February 9, 2026: Board of Commissioners Meeting Notice [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/4002/14?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSnow Shovel \r\nWinter Weather Safety 2026 [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/3984/14?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nCPR CLASS \r\nWednesday, February 11, 2026: CPR Training Class Available [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/3998/14?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nA Vision for Radnor Logo \r\nThursday, February 5 2026: Get Involved in Shaping the Future of Downtown Wayne! [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/3971/14?loadingmode=PreviewContent&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSam Woods \r\nSam Woods Thomas Announced as First Economic Development Manager in Radnor [ https://www.radnor.com/Home/Components/News/News/3976/14?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nParks & Recreation\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nIn the event of unforeseen situations, such as those imposed by inclement weather or health and safety issues, cancelations may occur for any program or event listed below. **Please note, health & safety protocols will be implemented.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nPrograms [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/default.aspx?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nThe Parks & Recreation Department offers a wide range of programs for residents of all ages. Click the link above for a complete list of programs currently available and to register.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nRadnor Day Camp [ https://www.radnor.com/government/departments/parks-recreation/radnor-day-camp?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nRegistration is opening Monday at 9am for our 2026 Radnor Day Camp taking place the weeks of June 22\xc2\xa0\xe2\x80\x93 July 31 at Radnor High School! This six week, full day or half day camp is for children entering grades 1-9. Join us for 6 weeks of summer fun that will include a wide variety of weekly activities including arts & crafts, sports & games, swimming, field trips, performing arts, water games, and more! Once again we will also be offering aftercare for camp families from 3pm-5pm. For full details, FAQs, and online registration visit\xc2\xa0www.radnor.com/RDC [ https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?data=05%7C02%7Cimyers%40radnor.org%7C54abdf2dc7904544cd0908de603d7ce1%7Cb321154193fc4b5cb1808f75e9cfe8b5%7C0%7C0%7C639054014366133258%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&reserved=0&sdata=ZUEL8Hpxcz4aYeM89T74ObhgR%2BNo9MPSil5uoa%2B8GLM%3D&url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.radnor.com%2FRDC%3Futm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dgovdelivery&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ].\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nWicked On Broadway Bus Trip [ https://radnorpa.myrec.com/info/activities/program_details.aspx?ProgramID=30296&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nOn Saturday, April 11th\xc2\xa0take a trip to New York City to see Wicked on Broadway! Registration includes tickets to the 2:00 PM Wicked performance at the Gershwin Theatre and roundtrip transportation on deluxe motor coach.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n15th\xc2\xa0Annual Radnor Sweetheart Valentine\xe2\x80\x99s Dance [ https://www.radnor.com/government/departments/parks-recreation/community-events/radnor-sweetheart-valentine-s-dance?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#!/ ]\r\n\r\nRadnor Sweetheart Valentine\xe2\x80\x99s Dance will take place on Friday, February 6th (inclement weather date 2/20) from 6:30 PM to 8:30 PM at The Inn at Villanova University. We have an exciting night planned for registered families attending that will include music & dancing, refreshments, caricatures, and fun crafts!\xc2\xa0Registration currently closed. Click the link above to sign up for the event wait list.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nBishop Richard Allen Wreath Laying Ceremony\r\n\r\nOn Friday, February 13th join members of the African United Methodist AME community, friends, and Radnor Township Staff as we celebrate the life and legacy of Bishop Richard Allen and commemorate his historic walk to Radnor in 1784\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nRadnor Wizarding Summer Camp [ https://www.radnor.com/government/departments/parks-recreation/recreational-programming/wizarding-camp?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nRegistration opens Wednesday, January 21st\xc2\xa0for our 2026 Radnor Wizarding Summer Camp taking place the weeks of August 3-7, August 10-14, or August 17-21 at Hill Top Preparatory School. This one week, full day camp is for the Harry Potter fan in grades 1-8. This dynamic camp allows children the opportunity to engage in a variety of creative, physical, and social activities throughout the week! Click the link above to learn more.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nCalling Local Community Organizations, Institutions, and Groups [ https://www.radnor.com/government/departments/parks-recreation/draft-community-events?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nWe would like to ask for your consideration in participating at our many community events this year. Our community events offer an opportunity to interact with members of the community by providing information about your organization and services, providing fun giveaways, conducting interactive games, and even having fundraisers that will help your organization. There is no fee to attend any of the great events taking place. Click the link above to see the 2026 event schedule and please contact our department if you are interested in learning more or attending any of the number of events being offered. \xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nAttention Skunk Hollow Park & Trails Dog Walkers\r\n\r\nOrdinance 2024-01 was adopted by the Board of Commissioners on 2/26/24 \xe2\x80\x93 All dogs must be on a leash on Saturdays, Sundays and on all Township holidays (Township Holiday schedule is established by the Township on an annual basis) from 12:00 PM (noon) to the closing of the park at dusk. Reminder that Dogs are NOT Permitted at the Willows Park. Dogs must be on a leash in the Willows Park parking lot before entering the trail. Please\xc2\xa0click here [ https://ecode360.com/10972855?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#10972860 ]\xc2\xa0to view Ordinance 2024-01 and please\xc2\xa0click here [ https://www.radnor.com/government/departments/parks-recreation/parks-facilities/dogs-in-township-parks?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0for more information about dogs in parks and on trails.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nEnvironmental and Nature Initiatives [ https://radnor.prod.govaccess.org/government/departments/parks-recreation/environmental-nature-initiatives?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\nThe Parks & Recreation Department offers a variety of ongoing and annual events to celebrate our parks & trails.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nSign up for our Weekly Recreation E-Newsletter! [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/PARADNOR/subscriber/new?topic_id=PARADNOR_2&pop=t ]\r\n\r\nStay updated on all the happenings in the Recreation & Community Programming Department!\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nYou can also follow us on\xc2\xa0Facebook [ https://www.facebook.com/Radnor-Township-Recreation-Department-1154615594746513/?modal=admin_todo_tour&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0and\xc2\xa0Instagram [ https://www.instagram.com/radnorrecreation/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]!\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nTownship Meetings\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n*Board of Commissioners* [ https://www.radnor.com/government/boards-and-commissions/board-of-commissioners?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nMonday, February 9, 2026 - 6:30 PM\r\n@ Radnorshire Room\r\n\r\n*Design Review Board* [ https://www.radnor.com/government/boards-and-commissions/design-review-board?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nWednesday, February 11, 2026 - 6:00 PM\r\n@ Radnorshire Room\r\n\r\n*Parks and Recreation Board* [ https://www.radnor.com/government/boards-and-commissions/parks-recreation-board?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\nThursday, February 12, 2026 - 6:30 PM\r\n@ Radnorshire Room\r\n\r\n*Agendas & Minutes* [ https://radnor.prod.govaccess.org/government/agendas-minutes?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nTownship Projects\r\n\r\nRadnor Township is committed to improving the quality of life of its residents through a variety of projects, be it stormwater and sewer, or general township initiatives. Check this page for information regarding completed and current projects. Your engagement and understanding are crucial to us, and we invite you to learn more about these efforts aimed at making our Township a better place for all.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Learn More* [ https://www.radnor.com/government/departments/engineering/township-projects?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nUpdate your subscriptions, modify your password or email address, or stop subscriptions at any time on your Subscriber Preferences Page [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/PARADNOR/subscriber/new?preferences=true ]. You will need to use your email address to log in. If you have questions or problems with the subscription service, please visit subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]. \r\n\r\nThis service is provided to you at no charge by Township of Radnor, PA [ https://www.radnor.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]. \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using govDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: Township of Radnor, PA \xc2\xb7 301 Iven Avenue \xc2\xb7 Wayne, PA 19087-5297 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block {min-height: 5px;}\r\n'
