hSuY-2FpSR6GBGaO7k60MAt8-2F8cK3LSZkC8T-2FbsgTsPQVdTuz8z1Zuz21egrdQHRh08VsuK4cKMVsLoOlQ3AEar2IfcW6ytF54ixtxSwmqPG3ddZ8IoDAA73aYt839gnCRN3HN7PjLZeoYV-2BqJZxAfqUQNXYrGZMy6HMBi4JjJjAc-2FsuGE-2B18U-2BkyTdBEthYWXLIvNjQlzkZ319AvMd72lUlOaok-2FPZKHoGW5DyompdsKamyUNbv2ztwJaTA1ePbV0hXlRf2TIsqzqj5HJ6fE2A7-2B2t7B2Sq4e5TktjYezWlLDMI04N1Us7lAxis5UYvn9sr1bmQzFA )WEEK AHEAD ON WALL STREET\r\nA Read on Both Jobs and\r\nInflationwallstreet.png(\r\nhttps://ablink.newsletter.sofi.com/ls/click?upn=u001.k-2FImUMyJvquSjfrastfytIPj6h1-2BVfWjnUDDp-2FeYQFLpjhu-2F6ot-2F5dL1x7ZEqHyiUNGtzFkjjgTRgCH88hkgWT22B5jOlxdZRMhlZE7Og1Ie5AULKjAjSa9Qe-2BCq6VCLjkmev7vRKTs2KxxXPYXDcX0CZs5cHfQ2OIw4uE7m5G1ZgaWdzso10GwTgZ2d-2FqsYIdDnCcNDL7BUdvlJ5bAHwZ6glzf9od9lildAvHKuXUtg7c3kCpKTs-2Bl-2BUDAW-2FGs2G62jByoWpJevVh2N52l8Tw-3D-3DIdmh_Hvirw9jLOYnqUg7ucIAtvDa4JCWhfjePQT8cfdKWfeKaKK6WyzUu0MT5hcL83ezarLAJeFzEeRP-2BR0XWfLa6cxqR1rUjaeXRVZL0m0KysVzvmopG2Xl5-2Bz0drIJajW7pnpfaRrlBjxzb-2FGH4SrLlxIAf5oRc10RCkGj8bURHHKFas8UEXfxGog4jdYLkvTwr36Z5JT461foy0-2BsUIZ-2BGJRwvlk7O2WjB4dl-2FX4-2B9VZlsY8iWVy9hItN0ZX1qTde7hgsBntOTQyy91-2FpR-2FZrNH1bmIwkGAS1CBVtvnHuXAQYfToOr4y9bbBrh37HKg8i-2FgTsEk-2B8fxVVlAnkHNtF0ByViQinpX5nWuU9q3HlpUCDzpZgrVCiEpzhqhiMB5JqQWsZzBdAbZ81mem4zZDSOJG-2FUz4cY0s9fxtR4NAHBHAATtNNuEgoCRIEhSuY-2FpSR6GBGaO7k60MAt8-2F8cK3LSZkC8T-2FbsgTsPQVdTuz8z1Zuz21egrdQHRh08VsuK4cKMVsLoOlQ3AEar2IfcW6ytF54ixtxSwmqPG3ddZ8IoDAA73aYt839gnCRN3HN7PjLZeoYV-2BqJZxAfqUQNXYrGZMy6HMBi4JjJjAc-2FsuGE-2B18W6UqQWUyUD0lb4gLyTeQ5QdZxl-2F6M27bpav8vPRPhF1v0UICbAORczFgusgickYpAmEMuF340qudFq4zUDmXmCnYbSiB-2FmrmhVtdBoxrTcG5eDfFATdlKZPsOvVDS9IBMX4VRj-2BX31K2Q-2FWW9V1TQ-2B\r\n)By Mario Ismailanji\r\n\r\nThe market is pretty pessimistic about interest rate relief,\r\nwith traders pricing in about a 25% chance that the Federal\r\nReserve will cut the benchmark interest rate at its March\r\nmeeting.\r\n\r\nBut this week we\xe2\x80\x99ll get a double dose of data to help gauge\r\nwhether that pessimism is justified, with both the January jobs\r\nreport and consumer inflation report scheduled for release\r\nfollowing last week\xe2\x80\x99s brief government shutdown.\r\n\r\n* If the data runs "hot" (more jobs added, higher inflation\r\nthan expected), that 25% chance could drop to zero. This means\r\nthat, all else being equal, mortgage rates, auto loans and credit\r\ncard APRs could stay elevated or even tick higher as the market\r\nadapts to a stronger economy.\r\n* If the data runs "cold" (fewer jobs added, lower inflation than\r\nexpected), the odds of a March cut could spike. This would likely\r\nspark a rally in stocks and send Treasury yields down, eventually\r\noffering some relief on borrowing costs.\r\nWhether you are trading a portfolio or just waiting to\r\nrefinance a home, these numbers could go a long way in setting\r\nthe market tone as recent upheaval leaves investors on edge.Keep&nbsp;reading (\r\nhttps://ablink.newsletter.sofi.com/ls/click?upn=u001.k-2FImUMyJvquSjfrastfytIPj6h1-2BVfWjnUDDp-2FeYQFLpjhu-2F6ot-2F5dL1x7ZEqHyiUNGtzFkjjgTRgCH88hkgWT22B5jOlxdZRMhlZE7Og1Ie5AULKjAjSa9Qe-2BCq6VCLjkmev7vRKTs2KxxXPYXDcX0CZs5cHfQ2OIw4uE7m5G1ZgaWdzso10GwTgZ2d-2FqsYIdDnCcNDL7BUdvlJ5bAHwZ6glzf9od9lildAvHKuXUuUyEFs9J44Tlyeg5PRHQVWIM6Uis-2FfvCzyXS17pV-2FFMw-3D-3Dsfl4_Hvirw9jLOYnqUg7ucIAtvDa4JCWhfjePQT8cfdKWfeKaKK6WyzUu0MT5hcL83ezarLAJeFzEeRP-2BR0XWfLa6cxqR1rUjaeXRVZL0m0KysVzvmopG2Xl5-2Bz0drIJajW7pnpfaRrlBjxzb-2FGH4SrLlxIAf5oRc10RCkGj8bURHHKFas8UEXfxGog4jdYLkvTwr36Z5JT461foy0-2BsUIZ-2BGJRwvlk7O2WjB4dl-2FX4-2B9VZlsY8iWVy9hItN0ZX1qTde7hgsBntOTQyy91-2FpR-2FZrNH1bmIwkGAS1CBVtvnHuXAQYfToOr4y9bbBrh37HKg8i-2FgTsEk-2B8fxVVlAnkHNtF0ByViQinpX5nWuU9q3HlpUCDzpZgrVCiEpzhqhiMB5JqQWsZzBdAbZ81mem4zZDSOJG-2FUz4cY0s9fxtR4NAHBHAATtNNuEgoCRIEhSuY-2FpSR6GBGaO7k60MAt8-2F8cK3LSZkC8T-2FbsgTsPQVdTuz8z1Zuz21egrdQHRh08VsuK4cKMVsLoOlQ3AEar2IfcW6ytF54ixtxSwmqPG3ddZ8IoDAA73aYt839gnCRN3HN7PjLZeoYV-2BqJZxAfqUQNXYrGZMy6HMBi4JjJjAc-2FsuGE-2B18V3g8YNzf8zPgcb6f-2BxmIc9chvMK1ss0Dhg2HRIdyS4TEkfD8H3KNucy1sS80C1Ca99lZiAcv7zGPP-2BQ6Nr0vWtsDZKM-2BTVX2968V-2BdPxUGV