[2026-04-27 11:16:05] Raw text/plain payload: b'OEJNewsletter [ https://dep.nj.gov/ej/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nNEW JERSEY DEPARTMENT OF ENVIRONMENTAL PROTECTION\r\n\r\nOFFICE OF ENVIRONMENTAL JUSTICE\r\nBI-WEEKLY NEWSLETTER\r\n\r\nFebruary 9th, 2026\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nTable of Contents\r\n\r\n  * ANNOUNCEMENTS [ #link_1 ] \r\n  * PARTICIPATION OPPORTUNITIES [ #link_2 ] \r\n  * FUNDING & TECHNICAL ASSISTANCE [ #link_3 ] \r\n\r\nSummary of Important Events\r\n\r\n*Upcoming EJ Law Hearings*\r\n\r\n*February 12*\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n* Siegfried USA, LLC [ https://dep.nj.gov/wp-content/uploads/ej/siegfried-notice-20260212.pdf?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]*\r\n\r\n(EJ Rule Title V Renewal)- Pennsville, Salem County\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*April 22*\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*Nipro Pharmapackaging Americas Corp [ https://dep.nj.gov/wp-content/uploads/ej/nipro-notice-20260422.pdf?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*(EJ Rule Title V Renewal)- Millville, Cumberland County\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nANNOUNCEMENTS\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nDEP SEEKS COMMUNITY PARTNERS FOR ITS ANNUAL YOUTH INCLUSION INITIATIVE TO EMPOWER FUTURE ENVIRONMENTAL LEADERS\r\n\r\nyii [ https://dep.nj.gov/yii/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nThe Department of Environmental Protection invites community-based organizations across the state to apply for grants to participate in its annual Youth Inclusion Initiative. [ https://dep.nj.gov/yii/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] *The six-week summer program provides young people from overburdened communities with training in environmental careers, building a more inclusive workforce and boosting community connections* Local environmental organizations, higher education institutions, and community advocacy or religious groups can now apply for grants that provide up to $100,000 per organization to support the recruitment, supervision, and mentorship of participants aged 16 to 20.\r\n\r\nProgram participants will receive hands-on training and guidance from DEP professionals, gaining valuable skills and knowledge across a wide range of environmental fields.\xc2\xa0Each group that receives grant funding will also complete community projects that reduce pollution, enhance green spaces and increase community pride.\r\n\r\n*A webinar providing an overview of the grants\' details is scheduled for Feb. 12. Proposals are due** March 12th, 2026.*\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*LEARN MORE AND APPLY NOW* [ https://dep.nj.gov/yii/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\nDEP UNVEILS VISION & ACTION PLAN FOR NEW JERSEY\xe2\x80\x99S NEWEST STATE PARK, A NINE-MILE GREENWAY IN ESSEX AND HUDSON COUNTIES\r\n\r\ngreenway [ https://dep.nj.gov/newsrel/26_0005/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n\r\nOn January 16th, former Environmental Protection Commissioner Shawn LaTourette unveiled the Vision & Action Plan [ https://dep.nj.gov/newsrel/26_0005/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] for New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s newest state park, a nine-mile greenway in Essex and Hudson counties. The plan looks beyond the nearly one-mile Newark segment of the project which broke ground in July, and establishes the foundational framework that will guide planning, design and investment for the remaining eight miles of the future park. *The future park traverses several overburdened communities that have historically lacked access to open space and face disproportionate environmental and public health challenges. Development of the park represents a significant step toward addressing these disparities and expanding access to nature and recreation.\xc2\xa0*Continued community engagement will be essential to realizing the full potential of the Vision & Action Plan for the greenway, ensuring the park serves\xc2\xa0each of the communities it will\xc2\xa0touch \xe2\x80\x93 Jersey City, Secaucus, Kearny, Newark, Belleville, Bloomfield, Glen\xc2\xa0Ridge\xc2\xa0and Montclair.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*READ THE VISION & ACTION PLAN AND LEARN MORE* [ https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/urban-state-parks-initiatives/greenway/future-vision/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nPARTICIPATION OPPORTUNITIES\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nUPCOMING ENVIRONMENTAL JUSTICE LAW PUBLIC HEARINGS\r\n\r\n*February 12-* Siegfried USA, LLC- Title V Renewal, EJ Rule (hybrid) [ https://dep.nj.gov/wp-content/uploads/ej/siegfried-notice-20260212.pdf?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*April 22-* Nipro Pharmapackaging Americas Corp, Title V Renewal, EJ Rule (hybrid) [ https://dep.nj.gov/wp-content/uploads/ej/nipro-notice-20260422.pdf?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\r\n\r\n*EJ LAW PUBLIC HEARINGS* [ https://dep.nj.gov/ej/meetings/?ceid=&emci=645e6286-83a3-f011-8e61-6045bded8ba4&emdi=ea000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\nREGISTER NOW FOR THE NEW JERSEY COASTAL AND CLIMATE RESILIENCE CONFERENCE!\r\n\r\nThe New Jersey Coastal Resilience Collaborative (NJCRC) and Department of Environmental Protection (NJDEP) will host the 2026 New Jersey Coastal & Climate Resilience Conference [ https://www.njcoastalresilience.org/nj-coastal-and-climate-resilience-conference/2026-new-jersey-coastal-and-climate-resilience-conference/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] from\xc2\xa0*Monday, March 9, through Wednesday, March 11,\xc2\xa0*at the Seaview Hotel in Galloway. With a theme of \xe2\x80\x9cNavigating Changing Tides,\xe2\x80\x9d the event will build on the success of our\xc2\xa02024 conference [ https://www.njcoastalresilience.org/nj-coastal-and-climate-resilience-conference/2024-new-jersey-coastal-and-climate-resilience-conference-2/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], with hundreds of coastal and climate resilience professionals to gather, learn, collaborate and celebrate during the three-day event.\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*County and municipal continuing education credits are now available at the conference!*\xc2\xa0CMFO, CCFO, CPWM, RMC (8.5 contact hours), QPA (7.0 contact hours), and CTC (4.0 contact hours) CEUs can all be earned by attending.\r\n\r\n*REGISTER NOW* [ https://www.njcoastalresilience.org/nj-coastal-and-climate-resilience-conference/2026-new-jersey-coastal-and-climate-resilience-conference/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\nOPEN FOR PUBLIC COMMENT: NATIONAL URBAN AND COMMUNITY FORESTRY TEN-YEAR ACTION PLAN\r\n\r\nThe National Urban and Community Forestry Ten-Year Action Plan\xe2\x80\x99s public input website [ https://sites.google.com/view/nucf-plan-update-2027/home?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] is now live. This Action Plan creates a guiding framework that optimizes innovations, resources, and collaborations for the field of urban and community forestry. It also drives federal funding priorities for Urban and Community Forestry and serves as a guidance document for State Urban and Community Forestry Programs and Forest Action Plans.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nInput gathered is part of the stakeholder engagement process and will help update the NUCF Ten Year Action Plan. Feedback supports better data, gap assessments and goal setting, which is critical for managing extreme heat, public health, and urban growth.\r\n\r\n*Comments must be submitted by May 31st, 2026 at 5:00 PM.*\r\n\r\n*SUBMIT COMMENTS AND LEARN MORE* [ https://sites.google.com/view/nucf-plan-update-2027/home?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nFUNDING & TECHNICAL ASSISTANCE\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nLEAD HAZARD REDUCTION CAPACITY BUILDING GRANT PROGRAM\r\n\r\nAdministered through the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development, the Lead Hazard Reduction Capacity Building Grant Program provides resources to rebuild infrastructure for lead hazard control programs. It assists jurisdictions in developing systems, hiring qualified staff, and creating partnerships to identify and mitigate lead-based paint hazards in eligible housing. The goal is to ensure sustainable capacity through strategies such as data-driven targeting, integration with housing programs, and collaboration between health and housing agencies.\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n*Applications are due February 26th, 2026.\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*LEARN MORE AND APPLY NOW* [ https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://bprc9c50.r.us-east-1.awstrack.me/L0/https:*2F*2Fwww.grants.gov*2Fsearch-results-detail*2F361107/1/02000000lmfop927-juscmaqr-d6j8-169p-rme7-7n3gc4ib0g00-000000/GApb6WnI09bNh6cY4mWoP6OYLF8=460__;JSUlJQ!!J30X0ZrnC1oQtbA!JhlobpDAMztGRJjmTJAXRK0vJ2tnaPv6v03BHIRJxnfXFbYhfH7mZGFi7Y5SsYFUWArXwhlzmqUzU1N3DuRbzzuCp2RM0fOUKQ%24?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\nAPPLICATIONS NOW OPEN FOR GREEN ACRES 2026 FUNDING ROUND!\r\n\r\nNJDEP\'s Green Acres Program [ https://dep.nj.gov/greenacres/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] is pleased to announce [ https://dep.nj.gov/newsrel/25_0050/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] its 2026 funding round.\xc2\xa0 *Applications for land acquisition, park development, and stewardship projects will be accepted. [ https://dep.nj.gov/greenacres/forms-and-regulations/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#green-acres-application-forms ] This year, a**pplicants are no longer limited to one acquisition or one park development funding request.* All applicants may submit up to one request of each of the three funding categories.\r\n\r\nFor questions at any time, please consult the Green Acres Contacts [ https://dep.nj.gov/greenacres/contact-us/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#local-and-nonprofit-assistance ] page and reach out to the Project Manager who handles projects in your area.\r\n\r\n*All applications are due\xc2\xa0February 27, 2026.*\r\n\r\n*LEARN MORE AND APPLY NOW* [ https://dep.nj.gov/greenacres/2026-funding/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\nCLIMATE SMART COMMUNITIES INITIATIVE\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nThe Climate Smart Communities Initiative (CSCI) [ https://climatesmartcommunity.org/funding/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] is pleased to announce the launch of the 2026 CSCI grants opportunity for US-based climate resilience projects.\r\n\r\n*Funded in part through the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Association, CSCI awards provide funding and technical assistance to advance community-based climate resilience in US communities or regions that are highly vulnerable to the impacts of climate change.* The total grants budget is $1.5-2 million and grants typically range from $75,000 to $115,000 based on the scope of work proposed in the application.\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\nThe program prioritizes funding for communities that include historically disinvested populations at increased risk to climate-related impacts. It is open to US-based project teams composed of a climate adaptation practitioner and representatives from a local or regional government entity and a community-based organization.\r\n\r\n*Applications are due March 12th, 2025.\xc2\xa0*\r\n\r\n*LEARN MORE AND APPLY NOW* [ https://climatesmartcommunity.org/funding/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\nSOLID WASTE RECYCLING ENHANCEMENT ACT HIGHER EDUCATION RESEARCH GRANT PROGRAM\r\n\r\nThe Solid Waste Recycling Enhancement Act (REA) Higher Education Research Grant Program [ https://dep.nj.gov/grantandloanprograms/solid-waste-recycling-enhancement-act-rea-higher-education-research-grant-program/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] is now accepting applications. The program funds projects that support the objectives of the Recycling Enhancement Act. Proposals may be designed to enhance existing resources, tools, or methodologies, or create new resources pursuant to the Recycling Enhancement Act. New Jersey institutions of higher education are eligible to apply and may collaborate with permitted entities. \r\n\r\n*Applications are due April 24, 2026, at 3PM.*\r\n\r\n*LEARN MORE AND APPLY NOW* [ https://dep.nj.gov/grantandloanprograms/solid-waste-recycling-enhancement-act-rea-higher-education-research-grant-program/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\n\r\n$19 MILLION IN FUNDING STILL AVAILABLE THROUGH DEP\'s NATURAL CLIMATE SOLUTIONS GRANT PROGRAM\r\n\r\nThe New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection (DEP) recently announced the award of nearly $11 million in Natural Climate Solutions grants [ https://dep.nj.gov/newsrel/25_0057/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] for three projects that will help mitigate greenhouse gas emissions by restoring coastal marshland and expanding urban tree canopy. The projects are located in Stone Harbor, Stafford and Montclair. The grants, funded through New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s participation in the Regional Greenhouse Gas Initiative (RGGI), are part of an ongoing $30 million second round of funding for local governments and nonprofits to implement projects that mitigate greenhouse gas impacts by creating, restoring, and enhancing coastal wetlands, forests and urban tree canopies.\r\n\r\nDEP continues to accept applications [ https://urldefense.com/v3/__https:/links-2.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:*2F*2Fdep.nj.gov*2Fclimatechange*2Fmitigation*2Fncs-grant*2F*3Futm_medium=email*26utm_source=govdelivery/1/0101019b3787c3a5-66428e45-a896-4205-8118-9850a6a90d7e-000000/xhwm9pNMA17o5Fo4zYwbbob88NXBxrCPgWx89DHdvZE=436__;JSUlJSUlJSU!!J30X0ZrnC1oQtbA!Ig9FgxVXE76lLrcjLduxylWdn28XQ-b63L-CkVhI0HkhrfK2R6gLAxgHhh4tukrOxO-BKtDvxIOIFG2TzxJ-xdXQz027hBVg%24?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] on a first-come, first-served basis through a rolling admission period.* Approximately 19 million in second round funding is still available for blue and green carbon sequestration initiatives. *Eligible projects include the creation of living shorelines, restoring tidal flows in tidal wetlands and tidal salt marsh vegetation, restoring forests, and enhancing urban forest canopy and water quality.\r\n\r\n*LEARN MORE AND APPLY NOW* [ https://www.epa.gov/brownfields/marc-grant-application-resources?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery#Open%20Solicitations ] \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n*All New Jersey residents, regardless of income, race, ethnicity, color, or national origin, have a right to live, work, and recreate in a clean and healthy environment. Historically, New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s low-income communities and communities of color face a disproportionately high number of environmental and public health stressors and, as a result, suffer from increased adverse health effects. New Jersey seeks to correct these outcomes by furthering the promise of environmental justice.*\r\n\r\n*DEP\xe2\x80\x99s Office of Environmental Justice (OEJ) [ https://www.nj.gov/dep/ej/aboutus.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0aims to improve the quality of life in New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s most vulnerable communities by educating and empowering communities who are often outside of government decision-making processes and guiding DEP\xe2\x80\x99s programs and other state departments and agencies in implementing environmental justice.*\r\n\r\nOEJLogoFooter  \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n  \r\n \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n"The New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection is dedicated to protecting New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s environment and public health. The agency prioritizes addressing climate change, protecting New Jersey\xe2\x80\x99s water, revitalizing its communities and managing and promoting its natural and historic resources."\r\n\r\n"For the most recent information, follow the DEP on Twitter @NewJerseyDEP [ https:/www.twitter.com/NewJerseyDEP?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ], Facebook @newjerseydep, Instagram @nj.dep, and LinkedIn @newjerseydep, or visit dep.nj.gov [ https://dep.nj.gov/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]."\r\n\r\n Like and Follow DEP*\r\n*Facebook [ https://www.nj.gov/dep/facebook.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0Twitter-X [ https://twitter.com/NewJerseyDEP?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]\xc2\xa0LinkedIn [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/nj-department-of-environmental-protection/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery&viewAsMember=true ]\xc2\xa0Instagram [ https://www.nj.gov/dep/instagram.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] YouTube [ https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC2C01lO4mVInYzqqwevFvSw?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ]  \r\n\r\nSUBSCRIBER SERVICES:\r\n\r\nManage Preferences [ http://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Unsubscribe [ https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/NJDEP/subscribers/new?preferences=true ] \xc2\xa0|\xc2\xa0 Help [ https://subscriberhelp.govdelivery.com/ ]\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n"\xc2\xa0"\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n This email was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com using GovDelivery Communications Cloud on behalf of: New Jersey Department of Environmental Protection \xc2\xb7 401 E. State St. \xc2\xb7 Trenton, NJ 08625 GovDelivery logo [ https://subscriberhelp.granicus.com/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery ] \r\n \r\nbody .abe-column-block { min-height: 5px; } table.gd_combo_table img {margin-left:10px; margin-right:10px;} table.gd_combo_table div.govd_image_display img, table.gd_combo_table td.gd_combo_image_cell img {margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px;} table.govd_hr {min-width: 100%;}\r\n'
