d \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad \xc2\xad\r\n\r\n3M learners (https://learn.educative.io/e3t/Ctc/RG+113/cz5H404/VWJNx93QrbXnW7mV4dL5BhqJ3W8VsNl15Kkh_5N7Hm8xT3prCCW7Y8-PT6lZ3lXW5PnCvc8hMdrjVKfXbZ2Rw3G8W6WMcfN7p4JZVW95wTrj4b3-zxW4cL_JD78T2nrW33N3zn8SnQ0VW2wRzf12NkY-pW2ppFk21wW-hRW5mW0Sy58LtDtN5y-yts5DnwYW1X8vWJ1nDP7_W4yftfg1wJmr2W6hwTnS5n3pr9W2-zSfl7vFNStW7_kZsy1CymyjW8Khgn863Ww0BW6NzS6r40BJgmW4YQgsn7sr0NVW7yMHyN4Lw-9sW288kkh2ZfYr7N8wkmBDKTwjpW2DZBpM2dR5m2W57QlwX286TXjW9fsnX17KcJt-W8h2DC-8KNwl3W2W902C1wy-Dff5vQHcq04 )\r\n\r\nJasonnorman,\r\n\r\nA quick note before we get started: we're still celebrating our milestone of 3 million developers learning with Educative. That means you can get 50% off (or more) (https://learn.educative.io/e3t/Ctc/RG+113/cz5H404/VWJNx93QrbXnW7mV4dL5BhqJ3W8VsNl15Kkh_5N7Hm8xT3prCCW7Y8-PT6lZ3lXW5PnCvc8hMdrjVKfXbZ2Rw3G8W6WMcfN7p4JZVW95wTrj4b3-zxW4cL_JD78T2nrW33N3zn8SnQ0VW2wRzf12NkY-pW2ppFk21wW-hRW5mW0Sy58LtDtN5y-yts5DnwYW1X8vWJ1nDP7_W4yftfg1wJmr2W6hwTnS5n3pr9W2-zSfl7vFNStW7_kZsy1CymyjW8Khgn863Ww0BW6NzS6r40BJgmW4YQgsn7sr0NVW7yMHyN4Lw-9sW288kkh2ZfYr7N8wkmBDKTwjpW2DZBpM2dR5m2W57QlwX286TXjW9fsnX17KcJt-W8h2DC-8KNwl3W2W902C1wy-Dff5vQHcq04 ) on all Educative subscriptions\xe2\x80\x94which all include access Fenzo.\r\n\r\nWhat's Fenzo, you ask? Well that's what I wanted to talk about today.\r\n\r\nAI is a double edged sword.\r\n\r\nI'm not talking about ethics or hallucinations right now.\r\n\r\nI'm talking about using it for learning.\r\n\r\nFor the most part, AI-powered workflows have helped developers move faster than ever. That\xe2\x80\x99s a good thing, and it\xe2\x80\x99s something I actively encourage people to embrace.\r\n\r\nBut learning with AI is trickier.\r\n\r\nAn overreliance on AI has been shown to harm skill retention (among other things). Studies from both Anthropic (https://learn.educative.io/e3t/Ctc/RG+113/cz5H404/VWJNx93QrbXnW7mV4dL5BhqJ3W8VsNl15Kkh_5N7Hm8xT3prCCW7Y8-PT6lZ3ncW88j-Ps3ZfSv0W5Wh1sQ1dcH4qW5LlFWG5GR7PJW1mNtSH6bDZhKVCbqLF3_YXCmW4Fhsn-5HVcH0W31ncsN66WqJFW7-xbGX2DPypvW8B7KTR74V7XMW4zRxbC5GZry1W8XyxlM1KCvKSW2z0XxC1FjY_SW5XJFw-1rbqNnVJk5LJ8tWdChW2zDvHh3BmXd1W64D7JS2RKnhDN9dWgR4grbvPW45nKnm8kxflWW9jB1pF6-Sw-9W3x_m6383vL-fW7V-mNH8KKnS7W54KNqm3xySybW7Lys355h3qJxW1D4flJ40cBKBW2rXc1g7RMDM7W2P2Ng28PSSt3f7Jz3Q204 ) and Microsoft have confirmed this.\r\n\r\nThe problem?\r\n\r\nMost AI tools aren't optimized for learning; they're optimized for speed.\r\n\r\nThat design choice matters more than it sounds.\r\n\r\nI'll explain why it matters\xe2\x80\x94and how we flipped the script with our AI learning assistant, Fenzo.\r\n\r\nWhere generic LLMs fall short for learning\r\n\r\nGeneric LLMs are optimized to predict the next best response.\r\n\r\nThat usually means:\r\n\r\n- Text-first explanations\r\n- Jumping quickly to code\r\n- Minimal structure\r\n- No guarantee the answer maps cleanly to a broader concept\r\n\r\nFor quick unblocks, that\xe2\x80\x99s fine.\r\n\r\nBut just because a generated snippet works doesn\xe2\x80\x99t mean you actually learned anything.\r\n\r\nTo learn something effectively, you need:\r\n\r\n- Context to fill a knowledge gap\r\n- Visuals and metal models to solidify concepts\r\n- Hands-on practice\r\n\r\nThis is what we designed Fenzo around.\r\n\r\nFenzo for depth and retention\r\n\r\nIf you\xe2\x80\x99ve ever solved a problem with AI and felt a quiet sense of unease about not fully grasping the solution, Fenzo is here to give you the full picture.\r\n\r\nWhen you ask Fenzo a question, it doesn\xe2\x80\x99t treat it as a prompt to answer. It's built as a teaching system from the ground up.\r\n\r\nBehind the scenes, Fenzo:\r\n\r\n- Identifies the skill gap behind your question\r\n- Follows a structured instructional sequence\r\n- Generates quizzes or live coding environments to reinforce learning\r\n- Anchors everything in Educative\xe2\x80\x99s verified curriculum to reduce hallucinations\r\n\r\nBuilding Fenzo was a major engineering effort for our team, and one of the highlights of 2025 at Educative. But the part I care most about isn\xe2\x80\x99t the design \xe2\x80\x94 it\xe2\x80\x99s how this shows up in real work.\r\n\r\nA quiz at the end of a Fenzo response\r\n\r\nFenzo in practice\r\n\r\nSay you\xe2\x80\x99re debugging a RAG pipeline that\xe2\x80\x99s returning irrelevant results.\r\n\r\nYou ask a generic AI what might be wrong. It gives you a plausible checklist: adjust chunk size, tweak embeddings, rerank results. You try a fix. It sort of works.\r\n\r\nBut you\xe2\x80\x99re left wondering why it helped (and what you\xe2\x80\x99d do differently next time).\r\n\r\nThat\xe2\x80\x99s the gap Fenzo is designed to close.\r\n\r\nAsk Fenzo the same question, and it doesn\xe2\x80\x99t jump straight to fixes.\r\n\r\nInstead, it:\r\n\r\n- Walks you through how retrieval, chunking, and embedding similarity actually interact\r\n- Shows you a mental model of the pipeline\r\n- Lets you experiment with the code to see how changes affect outcomes\r\n\r\nBy the end, you\xe2\x80\x99re not just unblocked. You\xe2\x80\x99ve learned something you\xe2\x80\x99ll reuse.\r\n\r\nBeing a developer means learning on the job. Most AI tools help you move faster\xe2\x80\x94Fenzo is built to help you get better while you do.\r\n\r\nWhat you can ask Fenzo\r\n\r\nYou can use Fenzo to:\r\n\r\n- Debug in the moment\r\n- Generate microtutorials\r\n- Write and run code to apply concepts\r\n\r\nYou can use it to navigate everything from computer science fundamentals to System Design to AI skills.\r\n\r\nHere are a few examples of the kinds of questions developers ask Fenzo:\r\n\r\n- \xe2\x80\x9cExplain how RAG works and why my retrieval quality is poor.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n- \xe2\x80\x9cHelp me build a mental model for async execution in this code.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n- \xe2\x80\x9cWhy does this caching strategy break under load?\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\nThere are still cases where a generic AI tool is the right choice. ChatGPT shines when you already have context and need speed\xe2\x80\x94brainstorming, prototyping, or quick lookups.\r\n\r\nFenzo is designed for the opposite moments: when understanding matters because you know you\xe2\x80\x99ll encounter the problem again.\r\n\r\nDevelopers need both. We built Fenzo for the cases where learning shouldn\xe2\x80\x99t be deferred.\r\n\r\nWhy this matters now\r\n\r\nAI will continue to reshape how software gets built. That part is inevitable.\r\n\r\nWhat\xe2\x80\x99s still in our control is how developers evolve alongside it.\r\n\r\nIf we optimize purely for speed and don\xe2\x80\x99t retain what we\xe2\x80\x99re learning, the cost will surface years later in brittle systems, shallow intuition, and codebases that are harder to reason about.\r\n\r\nWith AI becoming a permanent layer in the developer workflow, we need tools that don\xe2\x80\x99t just accelerate output, but strengthen understanding.\r\n\r\nFenzo is our answer, and we're thrilled our users have reported positive experiences with it so far.\r\n\r\n\xf0\x9f\x91\x89 You can try Fenzo (https://learn.educative.io/e3t/Ctc/RG+113/cz5H404/VWJNx93QrbXnW7mV4dL5BhqJ3W8VsNl15Kkh_5N7Hm8xT3prCCW7Y8-PT6lZ3pjW9k0Slc8vK9hjV-zCRl51MFddW75fdqw8SwG9pW1mtM7N8mqzm0W5SVc9V91vdcZW4SXrFX3-fL9rW682QmF6LKftWW5FVPY35zsMW4W5R2zNL6D1PZKW5Pb8Fz372rqdW1XD8rk3mLC2hW8MmtL481F8vLW6gx-Kr685jwqW4FXbdT838F_VW1RCGLP8-hXnpW6V8k1X6CjtmZW4-6tyV8pkT0rW32T4ZG1GYbXQW3K5c_56zzhD0W5l4d7y5Xd8K0W6JB66W1SPWcCW59LKnX1fncLgN5_6_gZm5gHDVgHRhz29k1zBW2M6wbh3fgWhqW3rRpSV1-Bv4Sf2nxgfP04 ) today with any Educative subscription at 50% off (or more) during our 3 million user celebration sale.\r\n\r\nGet 50% off (or more)\r\n(https://learn.educative.io/e3t/Ctc/RG+113/cz5H404/VWJNx93QrbXnW7mV4dL5BhqJ3W8VsNl15Kkh_5N7Hm8xT3prCCW7Y8-PT6lZ3lXW5PnCvc8hMdrjVKfXbZ2Rw3G8W6WMcfN7p4JZVW95wTrj4b3-zxW4cL_JD78T2nrW33N3zn8SnQ0VW2wRzf12NkY-pW2ppFk21wW-hRW5mW0Sy58LtDtN5y-yts5DnwYW1X8vWJ1nDP7_W4yftfg1wJmr2W6hwTnS5n3pr9W2-zSfl7vFNStW7_kZsy1CymyjW8Khgn863Ww0BW6NzS6r40BJgmW4YQgsn7sr0NVW7yMHyN4Lw-9sW288kkh2ZfYr7N8wkmBDKTwjpW2DZBpM2dR5m2W57QlwX286TXjW9fsnX17KcJt-W8h2DC-8KNwl3W2W902C1wy-Dff5vQHcq04 )\r\n\r\nAs always, if you give it a try, I\xe2\x80\x99d love to hear how it goes. And if you\xe2\x80\x99re already using Fenzo, hit reply and tell me how it\xe2\x80\x99s been working for you.\r\n\r\nUntil next time,\r\n\r\n- Fahim\r\n\r\nApp Store (https://learn.educative.io/e3t/Ctc/RG+113/cz5H404/VWJNx93QrbXnW7mV4dL5BhqJ3W8VsNl15Kkh_5N7Hm8xT3prCCW7Y8-PT6lZ3mxW38-dmQ3XRJ8pW8Z6Dg33p9_FGW2LlZ4h43wJn1W6Smj1n5bjKfQN4mY_bN-5tJyW73xxJm7LJQvtW48Smqh2M1DvNW3D46dB2x5bgXW1dK47r2tgqr0W40kKr_7BlGgHVnbBrs2QgKJvW2hmfVY8k02s3W6CQmCR57r-dtW8CTCgD3tv8NjW66-VQS21xt6KW2HkN-m7xrBtDMygFn4m3TXJW5F14zD2Y20QjW8fB2P85MB6y5W1sqHGC1lsSKRW8B5gNH8mW5yGW2dvxbp69THDHVbpMVj5F5PK5W7dDRKs6V8dP9W6pmBQz1q43-kN64mw_k8tDmXf1HMZT004 )\r\n\r\nGoogle Play (https://learn.educative.io/e3t/Ctc/RG+113/cz5H404/VWJNx93QrbXnW7mV4dL5BhqJ3W8VsNl15Kkh_5N7Hm8y83prCCW8wLKSR6lZ3q0W2PQ51z5v1Jl0W1BynJ928ph0nW6rmMhY15CGJVW86bl042gG6zbN7yp-RYvvL5QW6hnt7S3f9-QCW7jTdc24SWDxfW45bQmR4dWn0mW8cwwnf6X7cC7W950Jkk8MNT-VW5njGL215DM8SW5MzZj54Y7_KGW7x5G9p4DdcnzW2YmDlt1P22xcW8FvvCk8BLMmNN5jVmDkdfdrhW2sNGqB8pvptrW8mNJ-Q9jWzXZW5j18jl4Q6Q6qW98dgpy2KJ1LgW23v_ZL1-MbK4W74fN1z5W3RwBW6DvQn44lknZ1N3Hv3CBFMKJjW5Djz6V83tyqqW3W73_q6W00KpW4T_hrD6lbFttW1MNscK5mP2-4dw52Kd04 )\r\n\r\nEducative, 12280 NE District Way, Bellevue, WA 98005, United States\r\n\r\nManage preferences (https://learn.educative.io/hs/preferences-center/en/page?data=W2nXS-N30h-BbW43wT_s4hmtpjW2TC87v3jltfJW1BdWrP3VLJhDW2Wy6B71_f8ngW47Fygj34Fk1dW34DZqR49RHPwW1QcDbS2vwddGW3H7lDN3DWyKXW1_tb_l1BdXw1W383Xg-1-VC8BW2TKplM1Nh_byW2KQQGr1VhM9fW3SHzt82WN_4TW2KrrKt2