[2026-04-27 11:17:11] Raw text/plain payload: b'Roof condition can affect solar cost, timing, and future repairs.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x8a\r\n\r\nSolar Works Best When the Roof Is Ready\r\n\r\n\r\nHi Jason,\r\n\r\n\r\n Homeowners who plan solar often pause to review their roof first.\r\n\r\nHere is why.\r\n\r\nSolar systems are designed to last decades.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIf roof work is needed later, panels may need to be removed and reinstalled, \r\nwhich adds cost and delays.\r\n\r\nA quick roofing review helps avoid that.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSee Local Roofing Installers  \r\n<https://www.fetchapro.com/roofing/la/?tg_ref=ERCS&camp_id=2.9.3&keyword=o1&sub2=main>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat clicking does:\r\n\xe2\x80\xa2 Shows roofing installers who work in Cartersville\r\n\xe2\x80\xa2 Lets you compare pricing and timelines in one place\r\n \xe2\x80\xa2 Helps confirm whether roof work should happen before solar\r\n\r\n\r\nFetchAPro makes it easy to review roofing options without calling multiple \r\ncompanies or committing to a project.\r\n\r\nMany homeowners use this step to make sure their solar investment is protected \r\nbefore moving forward.\r\n\r\nKind regards,\r\nThe FetchAPro Team\r\n\r\n\r\n\xe2\x80\x8a\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis message was sent to jasonnorman66994@gmail.com from Lendgo because you \r\npreviously subscribed to receive email correspondence.Click here to unsubscribe.\r\n \r\n<http://links.ebcsolarmail.com/e/encryptedUnsubscribe?_r=a5b385c9ed104e9baa0616bcbbf74110&_s=b780441c70524ad29c9be96f34f3ea14&_t=xWW7DLqMx0DcyfhFIHkHhtiVhPWCd5Nua_UYOz37S1t8lELapFl05sYilyksRIRF6Dj4ZvCjGfYf26bVUVS08LYpUCwPptEHHG4Rm7AFfa5X1tBZUJ9Mb-HgnK2TGbQx>\r\n\r\nEnergyBillCruncher Services, 6834 Cantrell Road #2024, Little Rock AK 72207\r\n'
