[2026-04-27 11:17:41] Raw text/plain payload: b'Clean Fuel Product Credit, Taxpayer Advocate Service Annual Report to Congress; FAQ for modernizing payments; qualified overtime compensation credit and other news\r\n\r\nBookmark and Share [ https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USIRS/bulletins/408f5aa?reqfrom=share ]\r\n\r\nIRS.gov Banner \r\n\r\ne-News for Small Business\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nFebruary 10, 2026\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nIssue Number: \xc2\xa02025-03\r\n\r\nInside This Issue\r\n\r\n  * IRS seeks public input on proposed Clean fuel Product Credit regulations [ #First ] \r\n  * National Taxpayer Advocate delivers annual report to Congress [ #Second ] \r\n  * Modernizing payments to and from America\xe2\x80\x99s bank account [ #Third ] \r\n  * FAQs address qualified overtime compensation deduction [ #Fourth ] \r\n  * Other tax news [ #Fifth ] \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*\xc2\xa0 IRS seeks public input on proposed Clean fuel Product Credit regulations* \r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nProposed regulations are now available for domestic producers of clean transportation fuel to determine eligibility and calculations for Clean Fuel Product Credit. This credit provides businesses with an income tax credit for clean transportation fuel produced domestically *after Dec. 31, 2024, and sold by Dec. 31, 2029*.\r\n\r\nBusinesses are encouraged to use the Federal e-Rulemaking portal [ https://www.regulations.gov/ ] to submit comments indicate \xe2\x80\x9cIRS\xe2\x80\x9d and \xe2\x80\x9cREG-121244-23.\xe2\x80\x9d\r\n\r\nFor more details about the changes to this credit and instructions on how to claim it see the news release [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/treasury-irs-issue-proposed-regulations-on-the-clean-fuel-production-credit-under-the-one-big-beautiful-bill ] or visit the One, Big, Beautiful Bill Provisions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/one-big-beautiful-bill-provisions ] page on IRS.gov.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0Back to top [ #top ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*\xc2\xa0 National Taxpayer Advocate delivers annual report to Congress*\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nNational Taxpayer Advocate Erin M. Collins recently sent the 2025 Annual Report to Congress [ https://links-1.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.taxpayeradvocate.irs.gov%2FAnnualReport2025/2/0100019c1fb2b89b-732173c4-719b-4d05-b246-dd8b0493a722-000000/wQ2x9-BWQUKh1yYiXrFPyDoXTbdO-AaS_7KxSfRV6E4=442 ]. The report acknowledges what went well in 2025, but also highlights upcoming 2026 challenges.\r\n\r\nThe report identifies the 10 most serious problems business and individual taxpayers are experiencing when dealing with the IRS and makes administrative and legislative recommendations to address those problems.\r\n\r\nSome key points include recommending credentials for federal tax return preparers, timely processing claims for credit or refund and providing consistent tax relief for victims of federally declared disasters.\r\n\r\nVisit Taxpayer Advocate Service website [ https://www.taxpayeradvocate.irs.gov/ ] for more information or check out National Taxpayer Advocate blog [ https://www.taxpayeradvocate.irs.gov/taxnews-information/blogs-nta/ ] about key issues in tax administration.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0Back to top [ #top ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*\xc2\xa0 Modernizing payments to and from America\xe2\x80\x99s bank account*\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nFrequently asked questions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-issues-frequently-asked-questions-about-executive-order-14247-modernizing-payments-to-and-from-americas-bank-account ] are now available to help businesses and individual taxpayers understand the changes under Executive Order 14247: Modernizing Payment to and from America\xe2\x80\x99s bank account [ https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/03/modernizing-payments-to-and-from-americas-bank-account/ ]. *The way taxpayers file their federal tax returns is not changing*.\r\n\r\nThese changes apply to payments:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * *Sent by federal government*: tax refunds, benefits, grants, and vendor or contractor payments \r\n  * *Made to federal government*: tax balances due, fees, penalties, and other payments from individuals, businesses, nonprofit organizations and state or local partners \r\n\r\n*Business and individual taxpayers are encouraged to*:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Use direct deposit [ https://links-1.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.irs.gov%2Frefunds%2Fget-your-refund-faster-tell-irs-to-direct-deposit-your-refund-to-one-two-or-three-accounts/1/0100019c1fb2b89b-732173c4-719b-4d05-b246-dd8b0493a722-000000/HUph8Jo8SEWYWSEPIpktovGMFkV7JfU1MA-M1tvMHHs=442 ] for refunds by providing accurate bank or prepaid debit card information when filing \r\n  * Choose electronic payment options when paying taxes, such as IRS Direct Pay, Electronic Federal Tax Payment System [ https://links-1.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.irs.gov%2Fpayments%2Fdirect-pay-with-bank-account/1/0100019c1fb2b89b-732173c4-719b-4d05-b246-dd8b0493a722-000000/i3JMs7dcqOZTu-5wK6IKgBdGcy__NJ9CDYxO1UBrXCw=442 ], or other approved methods \r\n  * Review account information to ensure bank details are current and correct \r\n  * Visit IRS.gov to learn about electronic payment  [ https://links-1.govdelivery.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fwww.irs.gov%2Fpayments/1/0100019c1fb2b89b-732173c4-719b-4d05-b246-dd8b0493a722-000000/r2cs0DODGMvqbgMXrm9sn2Yn0OTSO8-V-ZgnHOv-Jk0=442 ]options\xc2\xa0and available resources for taxpayers without a bank account \r\n\r\nSee the news release [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-issues-frequently-asked-questions-about-executive-order-14247-modernizing-payments-to-and-from-americas-bank-account ] for more information.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0Back to top [ #top ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*\xc2\xa0 FAQs address qualified overtime compensation deduction*\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nFrequently asked questions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/treasury-irs-issue-faqs-to-address-the-new-deduction-for-qualified-overtime-compensation-under-the-one-big-beautiful-bill ] are now available to help businesses and individual taxpayers understand the new deduction for qualified overtime compensation under the One, Big, Beautiful Bill\r\n\r\nThese FAQs have information about the deduction, resources to assist in determining if an individual received qualified overtime compensation, and useful information about the differences in reporting requirements for tax year 2025 and 2026-2028.\r\n\r\nFor more information, see One, Big, Beautiful Bill Provisions [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/one-big-beautiful-bill-provisions ] on IRS.gov.\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0Back to top [ #top ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\n*\xc2\xa0 Other tax news*\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe following information may be of interest to individuals and groups in or related to small businesses:\r\n\r\n*Filing season information*:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * Get Ready for the filing season and save time with Tax Pro Account [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/tax-pros-get-ready-for-the-filing-season-and-save-time-with-tax-pro-account-encourage-clients-to-use-their-irs-individual-online-account ] \r\n  * 2026 Tax Counseling for the Elderly and Volunteer Income Tax Assistance Program Grants [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-announces-2026-tax-counseling-for-the-elderly-and-volunteer-income-tax-assistance-program-grants ] \r\n  * Use online tools when claiming One, Big, Beautiful Bill tax advantages [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/use-online-tools-when-claiming-one-big-beautiful-bill-tax-advantages-for-families-and-education ] \r\n\r\n*Other news*:\r\n\r\n\r\n  * EITC Awareness Day [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-joins-national-partners-to-launch-eitc-awareness-day ] \r\n  * 2026 funding for Low Income Taxpayer Clinic grant recipients [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/taxpayer-advocate-service-announces-2026-funding-for-low-income-taxpayer-clinic-grant-recipients ] \r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0 \xc2\xa0Back to top [ #top ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nFaceBook Logo [ https://www.facebook.com/IRS/ ]\xc2\xa0\xc2\xa0YouTube Logo [ https://www.youtube.com/user/irsvideos ] \xc2\xa0Instagram Logo [ https://www.instagram.com/irsnews ]\xc2\xa0 Twitter Logo [ https://twitter.com/IRSnews ] \xc2\xa0LinkedIn Logo [ https://www.linkedin.com/company/irs/ ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThank you for subscribing to this IRS email service.\r\n\r\nThis message was distributed automatically from the mailing list e-News for Small Business. Please Do Not Reply To This Message.\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\nTax Resources for Small Business\r\n\r\nSmall Business Self-Employment Center [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed ]\r\n\r\nSmall Business Forms & Instructions [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/small-business-forms-and-publications ]\r\n\r\nSmall Business Tax Workshops, Meetings and Seminars [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/small-business-tax-workshops-meetings-and-seminars ]\r\n\r\nWebinars for Small Businesses [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/webinars-for-small-businesses ]\r\n\r\nE-file Employment Tax Forms [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/e-file-employment-tax-forms ]\r\n\r\nBusinesses with Employees [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/businesses-with-employees ]\r\n\r\nSelf-Employed Individuals Tax Center [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/self-employed-individuals-tax-center ]\r\n\r\nS Corporations [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/s-corporations ]\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nOther Resources\r\n\r\nIRS Home Page [ https://www.irs.gov/ ]\r\n\r\nA-Z Index for Business [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/a-z-index-for-business ]\r\n\r\nForms, Instructions & Publications [ https://www.irs.gov/forms-instructions ]\r\n\r\nFiling Your Taxes [ https://www.irs.gov/filing ]\r\n\r\nPay Online [ https://www.irs.gov/payments ]\r\n\r\nTaxpayer Advocate Service [ https://www.irs.gov/taxpayer-advocate ]\r\n\r\nRetirement Plans for Small Entities and Self-Employed [ https://www.irs.gov/retirement-plans/retirement-plans-for-small-entities-and-self-employed ]\r\n\r\nTax Information for Charities  [ https://www.irs.gov/charities-and-nonprofits ]\r\nand Other Non-Profits [ https://www.irs.gov/charities-and-nonprofits ]\r\n\r\nState Government Websites [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/state-government-websites ]\r\n\r\nSSA/RS Reporter [ https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/ssa-irs-reporter ]\r\n\r\nIRS Social Media [ https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-social-media ]\r\n\r\n\xc2\xa0\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n/*start reset css*/ div { line-height: 1; } body, table, td, p, a, li, blockquote { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; } body { -webkit-text-size-adjust: none; -ms-text-size-adjust: none; } table { border-spacing: 0; } table, td { mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; } img { -ms-interpolation-mode: bicubic; } body { margin: 0; padding: 0; } img { border: none !important; height: auto; line-height: 1; outline: none; text-decoration: none